PVD("india_ndp_2018-2022",{"docs":["","IND Strategy for New India 2018 22"],"s":{"1":[[1,"57","2","Universal Bank Account Access Initiative","Ensuring universal access to bank accounts, which are a gateway to all financial services.",""],[1,"57","3","Digital Payment Services Expansion","Digital payment services: Providing access to digital payment services and increasing its penetration.",""],[1,"57","4","Universal Insurance and Social Security Coverage","Ensuring universal coverage of insurance for life, accidents, etc., and of pensions and other retirement planning services.",""],[1,"57","7","Financial Inclusion and Financial Security Flagship Schemes","The government has launched many flagship schemes to promote financial inclusion and provide financial security to empower the poor and unbanked in the country.",""],[1,"57","7","Aadhaar and Direct Benefit Transfer Promotion","In addition, the promotion of Aadhaar and direct benefit transfer schemes facilitate financial inclusion.",""],[1,"57","10","Mobile Payments Expansion Initiatives","Several new initiatives such as Aadhaar-enabled payment services, payment banks, etc. will boost the use of mobile payments.",""],[1,"60","2","Payments System Expansion in Underserved Areas","Leverage payment banks and other platforms to scale up payments systems in underserved areas",""],[1,"60","6","Consumer Refunds for Failed USSD Transactions","fee on failed USSD transactions should be refunded to consumers to enable greater participation.",""]],"2":[[1,"8","2","Policy Environment Improvement for Private Investment","The focus of the strategy is to further improve the policy environment in which private investors and other stakeholders can contribute their fullest towards achieving the goals set out for New India 2022.",""],[1,"17","3","Public-Private Partnership Expansion","There is an ongoing effort to achieve an optimum level of public-private partnership.",""],[1,"17","3","Improved Delivery of Public Goods and Services","Policies have been put in place for more efficient delivery of public goods and services such as health, education, power, urban water supply and connectivity.",""],[1,"17","3","Red Tape Reduction and Regulatory Simplification","a deliberate effort is being made to cut red tape and end burdensome over- regulation for promoting entrepreneurship and private investment.",""],[1,"23","10","Measures to Boost Private and Public Investment","a slew of measures will be required to boost both private and public investment.",""],[1,"25","3","Renewed Public-Private Partnership Mechanism for Infrastructure Investment","Private investment needs be encouraged in infrastructure through a renewed public-private partnership (PPP) mechanism on the lines suggested by the Kelkar Committee.",""]],"3":[[1,"34","8","Technology Commercialization Enhancement Measures","Some measures for enhancing technology commercialization by public funded institutions are provided below:",""],[1,"34","9","Value Addition Centres in Institutions","Value addition centres may be set up in each of these institutions for (i) up-scaling technologies, (ii) improving technologies from Technology Readiness Level (TRL) 4 to TRL 6/7, (iii) demonstrating industrial scale pilot production, (iv) coordinating with investors to incubate entrepreneurs, (v) bridging the gap between industry and technology development teams, (vi) enabling formal technology transfer, (vii) enabling commercialization and marketing and (viii) providing technology support during production.",""],[1,"34","10","National Technology Data Bank","DST should create a National Technology Data Bank in coordination with all publicly funded R&D institutions.","DST"],[1,"34","11","Socially Relevant Technology Development and Deployment","Public funded research institutions should consider shifting their focus to the development and deployment of socially relevant technologies in areas such as clean drinking water, sanitation, energy, affordable healthcare, organic farming, etc.",""]],"4":[[1,"36","2","Industry 4.0 Technology Adoption Promotion","Promote in a planned manner the adoption of the latest technology advancements, referred to as 'Industry 4.0', that will have a defining role in shaping the manufacturing sector in 2022.",""],[1,"39","9","Industry 4.0 Adoption Initiative","Launch a major initiative to push industry to adopt Industry 4.0.",""],[1,"39","10","National Artificial Intelligence Programme","In his 2018 Budget Speech, the Finance Minister mandated NITI Aayog to initiate a national programme directing India's efforts on Artificial Intelligence6.",""],[1,"39","10","Industry 4.0 Consultation Forum","NITI Aayog could organize a discussion on \"Industry 4.0,\" inviting leading manufacturing companies from various sectors including automobile/auto components, electrical and electronics, chemicals, cement/steel, etc., along with concerned ministries to discuss plans for adopting Industry 4.0.",""],[1,"39","11","Smart Manufacturing Specialized Training Programmes","The Indian Institute of Science, a few select Indian Institutes of Technology (IITs), National Institutes of Technology (NITs) and other premier engineering colleges should create specialized training programmes on 'Smart Manufacturing' to address the shortage of high-tech human resources.",""],[1,"39","12","Centre of Excellence for Industry 4.0 Research and Development","The Department of Heavy Industry (DHI) should develop the Central Manufacturing Technology Institute (CMTI), Bangalore, as a Centre of Excellence for pursuing R&D in Industry 4.0 technologies and systems.","Department of Heavy Industry (DHI)"],[1,"39","12","Industry-Academia Research Projects on Cyber-Physical Systems","The Department of Science & Technology should spearhead industry-academia R&D projects on cyber physical systems.","Department of Science & Technology"],[1,"40","1","Industry 4.0 Manufacturing Incentive Support","The development of industries that produce the key building blocks forming the basis of Industry 4.0 could be incentivized.",""],[1,"40","2","Indian Standards for Smart Manufacturing Systems","Reliability, stability and integrity of smart manufacturing systems can be increased by creating Indian standards for the systems and sub-systems for adoption by manufacturers.",""]],"5":[[1,"36","4","Make in India Action Plan","the Make in India Action Plan aimed at increasing the manufacturing sector's contribution to 25 per cent of GDP by 2020",""],[1,"36","4","MUDRA and Stand-up India Credit Access Support","the Micro Units Development and Refinance Agency (MUDRA) and Stand-up India to facilitate access to credit",""],[1,"36","4","Industrial Corridor Development","it has undertaken major infrastructure projects, such as the setting up of industrial corridors, to boost manufacturing",""],[1,"38","3","Self-Sufficient Manufacturing Cluster Development","Efforts should be made to develop self-sufficient clusters of manufacturing competence, with Cluster Administrative Authorities empowered to provide single window clearances to entrepreneurs and investors.",""],[1,"38","3","Industrial Corridor Infrastructure and Logistics Upgrading","Industrial corridors should address the lack of infrastructure and logistics.",""],[1,"38","3","Manufacturing Supply Chain Warehousing Expansion","Logistics will need to be supplemented with warehousing and other elements of the manufacturing supply chain.",""],[1,"38","4","Manufacturing Cluster Development and Export Strategy Support","NITI Aayog could work with states to prepare manufacturing clusters and develop export strategies based on their sector competitive- ness and resource strengths.","NITI Aayog"],[1,"38","6","Foreign Direct Investment Promotion in Manufacturing","For India to become the world's workshop, we should encourage further FDI in manufacturing, particularly when it is supported with buybacks and export orders.",""],[1,"39","4","Mega Parks and Manufacturing Clusters in Labour-Intensive Sectors","Setting up of mega parks and manufac- turing clusters in labour intensive sectors with common facilities to reduce costs and improve quality.",""],[1,"39","5","Worker Accommodation in New Mega Parks","Workers of industrial units in the new mega parks should have decent accommodation within reasonable proximity of the work place.",""],[1,"39","6","Sector-Specific Pain Point Review Committee","An expert committee should examine sector-specific pain points and make its recommendations within three months.",""],[1,"39","7","PSU Registration on TREDS Portal","The Department of Public Enterprises (DPE) should ensure registration of all public sector units (PSUs) on the Trade Receivables Discounting System (TREDS) portal.","Department of Public Enterprises (DPE)"],[1,"39","8","Small Business Research Programme for MSME R&D","Initiate a small business research programme in some select ministries for encouraging R&D in MSMEs.",""],[1,"55","11","Export-Oriented Cluster Development with Common Infrastructure","The Agricultural and Processed Food Export Development Authority (APEDA) has been championing the development of export-oriented clusters with common infrastructure facilities.",""]],"6":[[1,"203","3","Urban Governance Modernization Initiatives","Indian cities are in the process of modernizing their governance structures.",""],[1,"204","4","City Economic Councils","In larger cities, City Economic Councils can serve as a clearinghouse",""],[1,"204","6","Quarterly City Dashboard Framework","a quarterly city dashboard capturing city-level investments, GDP and employment growth, financial position and financial performance, and status of infrastructure projects can provide a framework for data-driven decisions.","Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs | Ministry of Finance | Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation"],[1,"205","1","Urban Governance Framework for City Decentralization","there is an urgent need for articulating a framework for governance of cities that includes development authorities, other parastatals, special purpose vehicles (SPVs) and Census Towns.",""],[1,"205","2","Two-Tier Metropolitan Governance Reform","There is a strong case for having a two-tier governance structure where all local functions are transferred to the ward committees and citywide services, such as transportation, water supply, sewerage, etc., are vested with the city council or regional authorities.",""],[1,"205","3","Urban Local Body Devolution and Ward-Level Governance Reform","state governments can be encouraged to transfer 12th Schedule funds, functions and functionaries to the ULBs.",""],[1,"205","4","National Urban Spatial Planning Framework","There is urgent need for a synchronous and modern national framework for the spatial planning of cities that replaces the current Urban Development Plans Formulation and Implementation (UDPFI) guidelines.",""],[1,"205","5","Guaranteed Land Titling and Settlement Formalization","Guaranteed land titling may also be evaluated to foster a transparent land market.",""],[1,"205","7","Urban Financial Sustainability Roadmap","Cities require a financial sustainability roadmap to be financially self-sufficient to support high-quality infrastructure and the delivery of services.",""],[1,"205","8","Fiscal Decentralization and Urban Revenue Mobilization Measures","This comprises fiscal decentralization, medium- term fiscal plans, innovative models to improve revenue collection, optimizing return on assets especially land and buildings, value capture methods, market-oriented revenue models, PPPs in urban infrastructure and services, and financial accountability through audited balance sheets and performance MIS reports.",""],[1,"205","9","Model Provisions for Municipal and Civic Agency Acts","MoHUA, in consultation with the Ministry of Finance, may draw up model provisions for consideration by states in their municipal and civic agency acts.","MoHUA | Ministry of Finance"],[1,"205","11","Model Municipal Talent and Outsourcing Guidelines","MoHUA will develop model municipal talent and in/outsourcing guidelines to leverage efficiencies generated by technology and outsourcing.","MoHUA"],[1,"205","12","Municipal Jobs Skills and Competency Framework Development","The National Skill Development Corporation (NSDC) should be leveraged to improve understanding of municipal jobs including job definitions, technical competencies and key result areas, which can be considered for",""],[1,"206","1","State-Level Inclusion in Recruitment Rules","inclusion in recruitment rules at the state level",""],[1,"206","1","Training Institute Performance Standards and Accreditation","for performance standards/accreditation for training institutes",""],[1,"206","1","Municipal Services Sector Skill Council","A separate sector skill council for municipal services may be considered.",""],[1,"206","2","Ward Committee and Area Sabha Activation","Ward committees and area sabhas should be activated with a technology-",""],[1,"206","3","Open Cities Framework and Digital Feedback and Reporting Tools","enabled 'Open Cities Framework' and the use of digital tools for feedback and reporting.",""],[1,"206","4","Urban Local Body Community Participation and Partnership Framework","ULBs should also encourage the participation of all community associations, including settlements of the underprivileged and civil society organizations.",""],[1,"206","4","City Watch Groups, Public Hearings, and City Consultations","ULBs should engage with them frequently through city watch groups, public hearings and city consultations to create a framework for formal partnerships.",""],[1,"206","4","Simplification of Rules and Procedures for Faster Implementation","Rules and procedures need to be simplified for faster implementation of constructive recommendations.",""],[1,"210","13","Urbanization Financing Instruments","Tools such as land value capture, incentive zoning, town planning schemes, and land- based taxes like land value tax, vacant land tax, land value increment tax, etc., can be used to finance rapid and efficient urbanization.",""]],"7":[[1,"18","9","Bharat Net Programme Completion and Last-Mile Rural Connectivity","With the completion of the Bharat Net programme in 2019, all 2.5 lakh gram panchayats will be digitally connected.",""],[1,"18","9","Digital Delivery of Government Services","The aim will be to deliver all government services at the state, district, and gram panchayat level digitally by 2022-23, thereby eliminating the digital divide.",""],[1,"104","3","Digital Delivery of Government Services","Delivery of government services digitally by 2022-23.",""],[1,"105","1","BharatNet Rural Broadband Connectivity Expansion","under BharatNet, work had started in 1.24 lakh GPs of which 1.08 lakh GPs were service ready.",""],[1,"105","1","National Information Infrastructure Integration Initiative","the National Information Infrastructure (NII) will ensure the integration of the networks and cloud infrastructure to provide high-speed connectivity to various government departments up to the panchayat level.",""],[1,"105","2","Public Internet Access Programme","The government also launched the Public Internet Access Programme7 to make 2,50,000 common service centres (CSCs) operational at the gram panchayat level to deliver government services online.",""],[1,"105","2","Conversion of Post Offices into Multi-Service Centres","Under this programme, 1,50,000 post offices will be converted into multi-service centres.",""],[1,"105","2","Universal Service Obligation Fund Last-Mile Connectivity Expansion","The last mile connectivity, through Wi-Fi or any other suitable broadband technology, is to be provided at all GPs in the country, funded by the Universal Service Obligation Fund (USOF).",""],[1,"105","3","Phased Mobile Coverage Expansion Plan","A comprehensive development plan, to be implemented in phases,",""],[1,"106","4","BharatNet Phase-II Broadband Connectivity Expansion","A modified strategy for expediting the pace of implementation of the BharatNet project was approved on July 19, 2017.",""],[1,"106","5","Rural Telephone Exchange Broadband Upgrade","up by BSNL at its 25,000 telephone exchanges in rural areas",""],[1,"106","5","Wi-Fi Choupal Deployment in Gram Panchayats","Wi-Fi choupals are being set up in 5,000 GPs by CSC-SPV under the Ministry of Electronics and Information Technology (MeitY).","Ministry of Electronics and Information Technology (MeitY)"],[1,"106","6","Universal Broadband Coverage and On-Demand Institutional Broadband Policy","The provision of universal broadband coverage at 50 Mbps to every citizen and the enabling of 100 Mbps broadband on demand to all key development institutions, including educational institutions, are under consideration in the new National Digital Communications Policy, 2018.",""]],"8":[[1,"106","9","National Digital Literacy Mission in Schools and Colleges","The National Digital Literacy Mission should focus on introducing digital literacy at the primary school level in all government schools for basic content and in higher classes and colleges for advanced content.",""],[1,"107","1","Regional Language Government E-Services Content Development","State governments should pay special attention to creating content, particularly those relating to government e-services, in Indian regional languages.",""],[1,"107","2","Collaborative Natural Language Processing Promotion for Multilingual E-Government Services","To fulfil the vision of making all government's online services available in all 22 official languages, there needs to be focused collaboration between the centre, states and researchers to promote Natural Language Processing (NLP) in Indian languages.",""],[1,"107","2","Automatic Translation of Government Content into Regional Languages","Focus could be laid on the automatic translation of content into regional languages from Hindi or English.",""],[1,"107","2","International Case Study Review for Multilingual Service Delivery","Case studies like those of the European Union, which had similar problems in making content available in the languages of member countries, should be explored to identify models that can potentially be adopted.",""]],"9":[[1,"116","7","Groundwater Sustainability Measures","Ensure long-term sustainability of finite ground water resources.",""],[1,"117","3","Groundwater Development and Management Scheme","Besides, a scheme for groundwater development and management to prepare aquifer management plans and facilitate sustainable management of groundwater has been launched.",""],[1,"118","13","Participatory Aquifer Management Strengthening","Participatory aquifer management initiated in the 12th Plan National Aquifer Management (NAQUIM) under PMKSY should be strengthened through a network of partnerships to control unbridled, competitive extraction of groundwater since it is virtually impossible to police more than 30 million groundwater structures through licences and permits.",""],[1,"118","14","Community-Based Groundwater Management Expansion","The participatory approach to encourage behavioural changes and community engagement in ground water management at the gram panchayat level as envisaged in the Atal Bhujal Yojana (ABHY) should be adopted and extended to other regions.",""],[1,"119","13","State Water Regulatory Framework Establishment","A water regulatory framework should be established for water resources in all states.",""],[1,"123","16","National Water Mission Redesign for Efficient Water Resource Management","The National Water Mission should be re-designed for efficient water resource management.",""]],"10":[[1,"116","8","Water Infrastructure Operation and Maintenance","Ensure proper operation and maintenance of water infrastructure with active participation of farmers/consumers.",""],[1,"116","9","Water Sector Research and Development Promotion","Promote R&D to facilitate adoption of the latest technologies in the water sector.",""],[1,"118","5","Sprinkler and Drip Irrigation Incentive Reform","Incentivize the wider adoption of sprinkler and drip irrigation by diverting resources otherwise used to subsidize power and surface irrigation.",""],[1,"118","10","Industrial Recycled Water Use Promotion","Industries should be encouraged to meet a major share of their demand through recycled water.",""],[1,"118","10","Smart Water Meter Programme","programmes for smart water meters ... may be launched.",""],[1,"118","10","Tradable Permits for Recycled Water Use","tradable permits for use of recycled water may be launched.",""],[1,"118","15","Solar Pump Promotion for Irrigation","Promote the use of solar pumps to improve the utilisation of groundwater in Eastern India where utilisation is hampered by the lack of power.",""],[1,"118","15","Solar Pump Buyback Guarantee for Surplus Power","In Western India, solar pumps with a buyback guarantee for surplus solar power can offer reliable daytime energy for irrigation and stable cash income as well act as an incentive to conserve power and water.",""],[1,"119","6","Water Tariff Revision for Cost Recovery","This should be accompanied by a revision in water tariffs to recover at least operation and maintenance costs.",""],[1,"119","14","Water Use Efficiency Improvement Action Plan","An action plan should be drawn up to improve water use efficiency (with 2017 as the base year) by 20 per cent in all sectors by 2022.",""],[1,"119","15","Composite Water Management Index Use for Water Resource Efficiency","The composite water management index developed by NITI Aayog may be used as a potent tool to assess and further improve the efficiency of water resources management.","NITI Aayog"]],"11":[[1,"116","6","Additional Water Storage Capacity Expansion","Create additional water storage capacity to ensure full utilization of the utilizable surface water resources potential of 690 billion cubic metres (bcm).",""],[1,"117","10","Water Storage Capacity Expansion through Ongoing Projects","By 2022-23, the water storage capacity needs to be increased from the current level of 253 bcm to 304 bcm by completing on-going projects on time.",""],[1,"118","6","Water Body Revitalization, Renovation, and Repair Programme","the MoWR's programme to revitalize, renovate and repair water bodies should be significantly expanded and adequately funded.","MoWR"],[1,"118","7","Water Body Desilting Programme","Special emphasis should be laid on desilting of water bodies, including river, lakes, ponds and reservoirs.",""],[1,"118","9","Treated Wastewater Irrigation Pilot Scheme","a pilot scheme to irrigate 10 lakh ha with treated waste water by 2020 may initially be taken up.",""],[1,"118","12","Groundwater Recharge Zone Development","There is a need to develop recharging zones at identified places to make groundwater resources sustainable using check dam, farm ponds, tanks and injection wells.",""],[1,"119","5","Accelerated Watershed Development Projects","The timeline for watershed development projects needs to be shortened from seven to four years with special efforts by state governments.",""],[1,"119","5","Use of MGNREGA and State Plan Funds for Watershed Development","Funds available under MGNREGA and state plans may be used for watershed development projects.",""]],"12":[[1,"77","2","24x7 Universal Power Supply","Make available 24x7 power to all by 2019.",""],[1,"79","6","Smart Grid and Smart Meter Promotion","Promote smart grid and smart meters.",""],[1,"80","1","Privatization of State Distribution Utilities and Franchisee Model","Privatizing state distribution utilities and/or the use of a franchisee model will reduce AT&C losses.",""],[1,"80","2","Rural Discom Franchisee Model for Retail Electricity","Discoms may adopt a franchisee model for its retail business in rural areas and stipulate a minimum level of performance parameters, including the use of decentralized generation sources and storage systems for local reliability and resilience.",""],[1,"80","3","Strengthening and Independence of Regulatory Bodies","Regulatory bodies need to be further strengthened and made truly independent.",""],[1,"80","6","Discom Load Shedding Penalty Measure","Discoms may be fined for load shedding.",""],[1,"80","7","Cross-Subsidy Cap Enforcement and Open Access Charge Reduction","Ensure effective enforcement of a cap on cross- subsidy and open access.",""],[1,"80","10","Performance-Based Tariff Incentives","Introduce performance-based incentives in the tariff structure.",""],[1,"80","11","Electricity Metering and Smart Meter Rollout","To manage the demand for power, it is necessary to introduce 100 per cent metering, net metering, smart meters, and metering of electricity supplied to agriculture.",""]],"13":[[1,"81","8","Bureau of Energy Efficiency White Paper on Energy Efficiency Strategy","The Bureau of Energy Efficiency (BEE) should come out with a white paper on its 5-year strategy on energy efficiency in various sectors and specify energy consumption norms.",""],[1,"81","9","Strengthening State Designated Agencies for Energy Efficiency Implementation","State designated agencies (SDAs) need to be more empowered and provided with adequate resources to implement EE related programmes.",""],[1,"81","10","Risk-Sharing Financing Models","appropriate financing models with a risk sharing mechanism, particularly by public sector banks.",""],[1,"81","11","Energy Conservation Building Code Adoption and Implementation","States should adopt the second version of the Energy Conservation Building Code (ECBC) in their building by-laws and ensure faster implementation.",""],[1,"81","12","Mandatory LED and Five-Star Appliance Efficiency Programme","Promote the mandatory use of LED and the replacement of old appliances in government buildings with five-star appliances.",""],[1,"81","12","UJALA Programme Focus on Lower-Income Households and Small Businesses","Focus the UJALA (Unnat Jyoti by Affordable LEDs for All) programme on lower-income households and small commercial establishments.",""],[1,"81","12","Expansion of Standards and Labelling Coverage","The number of appliances covered under the Standards and Labelling (S&L) programme should be increased.",""],[1,"81","13","PAT Programme Expansion and ESCert Trading Enforcement","Widen and deepen the perform, achieve and trade (PAT) programme; make Energy Saving Certificate (ESCert) trading under the PAT scheme effective by ensuring strict penalties against defaulters.",""],[1,"81","14","Cluster-Specific Energy Efficiency Programme for MSMEs","For the MSME sector, BEE should develop cluster-specific programmes for energy intensive industries to introduce energy efficient technologies.",""],[1,"81","15","Lower Heat Rate Requirements for New Power Stations","The Forum of Regulators and State Electricity Regulatory Commissions (SERCs) should provide for lower heat rate requirements for new power stations.",""],[1,"81","15","Phased Retirement of Old Inefficient Power Plants","Old and inefficient plants consuming more than the threshold energy should be retired in a phased manner.",""]],"14":[[1,"19","9","Swachh Bharat Mission Expansion for Waste Management","The scope of Swachh Bharat Mission may be expanded to cover initiatives for landfills, plastic waste and municipal waste and generating wealth from waste.",""],[1,"64","1","Fiscal Support for Recycled Product Use","Fiscal support should be provided to companies that use recycled products made from waste.",""],[1,"120","6","Solid Waste Management Rules Implementation","Implementing effectively the Solid Waste Management Rules, 2016.",""],[1,"122","17","Implementation of Solid Waste Management Rules, 2016","Effective implementation of Solid Waste Management Rules, 2016, which has significantly expanded the scope of efficient solid waste management in the country, will help achieve environmental sustainability by 2022-23.",""],[1,"122","18","Contaminated Site Remediation and Hazardous Waste Disposal Programme","It is necessary to ensure the remediation of contaminated sites, safe disposal of hazardous substances, protection and restoration of ecosystems through stringent enforcement of relevant Acts, implementation of specific schemes, generation of awareness, stakeholders' participation and application of best practices.",""],[1,"122","18","Action Plans for Contaminated Site Remediation","Action plans for remediation of contaminated sites should be prepared and implemented.",""],[1,"122","24","Bio-Digester Toilet Deployment","The use of bio-digester toilets, a technology licensed by the Defence Research and",""],[1,"123","1","Nationwide Sanitation Technology Implementation","Development Organisation (DRDO), may be expeditiously considered for nationwide implementation.",""],[1,"123","2","Implementation of Revised Waste Management Rules","Revised waste management rules including Plastic Waste (Management and Handling) Rules, Bio-Medical Waste (Management and Handling) Rules, E-Waste (Management) Rules, Hazardous and other Wastes (Management and Trans-boundary Movement) Rules and Construction & Demolition Waste Management Rules should be effectively implemented.",""],[1,"123","3","Eco-Labelling Scheme for Waste-Based Products","Introduce an eco-labelling scheme to promote the sale of products made out of waste.",""],[1,"123","4","Strengthened Enforcement of Environment-Related Acts","Introduce stringent civil penalties to strengthen enforcement of environment-related Acts.",""]],"15":[[1,"18","7","Establishment of the Rail Development Authority","Expediting the establishment of the Rail Development Authority (RDA), which is already approved.",""],[1,"18","7","Integrated Rail Pricing Mechanism","RDA will advise or make informed decisions on an integrated, transparent and dynamic pricing mechanism for the railways.",""],[1,"18","7","Railway Investment Scale-Up and Asset Monetisation","Investment in railways will be ramped up, including by monetising existing railway assets.",""],[1,"88","11","Fare Structure and Subsidy Rationalization","Rationalize fare structures and subsidies, and monetize assets to generate revenues:",""],[1,"88","11","Public Asset Monetization for Revenue Generation","Rationalize fare structures and subsidies, and monetize assets to generate revenues:",""],[1,"88","12","Indian Railways Pricing Model Revision","Revisit IR's pricing model to make the passenger and freight segments sustainable.",""],[1,"88","13","Establishment of the Rail Development Authority","Expedite the process of establishing the Rail Development Authority (RDA), already approved by the government19.",""],[1,"88","13","Integrated Rail Fare Pricing Mechanism","RDA must advise/ make informed decisions on an integrated, transparent and dynamic pricing mechanism to determine rail fares and rebalance the passenger and freight categories to improve efficiency and rebalance the modal mix of goods transport.",""],[1,"88","14","Railway Land Monetization and Non-Railway Revenue Development","Monetize land resources with the railways, particularly through developing non-railway revenues such as through retail or other activities.",""],[1,"88","15","Railway Station Commercial Revenue Enhancement","Increase retail revenues from railway stations by investing in facilities, modernizing stations and contracting space to private players.",""],[1,"89","8","Independent Railway Homologation and Standardization Agency","Set up an independent homologation and standardization agency to adopt new railway technology and improve the speed and reliability of the railway network.",""],[1,"89","9","Common Transport Documents and Liability Regime Reform","Switch to common transport documents with (i) an internationally accepted liability regime for domestic and international transportation and (ii) common carrier status to all rail-based service providers.",""],[1,"89","10","Tariff and Non-Tariff Rule Stability Measure","To enhance credibility, ensure that there are no interim changes in tariff and non-tariff rules.",""],[1,"89","14","Independent Railway Regulator","Set up an independent regulator for the Indian Railways:",""],[1,"89","15","Formation of the Railway Development Authority","The government has already approved the formation of the RDA, an independent regulator for IR in February, 2018.",""],[1,"89","16","Price Regulation and Non-Fare Revenue Enhancement","Take decisions regarding price regulation and enhancement of non-fare revenue.",""],[1,"89","18","Investment Attraction and Standards Enforcement Measures","Help attract investment, promote efficient resource allocation, benchmark service standards and enforce standards.",""]],"16":[[1,"96","9","Sagarmala Port Modernization and Coastal Connectivity Programme","The Ministry of Shipping's Sagarmala programme focuses on modernizing and developing ports, enhancing port connectivity, supporting coastal communities and stimulating port-linked industrialization.","Ministry of Shipping"],[1,"96","10","Sagarmala Development Company Funding Support Mechanism","The government has set up the Sagarmala Development Company Limited (SDCL) to provide funding support to special purpose vehicles (SPVs) set up to implement projects",""],[1,"96","10","Port-Rail Connectivity Project Delivery Corporation","the Indian Port Rail Corporation Limited (IPRCL) to undertake port- rail connectivity projects under Sagarmala.",""],[1,"99","1","Dredging Market Liberalization","Open up India's dredging market",""],[1,"99","2","Dredging Market Liberalization and Contract Consolidation","The government needs to open up the dredging market to attract more players, particularly international players, in dredging activities to increase and maintain draft depth at ports to attract large vessels and enable them to become hub ports.",""],[1,"99","3","Major Port Draft Deepening Action Plan","To enable major ports to handle larger vessels, an action plan to increase the draft depth of ports has been prepared.",""],[1,"99","4","Sagarmala Implementation Acceleration","Expedite the implementation of Sagarmala",""],[1,"99","5","Sagarmala Project Acceleration","Expedite the completion of various projects under Sagarmala, especially those aimed at improving port connectivity, setting up coastal economic zones (CEZs) and establishing new ports.",""],[1,"99","6","Single-Window Cargo Clearance and Mechanized Cargo Handling Infrastructure","The setting up of a single window facility for cargo clearance and putting in place fully mechanized cargo handling infrastructure will be critical to increase throughput.",""],[1,"99","9","Port Technology Upgradation and Efficiency Improvement","Enhance technology use in ports and, wherever feasible, draw lessons from successful global ports such as Rotterdam, Felixstowe and Singapore to improve efficiency.",""],[1,"99","11","Transhipment Port Cluster Development","Transhipment via Cochin ICCT (already commissioned), the upcoming Vizhinjam Port and the Enayam Port at Colachel will create a transhipment cluster similar to the clusters in Malaysian and Singaporean ports.",""],[1,"100","17","Major Port Capacity Re-rating on Berthing Policy","Port capacity of major ports rerated on berthing policy as per international norms.",""]],"17":[[1,"18","8","Coastal Shipping and Inland Waterways Freight Expansion","The share of freight transported by coastal shipping and inland waterways will be doubled.",""],[1,"18","8","Viability Gap Funding for Transport Infrastructure","Initially, viability gap funding will be provided until the infrastructure is fully developed.",""],[1,"18","8","Integrated Multimodal Mobility IT Platform","An IT-enabled platform would be developed for integrating different modes of transport and promoting multi-modal and digitised mobility.",""],[1,"85","14","Multimodal Logistics Parks Development","Identify and develop multimodal logistics parks (MMLP) to ensure seamless movement of freight.",""],[1,"85","15","Road Freight Technology Adoption Incentive Scheme","Encourage the road freight industry to adopt innovative technologies through incentives.",""],[1,"101","4","Logistics Skills and Employment Expansion","Improve logistics skilling and increase jobs in the sector to 40 million by 2022-23 from about 22 million in 2016.",""],[1,"101","5","National Trade Facilitation Action Plan Border Compliance Time Reduction","As per the approved National Trade Facilitation Action Plan, reduce border compliance time to 24 hours for exports and to 48 hours for imports by 2020.",""],[1,"101","7","Logistics Inclusion in Infrastructure Master List","the government has included logistics in the harmonized master list of the infrastructure subsector.",""],[1,"101","8","Logistics Division for Integrated Sector Development","The government has also created a new Logistics Division in the Ministry of Commerce and Industry that will focus on the integrated development of the logistics sector, improving procedures and introducing new technologies.","Ministry of Commerce and Industry"],[1,"102","8","Tariff Rationalization and Pricing Reform","Tariff policies need to be rationalized.",""],[1,"102","9","Transport Data Repository Body","Create an overarching body that maintains a repository of all transport data: Such a body or institute will be responsible for acquiring, man- aging and disseminating data to internal stake- holders.",""],[1,"102","10","Warehouse Efficiency Enhancement for Food Storage","3. Enhance efficiency of warehouses and their operation, especially to optimize food storage:",""],[1,"102","11","Vertical Food Grain Storage and Specialized Transport System","Create vertical silos for food storage and transport food grains by specialized wagons.",""],[1,"103","1","Warehouse Modernization and Expansion","Optimize existing warehouse space.",""],[1,"103","2","Multimodal Logistics Parks Development","Setting up multimodal logistics parks will help address issues related to underdeveloped infrastructure, an unfavourable modal mix and connectivity.",""],[1,"103","3","Private Operation of CONCOR Terminals and Port Terminals","Allow private players to operate in CON- COR and port terminals: There is no level playing field for private container train opera- tors (CTOs) vis-à-vis the Container Corporation of India (CONCOR). Providing shared space at CONCOR terminals to private CTOs will help utilize the infrastructure better. Similarly, opening up port terminals to private players at a fee will enhance capacity utilization.",""],[1,"103","5","Integrated Transport Information Technology Platform","Integrate technologies across modes of trans- port by developing an integrated information technology (IT) platform.",""],[1,"103","6","Integrated Logistics IT Platform and Single-Window Portal","The integrated IT platform should be a single window for all logistics related matters.",""],[1,"103","6","Container Tracking and RFID-Based Logistics Efficiency System","teroperability of technology across modes by implementing container tracking systems, radio frequency identification (RFID), etc., will reduce delays and enhance efficiency.",""],[1,"103","7","Institutional Mechanism for Technology Adoption in Transport","Create an institutional mechanism for technology adoption in transport.","Commerce Ministry"],[1,"103","8","Adoption of International Transport Equipment and Software Standards","To increase efficiency and ensure compatibility, we should gradually adopt international standards, especially in operations, and adopt global benchmarking on unit load devices such as containers and pallets.",""]],"18":[[1,"88","2","Rail Terminal Strengthening","The functioning of terminals needs to be strengthened to improve rail freight.",""],[1,"88","5","Capacity Utilization Improvement and Network Upgrading","Prioritize ongoing projects to improve capacity utilization.",""],[1,"88","6","Dedicated Freight Corridors Completion and Feeder Route Development","Ensure that the dedicated freight corridors (DFCs) and the Mumbai-Ahmedabad High Speed Rail (MAHSR) are completed on schedule, particularly by timely completion of land acquisition for DFCs.",""],[1,"88","8","Private Sector Participation in Freight Terminal and Rolling Stock Operations","Consider opening up the ownership and operations of freight terminals and ownership of locomotives and rolling stock to the private sector under a transparent, neutral (non- railway) and fair regulatory mechanism.",""],[1,"88","9","Rail Coach and Locomotive Privatization with Safety Regulation","Consider transferring coach and locomotive manufacturing and repairs to private players.",""],[1,"89","11","Freight Scheduling and Routing Technology System","Use technology to schedule and route freight busi- ness to improve asset productivity and utilization.",""],[1,"89","12","Mission Hundred Freight Terminal Commissioning","Complete by 2022-23 the commissioning of the remaining 55 of the 100 new freight terminals announced in the Rail Budget of 2016-17 under 'Mission Hundred'.",""],[1,"89","13","Terminal Efficiency Improvement Measures","Improve terminal efficiency by promoting the concept of 'engine-on-load' system, developing proper terminal layouts, adopting efficient operational practices, operating trains end- to-end, and using proper handling methods/ systems for loading and unloading operations.",""],[1,"89","20","Non-Discriminatory Open Access Framework for Dedicated Freight Corridors","Provide a framework for non-discriminatory open access to the dedicated freight. corridors",""]],"19":[[1,"108","1","Smart Cities Urban Cluster Initiative","Leverage the 'Smart Cities' concept in select urban clusters to:",""],[1,"108","4","Technology for Inclusive, Sustainable and Participatory Development","Leverage technology for inclusive, sustainable and participatory development by 2022-23.",""],[1,"108","6","Smart Cities Mission Project Implementation","These cities have started implementing projects such as smart command and control centres, smart area- based development, smart roads, solar rooftops, intelligent transport systems and smart parks.",""],[1,"108","9","Inter-Agency Coordination Mechanism with Special Purpose Vehicles","An institutional mechanism for inter-agency coordination, including special purpose vehicles (SPVs), for effective delivery.",""],[1,"108","10","Robust Spatial Planning Framework for Smart Cities","A robust spatial plan as an overall framework within which smart city planning and implementation can happen.",""],[1,"108","12","Digital Master Plan and Roadmap","A digital master plan or a digital strategy and roadmap.",""],[1,"108","15","Smart Cities Financing and ULB Financial Sustainability Support","Financing smart cities and financial sustainability of ULBs.",""],[1,"109","3","Scaling Area-Based Urban Development","Scaling area-based development.",""]],"20":[[1,"48","16","Adoption of the Model Contract Farming Act, 2018","Encourage states to adopt the Model Contract Farming Act, 2018:",""],[1,"49","2","Model Contract Farming Act","The Draft Model Contract Farming Act, 2018, is an attempt to provide an enabling environment for contract farming to thrive.",""],[1,"49","3","Contract Farming Dispute Resolution Mechanism","The Model Act contains several provisions for dispute resolution.",""],[1,"49","4","Adoption of the Model Agricultural Land Leasing Act","Encourage states to adopt the Model Agri- culture Land Leasing Act, 2016:",""],[1,"207","2","Land Leasing Legalization and Simplification","Legalise and ease land leasing.",""],[1,"207","3","Farmland Consolidation Initiative","Consolidate fragmented plots of farmers to enhance efficiency and equity.",""],[1,"207","6","Waste and Fallow Land Productive Use Programme","Convert waste and fallow land to productive uses.",""],[1,"209","4","Land Pooling and Consolidation Scheme","Consolidate smaller plots of land through pooling to enhance productivity.",""],[1,"210","1","Public-Private Partnership Wasteland Development Initiative","Initiating Public Private Partnerships (PPPs) for wasteland development",""]],"21":[[1,"7","3","Agricultural Modernization Programme","We will have to focus on the necessary modernization of our agriculture",""],[1,"41","1","Agricultural Technology Modernization and Productivity Enhancement","Modernize agricultural technology, increase productivity, efficiency and crop diversification.",""],[1,"41","2","Agricultural Value Addition and Food Security Strategy","Generate income and employment through a paradigm shift that ensures food security while maximizing value addition in agriculture.",""],[1,"46","3","Agripreneurship Promotion Policy","Promote through government policies the emergence of 'agripreneurs' so that even small and marginal farmers can capture a higher share of value addition from 'farmgate to fork'.",""],[1,"46","6","Private Investment Promotion in Agriculture","The current government has taken several steps to improve private investment in agriculture.",""],[1,"50","10","Agripreneur Development and Agro-processing Promotion","Create and nurture agripreneurs for achieving greater value addition through agro-processing and propagation of modern extension services.",""],[1,"52","1","Rural Infrastructure and Integrated Value Chain Development","Transform the rural economy through the creation of modern rural infrastructure and an integrated value chain system.",""],[1,"52","3","Occupational Diversification and Quality Improvement Initiative","Create occupational diversification and quality",""],[1,"54","10","Agripreneur Promotion Initiative","The government has now shifted its attention to promoting \"agripreneurs\".",""]],"22":[[1,"50","2","Increase Agricultural Research Spending","Research spending, currently at 0.3 per cent, needs to be increased to at least 1 per cent of agricultural GDP.",""]],"23":[[1,"18","3","Expansion of e-National Agriculture Markets","In agriculture, emphasis must shift to converting farmers to 'agripreneurs' by further expanding e-National Agriculture Markets (e-NAMs) and replacing the Agricultural Produce Marketing Committee (APMC) Act with the Agricultural Produce and Livestock Marketing (APLM) Act.",""],[1,"18","3","Agricultural Marketing Law Reform","In agriculture, emphasis must shift to converting farmers to 'agripreneurs' by further expanding e-National Agriculture Markets (e-NAMs) and replacing the Agricultural Produce Marketing Committee (APMC) Act with the Agricultural Produce and Livestock Marketing (APLM) Act.",""],[1,"18","3","Unified Agricultural Market and Trade Liberalization","The creation of a unified national market, a freer export regime and abolition of the Essential Commodities Act are essential for boosting agricultural growth.",""],[1,"47","4","Mechanism to Ensure Remunerative Farm Prices","Mechanisms need to be developed to ensure remunerative prices to farmers, in both 'good' and 'bad' monsoon years.",""],[1,"47","8","Adoption of the Model Agricultural Produce and Livestock Marketing Act","Many of the constraints in marketing can be addressed by adopting the Model Agricultural Produce and Livestock Marketing Act (APLM), 2017,3 which provides for progressive agricul- tural marketing reforms, including the setting up of markets in the private sector, allowing",""],[1,"48","1","Agricultural Market Liberalization and Unified Trading System","direct sales to exporters/processors and cus- tomers, farmer-consumer markets, e-trading, single point levy of market fee, a unified single trading licence in a state, declaring warehouses/ silos/cold storage as market sub-yards and the launch of the National Market for Agriculture.",""],[1,"48","5","Minimum Reserve Price Auction Reform","Replacing the minimum support price (MSP) by a minimum reserve price (MRP), which could be the starting point for auctions at mandis.",""],[1,"48","8","Private Trader Inclusion in Minimum Support Price Regime","Examine options for including private traders operating in markets to complement the minimum support price regime through a system of incentives and commission payments.",""],[1,"48","9","National Agricultural Market Integration Reform","A long-term solution lies in the creation of a competitive, stable and unified national market to enable better price discovery, and a long-term trade regime favourable to exports.",""],[1,"49","1","Farmer Produce Procurement Contracting","contract will specify the price and quality at which the farmers' produce will be purchased.",""],[1,"53","5","Development of Grameen Agriculture Markets","The recent 2018-19 budget announcement to develop the existing 22,000 Rural Periodic Markets (RPMs) into Grameen Agriculture Markets (GrAMs) will offer better market access to small and marginal farmers.",""],[1,"53","5","Electronic National Agriculture Market Platform","The electronic national agriculture market (e-NAM) was launched in 2016 to create a unified national market.",""],[1,"54","8","Village-Level Procurement Centres and Warehousing Facilities","To benefit small and marginal farmers, government collection centres and warehousing facilities should be set up at the village/block level.",""],[1,"54","8","Gramin Agricultural Markets (GrAMs) Development","The budget announcement of developing Gramin Agricultural Markets (GrAMs) will help develop the agricultural marketing infrastructure and bring markets closer to the farm-gate.",""],[1,"54","11","Private Rural Market Yard Development","Rural markets: Develop private market yards.",""],[1,"54","11","Government-Private Sourcing Partnership for Rural Markets","Agro-processors and food processors that wish to establish backward integration to secure their raw material should partner with the government in organizing sourcing through the RPMs.",""],[1,"54","12","Wholesale Market Upgrading Programme","Upgrade wholesale markets with facilities for temporary storage, pack- house operations and cold storage facilities.",""],[1,"55","1","Warehouse Receipt Financing and e-NWR Trading Promotion","Pledge financing at warehouses, through negotiable warehouse receipts (NWR), needs to be adopted and popularized as an alternative means of financing.","Department of Agriculture and Farmers' Welfare (DACFW)"]],"24":[[1,"66","2","Tourism Infrastructure and Facilitation Measures","Recognizing the sector's potential to generate income and employment, the government has undertaken several measures to strengthen infrastructure and facilitate tourism.",""],[1,"66","2","Tourism Circuit Development Schemes","The government has launched several schemes to develop tourist circuits; develop our islands as tourist destinations; build large-scale convention centres in different cities; improve connectivity and develop niche offerings such as medical tourism and pilgrimage-based tourism.",""],[1,"66","2","Island Tourism Destination Development","The government has launched several schemes to develop tourist circuits; develop our islands as tourist destinations; build large-scale convention centres in different cities; improve connectivity and develop niche offerings such as medical tourism and pilgrimage-based tourism.",""],[1,"66","2","Convention Centre Construction Programme","The government has launched several schemes to develop tourist circuits; develop our islands as tourist destinations; build large-scale convention centres in different cities; improve connectivity and develop niche offerings such as medical tourism and pilgrimage-based tourism.",""],[1,"66","2","Tourism Connectivity Improvement Programme","The government has launched several schemes to develop tourist circuits; develop our islands as tourist destinations; build large-scale convention centres in different cities; improve connectivity and develop niche offerings such as medical tourism and pilgrimage-based tourism.",""],[1,"66","2","Niche Tourism Development Initiatives","The government has launched several schemes to develop tourist circuits; develop our islands as tourist destinations; build large-scale convention centres in different cities; improve connectivity and develop niche offerings such as medical tourism and pilgrimage-based tourism.",""],[1,"67","3","Tourism Infrastructure Notification for Priority Lending","Tourism infrastructure projects, viz., hotels, resorts, equipment, parks etc., having a project cost more than INR 1 crore should be notified as 'infrastructure' to enable promoters to avail loans on a priority basis.",""],[1,"67","4","Heritage Site Conservation and Development","Conservation and development of all heritage sites should be undertaken and completed through either government funding or through NGOs/Corporate Social Responsibility (CSR) activities.",""],[1,"67","4","Swadesh Darshan and PRASHAD Heritage Site Development","The Ministry of Tourism's Swadesh Darshan and National Mission on Pilgrimage Rejuvenation and Spiritual Heritage Augmentation Drive (PRASHAD) schemes are already undertaking the development or maintenance of heritage sites.","Ministry of Tourism"],[1,"67","4","Expansion and Acceleration of Heritage Site Projects","The number of projects sanctioned under this scheme should be increased and their implementation accelerated.",""],[1,"67","5","Domestic Tourism Infrastructure Upgrading and PPP Destination Development","Increase domestic tourist traffic by upgrading existing infrastructure and leasing out the maintenance of such infrastructure to private players.",""],[1,"67","11","Buddhist Circuit Promotion and Connectivity Enhancement","Promote India's Buddhist circuit by increas- ing coordination among all stakeholders and improving connectivity.",""],[1,"67","12","Smart Tourist Destination Sites Development","Develop 100 \"Smart Tourist Destination Sites\" showcasing theme-based museums and heri- tage sites.",""],[1,"67","13","Model Swachh Tourist Destinations Initiative","Develop 100 \"Model Swachh Tourist Destina- tions\" by undertaking a special clean-up initia- tive focused on 100 iconic heritage, spiritual and cultural places in the country.",""],[1,"67","14","Beach Destinations as Exclusive Tourism Zones","Develop at least five \"Beach Destinations\" as exclusive tourism zones.",""],[1,"68","2","Development of World-Class National Circuits","Plan and develop five globally competitive and world-class national circuits from entry to exit.",""]],"25":[[1,"19","4","Urban Affordable Housing Expansion","affordable housing in urban areas will be given a huge push to improve workers' living conditions and ensure equity while providing a strong impetus to economic growth.",""],[1,"24","8","Public Investment in Housing","Investment in housing, especially in urban areas, will create very large multiplier effects in the economy.",""],[1,"61","1","Universal Pucca Housing and Basic Services Provision","Provide every family with a pucca house, with a water connection, toilet facilities, and 24x7 electricity supply and access.",""],[1,"61","2","Rural and Urban Housing Construction Programme","Build 2.95 core housing units in rural areas and 1.2 crore housing units in urban areas.",""],[1,"61","3","Housing for All Scheme","The President's clarion call to ensure the provision of houses to every family remains the key objective of the 'Housing for All' scheme.",""],[1,"61","4","Rural Housing Scheme for BPL Families","Since 1985, the Government of India has been implementing a rural housing scheme for families living below the poverty line (BPL).",""],[1,"61","4","Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana (Gramin) - PMAY-G","A new scheme, the Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana (Gramin - PMAY-G) was launched in 2016.",""],[1,"61","6","Convergence of PMAY-G with Sanitation and Rural Employment Schemes","PMAY-G is converged with Swachh Bharat Mission (Gramin) and Mahatma Gandhi National Rural Employment Guarantee Scheme (MGNREGS) for the construction of sanitary toilets and also to provide the unskilled wage component.",""],[1,"61","7","PMAY-G Rural Housing Construction Programme","Under PMAY-G, it was proposed to build one crore rural houses in three years between 2016-17 and 2018-19.",""],[1,"61","8","Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana (Urban) Housing for All Mission","Under the Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana (Urban- PMAY-U), the mission aims to achieve the objective of 'Housing for All' by 2022 through its four pillars - a) in-situ slum redevelopment; b) affordable housing through a credit linked subsidy scheme; c) affordable housing in partnership between public and private agencies and d) subsidy for beneficiary- led individual house construction or enhancement.",""],[1,"63","1","Affordable Housing Constraint-Reduction Measures","The strategies to overcome the constraints on affordable housing can be grouped into the following categories: 1) access to finance; 2) technology for construction; 3) reducing costs and 4) efficient use of land.",""],[1,"63","2","Priority Sector Lending Support for Affordable Housing","To ensure greater access for the poor to institutional finance, the Department of Financial Services should consider a sub- category under priority sector lending (PSL) for affordable houses.","Department of Financial Services"],[1,"63","2","Relaxation of Housing Loan Eligibility Conditions","It should also consider relaxing eligibility conditions for bank loans such as raising the cap of INR 10 lakh on the cost of the house and raising the INR 2-lakh income threshold.",""],[1,"63","3","Affordable Housing Fund","The Union Budget 2018-19 announced the setting up of an Affordable Housing Fund in the National Housing Bank (NHB).","National Housing Bank (NHB)"],[1,"63","5","Alternative and Sustainable Construction Technologies","These alternate and sustainable technologies offer safer and disaster resilient affordable housing.",""],[1,"63","7","Public Housing Redevelopment Replication","The success of the East Kidwai Nagar redevelopment project in Delhi may be replicated wherever possible.",""],[1,"63","8","Converged Mason Training Initiative","It is necessary to ensure convergence of provisions under the National Urban Livelihood Mission, Pradhan Mantri Kaushal Vikas Yojana, Construction Skill Development Council of India and MGNREGS (for rural areas) for large-scale training of masons to meet construction targets.",""],[1,"63","10","Life Cycle Cost Housing Construction Approach","Government projects should focus on the life cycle cost (LCC) approach to the construction of houses rather than the cost per square foot approach to ensure quality of construction and reduce expenditure incurred on the maintenance of houses.",""],[1,"64","2","Single-Window Urban Housing Approval Reform","Regulatory complexities should be rationalized and a single window approval system adopted to reduce the time taken to construct houses in urban areas.",""],[1,"64","3","Rental-Cum-Ownership Housing Scheme","Financial engineering, like 'rental-cum- ownership housing' in which houses are initially offered on rent and ownership is transferred to the tenant once the cost of the unit is recovered, should be adopted.",""],[1,"64","4","Use Idle PSU Land for Affordable Housing","The land lying idle with various sick/loss making public sector undertakings(PSUs) of the central/ state governments may be used to resolve the issue of land availability for affordable housing projects under 'Housing for All'.",""],[1,"64","5","Release of PSU Land Parcels for Affordable Housing","The Department of Public Enterprises (DPE) should expedite release of land parcels available with central PSUs that have been identified for affordable housing projects.","Department of Public Enterprises (DPE)"],[1,"64","8","Urban Vertical Growth Awareness Campaign","Launch a mass campaign to sensitize cities and states on the benefits of vertical growth.",""],[1,"64","9","Capacity Building for Vertical Growth Measures","Provide capacity building to states and cities willing to undertake measures towards vertical growth.",""],[1,"64","10","Incentives for Cities to Relax Floor Space Index Norms","Provide considerable rewards to cities that relax their floor space index (FSI) norms.",""],[1,"64","10","Accelerated Review of Floor Space Index Norms","The discussion on changing FSI norms considering trunk infrastructure and other social issues needs to be expedited across India.",""],[1,"64","11","Central Funding Incentive for FSI Reforms in Cities","Provide additional central government funding to cities that undertake FSI reforms under the Smart Cities Mission.",""]],"26":[[1,"63","9","National Slum Rehabilitation Mission","A National Mission for Slum Rehabilitation will bring a greater focus on making the country slum free.",""]],"27":[[1,"116","4","Industrial Water Supply and Zero-Discharge Effluent Control","Provide water to industries, encourage industries to utilize recycled/treated water and ensure zero discharge of untreated effluents from industrial units.",""],[1,"120","7","Industrial Wastewater Recycling and Zero-Discharge Compliance","Encouraging industries to utilize recycled/ treated water to the extent possible and ensuring zero discharge of untreated effluents from industrial units.",""],[1,"122","20","Brick Kiln Pollution Control Task Force","A task force should be set up to study and implement measures to control pollution from brick kilns.",""],[1,"122","21","Industrial Emission and Effluent Standards Revision and Enforcement","Emission and effluent standards for industries need to be revised and effectively implemented.",""],[1,"122","22","Sewage Treatment Plant Installation","Sewage treatment plants of adequate capacity should be installed at suitable locations to make rivers pollution free.",""],[1,"122","23","Industrial Wastewater Discharge Reduction","Wastewater discharge from industrial units into rivers and other water bodies should be reduced to zero.",""]],"28":[[1,"46","6","SAMPADA Food Processing Infrastructure Scheme","Similarly, the SAMPADA scheme targets creation of food processing infrastructure.",""],[1,"52","2","Food Product Export Value Chain Enhancement","Leverage the value chain to boost India's exports of food products.",""],[1,"53","9","SAMPADA Agri-Value Chain Modernisation Scheme","The SAMPADA central sector scheme aims to supplement agriculture by modernising processing activities and decreasing agri-waste.",""],[1,"53","9","Operation Green","Similarly, in the 2018- 19 budget, 'Operation Green' on the lines of 'Operation Flood' was announced.",""],[1,"54","9","Village-Level Collection Centres Linked to Processing Units","Village level collection centres for fruits and vegetables should be linked to larger processing units.",""],[1,"54","9","Private Sector Development of Rural Processing Centres","Actively engage the private sector in developing processing centres near rural periodic markets (RPMs).",""],[1,"54","10","Food Processing Industry Promotion","A greater focus should be placed on the food processing industry for enhancing value addition in vegetable and fruit crops.",""],[1,"55","2","Block Level Resource Centres","Establish functional block level resource centres to create value chains, targeting clusters of villages along with social services.",""],[1,"55","3","Inter-Ministerial Coordination for Agricultural Value Chain Development","Coordination is needed between the initiatives of the Ministry of Agriculture, Food Processing, and Commerce to develop effective procurement linkages, processing facilities, retail chains and export activity.","Ministry of Agriculture | Ministry of Food Processing | Ministry of Commerce"]],"29":[[1,"24","9","Foreign Direct Investment Liberalization","The government has taken significant measures to attract foreign direct investment by easing caps on the extent of permissible stake holding",""],[1,"25","1","Further Liberalization of FDI Norms","By 2022-23, the government may consider further liberalizing FDI norms across sectors.",""],[1,"25","1","Foreign Investment Mobilization for Bonds and Government Securities","Domestic savings can be complemented by attracting foreign investment in bonds and government securities.",""],[1,"25","1","Relaxation of Regulatory Limits for Rupee-Denominated Debt","Regulatory limits can be relaxed for rupee denominated debt.",""],[1,"25","13","Financial Market Deepening Measures","There is a need to deepen financial markets with easier availability of capital, greater use",""],[1,"26","3","GIFT-Based Financial Sector Liberalization","The Gujarat International Finance and Tech City (GIFT) should be leveraged to push the envelope on financial sector liberalization.",""],[1,"26","4","Bond Market Deepening and Regulatory Liberalization","The bond market needs deepening through liberalization of regulations and continued fiscal consolidation.",""]],"31":[[1,"7","4","Public Service Delivery and Governance Reform","the government has focused on the efficient delivery of public services, rooting out corruption and black economy, formalizing the economy and expanding the tax base, improving the ease of doing business, nursing the stressed commercial banking sector back to a healthy state, and stopping leakages through direct benefit transfers and widespread use of the JAM trinity.",""],[1,"18","9","Digital Delivery of Government Services","The aim will be to deliver all government services at the state, district, and gram panchayat level digitally by 2022-23, thereby eliminating the digital divide.",""]],"32":[[1,"49","5","Land Records Digitization and Geo-tagging Initiative","Complete digitiza- tion of land records is a must for effective implementation of land leasing.",""],[1,"59","17","Digital Central Land Holding Register","a central land holding register could be prepared and maintained in a digital format.",""],[1,"207","4","Digitized and Integrated Land Records System","Create a digitized and integrated land records system that is easily accessible in all states.",""],[1,"209","11","Land Record System Updating and Modernization","Updating and modernization of land record systems",""],[1,"209","12","Digital Land Records Modernization Programme","Beyond creating and maintaining land records, efforts must be made to update and digitize these records in a user-friendly manner.",""],[1,"209","13","Statewide Land Record Digitization","all states must have digitized textual as well as spatial records so that they are easily available and verifiable.",""],[1,"209","13","Land Record Database-Bank Linkage","It will also be desirable to link the land record database with banks.",""],[1,"209","14","State Digitization and Land Titling Reform","Other states should review their progress in terms of digitization and move toward complete and accessible up-to-date records.",""],[1,"209","14","Conclusive Land Titling Transition","In due course, states may move towards conclusive land titling.",""],[1,"210","4","Property Rights Strengthening and Urban Planning Measures","Strengthen property rights, plan urbanization and prevent land degradation.",""],[1,"210","5","Common Land Identification and Tenure Clarification","Define and identify common land, along with details of ownership, control and use rights.",""],[1,"210","7","Public Land Encroachment Removal","Remove encroachments on public land to ensure that land is used efficiently.",""],[1,"210","8","Speedy Disposal of Land Litigation Cases","Free estimated ceiling surplus land of over 1 lakh acres that has been under litigation for several years through speedy disposal of cases.",""]],"33":[[1,"7","3","Technology Adoption, Innovation, and Upskilling Initiative","This implies embracing new technologies fostering innovation and upskilling.",""],[1,"18","5","Labour Law Codification and Apprenticeship Expansion","To ensure maximum employment creation, codification of labour laws must be completed and a massive effort must be made to upscale apprenticeships.",""],[1,"27","4","Labour Employability Enhancement and Apprenticeship Expansion","the employability of labour needs to be enhanced by improving health, education and skilling outcomes and a massive expansion of the apprenticeship scheme.",""],[1,"29","4","Employment Generation Schemes","The government has put in place several schemes to help generate employment.",""],[1,"30","5","Skills and Apprenticeships Enhancement","1. Enhance skills and apprenticeships",""],[1,"30","6","Labour Market Information System Operationalization","The LMIS should be made functional urgently.",""],[1,"30","7","Expansion of Apprenticeship Programmes","Ensure the wider use of apprenticeship programmes by all enterprises.",""],[1,"30","14","Inclusive Skills Training and Apprenticeship Programme","Ensure that skills training programmes and apprenticeships include women.",""]],"34":[[1,"19","2","Ayushman Bharat Health and Wellness Centres and Pradhan Mantri Jan Arogya Abhiyaan Rollout","Successfully implementing the Ayushman Bharat programme including the establishment of 150,000 health and wellness centres across the country, and rolling out the Pradhan Mantri Jan Arogya Abhiyaan.",""],[1,"149","1","Ayushman Bharat Comprehensive Primary Health Care Scale-up","Under Ayushman Bharat, scale-up a new vision for comprehensive primary health care across the country, built on the platform of health and wellness centres (HWCs), to:",""],[1,"149","2","Quality Ambulatory Services Expansion","Provide quality ambulatory services for an inclusive package of diagnostic, curative, rehabilitative and palliative care, close to the people.",""],[1,"149","8","Comprehensive Primary Health Care through Health and Wellness Centres","The National Health Policy (NHP), 2017, envisages comprehensive primary health care delivered through HWCs.",""],[1,"149","8","Primary Care Spending Allocation Commitment","The policy also commits that two-thirds or more of government spending will be targeted at primary care.",""],[1,"149","10","Health and Wellness Centre Expansion","the government is committed to accelerating the pace of sanctioning and putting up HWCs to meet the target in good time.",""],[1,"150","15","Health and Wellness Centre Network Expansion","Accelerate the establishment of a network of 150,000 HWCs",""],[1,"150","16","Health and Wellness Centre Network Expansion","Operationalize a network of 150,000 HWCs on priority by 2022-23 in order to ensure sufficient coverage of affordable primary care and lower the burden on secondary and tertiary care.",""],[1,"150","17","Health and Wellness Centre Service Expansion","HWCs should provide services such as screening and management of non- communicable diseases; screening and basic management of mental health ailments; care for common ophthalmic and ENT problems; basic dental health care; geriatric and palliative health care, and trauma care and emergency care.",""],[1,"151","3","Primary Health Care Nucleus Upgrade","A primary health care nucleus comprising five to six upgraded sub-centres coupled with a primary health centre, and population outreach.",""],[1,"151","5","District Health Facility Distribution Planning and Referral Linkage","Planning of health facility distribution in districts to ensure that a continuum of care is available on the principles of 'time to care' through a strong referral linkage.",""],[1,"151","6","Digitization of Family and Facility-Level Health Records","Digitization of family records and information from the community to the facility level.",""],[1,"151","7","Real-Time Public Health Data for Action and Monitoring","Use of real-time data to guide public health action and implementation monitoring.",""],[1,"151","8","Health and Wellness Centre Gateway Referral Function","The HWCs would act as the 'gateway' for access to secondary and tertiary health services.",""],[1,"151","9","Rapid Scale-Up Mechanisms","Enable mechanisms for rapid scale up",""],[1,"151","10","Health and Wellness Centre Expansion Workstreams","Put in place the following work streams to create 150,000 well-functioning HWCs across the country - infrastructure; human resources (mid-level professional recruitment, training",""],[1,"152","2","Ayushman Bharat Institutional Mechanisms for Health and Wellness","Under Ayushman Bharat, put in place the necessary institutional mechanisms with a focus on health and wellness at the central and state levels for effective, timely and robust system level implementation as well as strong engagement with departments/directorates of health in the states.",""],[1,"152","3","Special National and State-Level Task Forces and Command Centres","Establish special national and state level task forces and 'command centres'.",""],[1,"152","5","Empowered Governance Mechanisms for Efficient Implementation","Develop empowered governance mechanisms for efficient decision-making, coordination, funds flow, procurement, contracting, recruitment, construction and implementation.",""],[1,"152","6","CSR and NRI Funding Mobilization for Health and Wellness Centres","Mobilize Corporate Social Responsibility (CSR) and Non-Resident Indians for funding HWCs.",""],[1,"152","7","Mobile Health and Wellness Centres","Some HWCs could also be mobile, particularly for better access to remote communities.",""],[1,"152","11","Partnerships Between Health and Frontline Development Teams","Facilitate partnerships between HWC teams and other frontline development teams (nutrition, education, Swachh Bharat etc.) to engage with communities to address the socio-cultural and environmental determinants of ill health at the local level.",""],[1,"152","13","Health and Wellness Centre Community Partnership Mechanism","Mandate and motivate HWC teams to work closely with village health, sanitation and nutrition societies, panchayati raj institutions as well as all other constituents of civil society in rural and urban spaces.",""],[1,"152","14","Concurrent Learning, Operations Research, and Innovation Promotion","Emphasise concurrent learning, operations research and innovation",""],[1,"152","15","Primary Health Care Scaling Research Programme","Undertake a well-funded research programme to find the best pathways for effective and context-specific scaling up of primary health care.",""],[1,"152","17","Urban Primary Care Adaptation Programme","Develop urban adaptations of comprehensive primary care.",""],[1,"153","3","Deployment of Mid-Level Providers in Primary Healthcare","Deploy mid-level providers (MLPs) to manage the primary healthcare system.",""]],"35":[[1,"152","4","Rapid Training Scale-Up Mechanisms","Create mechanisms for rapid scaling up of training.",""],[1,"153","2","Health Workforce Availability in High-Priority Districts","Ensure availability of paramedics and doctors as per Indian Public Health Standard (IPHS) norms in high priority districts by 2020 (National Health Policy, 2017).",""],[1,"155","12","Governance Reform of Medical and Health Professional Education","Reform the governance of medical, nursing, dentistry and pharmacy education in the country",""],[1,"155","13","National Medical Commission Bill Enactment","Enact the NMC Bill, 2017.",""],[1,"155","14","Regulatory Council Revamp for AYUSH and Health Professions","Revamp the AYUSH, nursing, dentistry and pharmacy councils along the lines of the NMC Bill, 2017.",""],[1,"155","15","Council for Allied Health Professionals","Establish a Council for Allied Health Professionals to ensure standardization of education and putting in place quality control mechanisms for educational institutions, teaching methods, clinical protocols and workforce management.",""],[1,"155","16","Updated Medical and Allied Professions Curriculum","Put in place an updated curriculum for medical and allied professions that keeps pace with the changing dynamics of public health, policy and demographics.",""],[1,"155","17","District Nursing School Expansion","Establish a nursing school in every large district or cluster of districts with a population of 20-30 lakhs as per the National Health Policy, 2017.",""],[1,"155","18","Nursing Education Regulatory and Quality Reform","Take steps to revamp the regulatory system of nursing education, ensure quality training in nursing schools, develop specialties in nursing, develop centres of excellence in nursing and enhance the stature of government nurses.",""],[1,"155","19","Faculty Private Practice Restriction and Incentive Reform","Take steps to stop private practice by faculty of government teaching institutions by providing attractive salaries and incentives.",""],[1,"156","1","Doctor Production Expansion","2. Enhance production of doctors (especially specialists and super- specialists)",""],[1,"156","2","Expansion of DNB and CPS Diploma Training System","While some steps have been taken, the system of Diplomate of National Board (DNB) and Diplomas from CPS, may be expanded.",""],[1,"156","3","District Hospital-Medical College Linkage Initiative","Link at least 40 per cent of district hospitals with medical colleges.",""],[1,"156","4","Faculty Shortage Recruitment and Visiting Faculty System for New AIIMS","Meet faculty shortages in new AIIMS with an active search strategy, visiting/adjunct faculty system (from India and abroad), and other methods.",""],[1,"156","5","Private Hospital Doctor Specialty Training Pathways","Create pathways for training of doctors in specialties and super-specialties at private hospitals (certification, short courses, exchange programmes, etc.)",""],[1,"156","6","District Hospital Specialty Training Incentive Programme","Utilize extensively and incentivize district hospitals for formal (DNB/CPS diploma) and informal specialty training of doctors and nurses.",""],[1,"156","7","Specialized Training Opportunities for Medical Faculty","Provide opportunities for training in specialized/cutting edge areas at the best centres in the world for faculty of national institutions of excellence (NIEs) (AIIMS, PGIMER, JIPMER, NIMHANS) and of state medical colleges of repute.",""],[1,"156","8","Facilitate Import of Doctors of Indian Origin","Create conditions to facilitate the import of doctors, especially those of Indian origin, working abroad.",""],[1,"156","9","Visiting Professor Deployment at AIIMS and NIEs","Consider deploying teachers from universities abroad as visiting professors at AIIMS/NIEs.",""],[1,"156","10","Private Sector Doctor Deployment Pilot Framework","An enabling framework for deployment of doctors and specialists from the private sector to government hospitals on a visiting/honorary basis may be developed and piloted.",""],[1,"156","11","State Human Resources for Health Policy Development","3. Develop a comprehensive HRH policy in states",""],[1,"156","12","Model State Human Resources for Health Policy","develop a model policy covering issues pertaining to staff recruitment, retention, transfer, incentive structures for posting in difficult areas including access to housing facilities, performance management and competency- based career tracks for professional advancement.",""],[1,"156","13","Non-Physician Health Provider Deployment","Skill and deploy non-physicians and other health providers",""],[1,"156","14","Allied Health Professionals Training Plan","Develop plans for training a full range of allied health professionals such that it meets national requirements as well as creates a surplus for placements abroad.",""],[1,"156","15","Primary Healthcare Practitioner Cadre Development Programme","Create a cadre of primary healthcare practitioners by introducing a three-year competency-based dynamic course for primary, community and family medicine.",""],[1,"156","16","Deployment of Skilled and Independently Certified MLPs for Health and Wellness Centres","Place 150,000 skilled and independently certified MLPs to manage the health and wellness centres to be operationalized over the next five years.",""],[1,"156","17","Task Shifting for Nursing Practitioners and Physician Assistants","Explore some specific task shifting opportunities like developing a cadre of nursing practitioners and physician assistants.",""],[1,"156","19","Real-Time Human Resources for Health Data System","Generate comprehensive real-time data on forecasting, production capacity and skill mix as well as generate trends with respect to the key categories of HRH in the country.",""],[1,"156","20","HRH Progress Tracking System","By 2019, put in place a system for tracking progress against the stipulated HRH requirements.",""],[1,"157","2","Private Sector Engagement for Skilling and Training of Human Resources for Health","Engage private sector for skilling and training HRH",""],[1,"157","3","Medical Device Industry Skills Partnership","Establish partnerships with medical device manufacturers as part of the Skill India and Make in India programmes to identify skill gaps",""],[1,"157","5","Healthcare Sector Skill Development Partnership","Partner with private hospitals/private medical practitioners to skill technicians, nursing and para-nursing as well as para-medical staff under the National Skill Development Corporation's Healthcare Sector Skill Council.",""],[1,"157","8","District Hospital-Medical College Linkage Initiative","up to 20 per cent of district hospitals must be linked with medical colleges by 2020.",""]],"36":[[1,"116","2","Safe Drinking Water and Sanitation Water Supply Provision","Provide adequate (rural: 40 litres per capita per day (lpcd); urban 135 lpcd) and safe drinking water (piped) and water for sanitation for citizens and livestock.",""],[1,"119","2","Rural Drinking Water Quality Improvement in Contaminated Areas","Special focus should be placed on the quality of rural drinking water supply in arsenic and fluo- ride affected areas by tapping multiple sources through conjunctive use of surface water, ground water and rain water harvesting.",""],[1,"119","2","Community-Based Operation and Maintenance for Piped Water Schemes","All new, piped water supply schemes should have mandatory provisions on operation and maintenance involv- ing local communities and stakeholders.",""],[1,"147","12","Mainstream Nutrition, Water, and Sanitation in Local Government Functions","Make nutrition, water and sanitation part of the core functions of panchayati raj institutions and municipalities.",""]],"37":[[1,"106","7","Telecom Service Quality Monitoring System","TRAI should consider putting in place a credible system to track call drops, weak signals and outages to ensure the quality and reliability of telecom services.","TRAI"],[1,"106","7","Telecom Ombudsman for Complaint Redressal","Government should also put in place telecom ombudsman for complaint redressal.",""],[1,"106","8","Efficient Spectrum Allocation and Technology Migration","Efficient spectrum allocation in large contiguous blocks should be explored.",""],[1,"106","8","Migration to New Telecommunications Technologies","We should also explore migration to new technologies which would resolve some of the bandwidth challenges.",""]],"38":[[1,"120","3","Renewable Energy Generation Capacity Expansion","Creating 175 GW of renewable energy generation capacity.",""],[1,"123","15","New National Wind Energy Mission","New national missions on wind energy, waste-to-energy and coastal areas should be developed.",""]],"39":[[1,"82","2","Road Network Expansion for Connectivity","Increase connectivity by expanding the road network:",""],[1,"82","3","Bharatmala Phase-I Road Connectivity Programme","Achieve the Bharatmala Phase-I target by completing 24,800 km by 2021-22, including 2,000 km of coastal and port connectivity roads.",""],[1,"82","4","PMGSY Phase I Completion and Quality Monitoring","Complete Phase I of the Pradhan Mantri Gram Sadak Yojana (PMGSY) with quality monitoring at every stage.",""],[1,"82","7","Road Regulatory Framework Improvement","Improve the regulatory framework for roads to achieve better compliance, seamless connectivity, road safety and quality.",""],[1,"83","8","Road Network Expansion","Increase connectivity by expanding the road network",""],[1,"83","10","Bharatmala Pariyojana Phase-I Highway Development","Bharatmala Pariyojana Phase-I: complete 24,800-km by 2021-22.",""],[1,"83","11","Special Accelerated Road Development Programme for the North-Eastern Region, Phase A","Special Accelerated Road Development Programme for the North-Eastern region (SARDP-NE), Phase 'A': improve about 4,099 km in the North-East.",""],[1,"83","12","North-East Road Network Connectivity Project Phase I","'North-East Road Network Connectivity Project Phase I': improve infrastructure in Meghalaya and Mizoram and enhance connectivity with inter-state roads and international borders.",""],[1,"83","13","Chardham Highway Development Project","o Chardham Mahamarg Vikas Pariyojna.",""],[1,"85","10","PMGSY Phase-I Completion","Phase-I of PMGSY should be completed by March 2019.",""],[1,"85","10","LWE Road Programme Completion","The total length under the LWE (Left Wing Extremism) programme of 5400 km must be completed by March 2020.",""],[1,"85","11","Last-Mile Connectivity Development","Beyond 2020, we should focus on building last mile connectivity.",""]],"40":[[1,"86","2","Railway Infrastructure Capacity Augmentation","Augment the capacity of existing railway infrastructure.",""],[1,"87","6","Rail Infrastructure Investment Scale-Up","The government has recognized the need for additional investment in rail infrastructure and scaled up investment by almost three times, from INR 53,989 crore in 2013-14 to INR 1.47 lakh crore18 in 2018-19 (BE).",""]],"41":[[1,"91","1","Affordable Domestic Air Travel Expansion","Enhance the affordability of flying to enable an increase in domestic ticket sales from 103.75 million in 2016-171 to 300 million by 2022.2",""],[1,"91","4","Airport Capacity Expansion Programme","Expand airport capacity more than five times to handle one billion trips a year.",""],[1,"91","5","Regional Air Connectivity Expansion and Airport Upgrading Programme","Enhance availability and affordability of regional air connectivity and revive/upgrade 56 unserved airports and 31 unserved helipads",""],[1,"92","5","Regional Air Connectivity Scheme (UDAN)","The Ministry of Civil Aviation's regional connectivity scheme, UDAN, is a 10-year scheme, which will promote balanced regional growth and make flying affordable for the population.","Ministry of Civil Aviation"],[1,"93","11","Aviation Infrastructure Enhancement","1. Enhance aviation infrastructure",""],[1,"93","12","UDAN Airport Completion and Revival Programme","Complete the planned airports under the UDAN initiative in a time-bound manner.",""],[1,"93","13","Airport Capacity Expansion Programme","In addition to completing two new airports for Delhi and Mumbai by 2022, the infrastructure capacity in the 10 biggest airports (in terms of traffic) should be significantly augmented.",""],[1,"94","1","Metro Airport Aircraft Parking Infrastructure Upgrade","Increase aircraft parking infrastructure and facilities at metro airports.",""],[1,"94","2","Additional Parking Hubs for Aircraft","Create additional parking hubs at suitable locations, accessible through short haul flights, to accommodate additional aircraft.",""]],"42":[[1,"96","5","Inland Water Transport Capacity Augmentation","Augment the capacity of inland water transport by increasing the least available depth.",""],[1,"98","1","Inland Waterways Infrastructure Development and Maintenance","The Inland Waterways Authority of India (IWAI) is mandated to develop and maintain infrastructure for fairway, navigational aids and terminals.","Inland Waterways Authority of India (IWAI)"],[1,"98","1","Private Investment Facilitation for Inland Cargo Vessels and Services","The IWAI also provides an enabling environment for private investment in cargo vessels and operational services.","Inland Waterways Authority of India (IWAI)"],[1,"98","1","NW-L Capacity Augmentation under Jal Marg Vikas Project","The ministry is augmenting the capacity of NW-l under the Jal Marg Vikas project.",""],[1,"98","1","Central Road Fund Financing for Inland Waterways","The government is also proposing to fund NWs through the Central Road Fund (CRF).","Ministry of Finance"],[1,"99","13","Last-Mile Inland Waterway Connectivity Enhancement","5. Enhance last mile connectivity to inland waterways",""],[1,"99","14","Inland Water Transport Multimodal Connectivity Integration","IWT should be integrated to multimodal/ intermodal connectivity.",""],[1,"99","15","Floating Terminals and Cranes Procurement and Placement","Procure floating terminals and cranes and place them suitably so that access to roads is possible.",""],[1,"100","1","National and State Waterway Linkage Enhancement","Enhance linkages between national waterways and state waterways and feeder canals.",""],[1,"100","2","Inland Vessel Capital Access Facilitation","Facilitate access to capital for inland vessels",""],[1,"100","3","Priority Sector Lending for Inland Vessel Financing","Financing for inland vessels could be made part of priority sector lending by banks.",""],[1,"100","4","Inland Vessels Infrastructure Classification Reform","Categorizing inland vessels as infrastructure equipment will further ease access to capital issues for a sector where capital investments and operational costs are high.",""],[1,"100","5","Viability Gap Funding for Inland Water Transport Infrastructure","Initially, viability gap funding needs to be given at least for 10 years until the infrastructure is fully developed, so that inland water transport is competitive.",""],[1,"100","6","Waiver of Waterway and Lock Charges","We should consider waiving waterway charges and lock charges until operable infrastructure is made available.",""],[1,"100","8","Inland Waterways Technical and Regulatory Reform","Address technical and regulatory constraints in inland waterways to ease movement of inland vessels",""],[1,"100","9","Jal Marg Vikas Project","CCEA, chaired by the Hon'ble Prime Minister approved the implementation of the Jal Marg Vikas project (JMVP) to augment the capacity of National Waterway-1 (NW-1) with technical assistance and investment support from the World Bank at a cost of INR 5369.18 crore.",""],[1,"100","10","Regulation Prohibiting Unjustified Vessel Detention","From a regulatory standpoint, detention of a vessel without a valid reason should not be allowed.",""],[1,"100","11","Inland Vessel Security Directive","A clear directive needs to be issued for security of inland vessels, crew and cargo.",""],[1,"100","12","Inland Water Transport Directorate and Maritime Board Strengthening and Establishment","Strengthen existing Inland Water Transport Directorates or Maritime Boards or set them up in states where they do not exist to ease the IWT business and to ensure efficient regulation and facilitation of IWT for cargo movement.",""]],"43":[[1,"84","1","Metropolitan Urban Transport Authority Establishment","A dedicated Metropolitan Urban Transport Authority in each city with a population of more than 1 million by 2022-23 is needed.",""],[1,"84","2","Dedicated Cells for Integrated Urban Transport Planning","Similarly, set up dedicated cells for integrated planning, coordination and delivery of transport services in smaller cities.",""],[1,"85","1","Public Transport Capacity and Reach Expansion","Increase the capacity and reach of public transport",""],[1,"85","2","State Road Transport Undertaking Transformation and Public Transport Promotion","Transform state road transport undertakings (SRTUs) and promote public transport, rural transport and last mile connectivity.",""],[1,"85","3","Public Transport Funding and Interoperable Systems Expansion","Additional funding for public transportation and the creation of interoperable systems will help expand the reach and capacity of public transport.",""],[1,"85","4","Bus Port Development and Transport Software Support","The central government will work with states to develop bus ports and provide support on technologies/software such as VAHAN (for vehicle registration) and Saarthi (for driving licences).",""],[1,"85","13","Multimodal Urban Mobility Improvement","Urban mobility must move towards multimodal solutions by ensuring seamless movement between different modes.",""]],"44":[[1,"77","5","Emission Intensity Reduction Initiative","Continue to reduce emission intensity of GDP in a manner that will help India achieve the intended nationally determined contribution (INDC) target of 2030.",""],[1,"80","5","Solar Pump Promotion for Agriculture","Promote the use of solar pumps for agriculture.",""],[1,"80","8","Cross-Border Electricity Trade Promotion","Actively promote cross-border electricity trade to utilize existing/upcoming generation assets.",""],[1,"81","2","Cost-Effective Power Grid Balancing Mechanism","Provide a mechanism for cost-effective power grid balancing (gas-based, hydro or storage).",""],[1,"81","3","Renewable Purchase Obligation Enforcement and Inter-State Renewable Energy Trading","Renewable purchase obligations (RPO) should be strictly enforced and inter-state sale of renewable energy should be facilitated.",""],[1,"81","4","National Power Market and Balancing Regulation Mechanism","It is necessary to have national level markets and regulations for balancing of power.",""],[1,"81","4","System-Wide Cost Socialization for Inter-State Transmission Balancing","Central level agencies like Central Electricity Regulatory Commission or National Load Despatch Centre should socialize the costs of balancing of inter- state transmission systems (ISTS) connected power plants, over the entire system, on the lines of the point of connection (PoC) or a similar mechanism.",""],[1,"81","6","Hybrid Renewable Energy Systems Exploration","Hybrid renewable energy systems such as solar PV + biomass should be explored.",""],[1,"81","16","Public Transport Electrification Programme","Public transport systems may be converted to electric in a time bound manner.",""],[1,"81","16","Expansion of Corporate Average Fuel Efficiency Standards","Expand the corporate average fuel efficiency standards (CAFE) beyond passenger cars to other vehicle segments.",""]],"45":[[1,"120","11","Farm Forestry Promotion","Encouraging Farm Forestry.",""],[1,"123","5","Aggressive Afforestation through Joint Forest Management","Afforestation should be promoted aggressively through joint forest management (peoples' participation) and the involvement of the private sector.",""],[1,"123","5","Private Sector Leasing of Denuded Forests and Wastelands for Afforestation","Highly denuded forests and wastelands in the country could be leased out to the private sector for specified periods for afforestation.",""],[1,"123","5","Community Participation in Forest-Based Afforestation","Participation of people, particularly those dependent on forests for their livelihood, may also be encouraged along with the private sector.",""],[1,"123","6","Public Land Greening and Forest Restocking Initiative","Public land available along railway tracks, highways, canals, etc., should be used for greening India.",""],[1,"123","7","Agro-forestry Promotion and Tree Transit Permit Exemption","We should tap the huge scope that exists in agro-forestry.",""],[1,"123","8","Geo-Tagging System for Wood Origin Verification","geo tagging should be used to verify the origin of wood and wood-based products to identify species extracted from farm forestry.",""],[1,"123","11","Urban Green Space Conversion Initiative","Undertake measures to convert vacant spaces in urban areas into urban green areas.",""]],"46":[[1,"40","6","Replication of the GPCB Environmental Audit Scheme","Replicate in other states the Gujarat Pollution Control Board (GPCB) Environmental Audit Scheme based on third party certification.","Gujarat Pollution Control Board (GPCB)"]],"47":[[1,"32","3","National R&D Investment Target","India should aim to spend at least 2 per cent of gross domestic product (GDP) on R&D with equal contributions from the public and private sector.",""],[1,"32","7","Basic Research Promotion","Department of Science and Technology established. Promotes basic research via:","Department of Science and Technology"],[1,"32","8","Research Funding Schemes","Research funding schemes through Science and Engineering Research Board (SERB) and other in-house programmes",""],[1,"34","6","National Science Governance Body","An empowered body is needed to steer holistically the management of science in the country.",""],[1,"34","7","Inter-Ministerial and Inter-Disciplinary Research Body","proposed body will help in pursuing inter- ministerial, inter-disciplinary research besides breaking silos among various scientific departments/agencies.",""],[1,"35","10","International Research Collaboration for Emerging Basic Sciences","Foreign collaborators, consultants, visiting faculty, adjunct scientists, etc., need to be involved in pursuing R&D in the emerging areas of basic sciences such as nano-technology, stem cell research, astronomy, genetics, next generation genomics, drug discovery, etc.","DST | Indian Missions abroad"]],"48":[[1,"189","2","Connectivity and Financial Inclusion Platform for the North Eastern Region","Have adequate road, rail and air connectivity, waterways, internet connectivity and financial inclusion.",""],[1,"192","6","North East Region Scheme Dissemination Strategy","A targeted strategy needs to be devised, in consultation with representatives from all eight NE states, to disseminate information on the various central government schemes that are already in place for the development of the NER.",""],[1,"192","6","North East Region Budget Spending Modalities and Fund Acknowledgement","All central ministries and departments should consider sharing their targets and vision for the NER and spell out modalities for spending the stipulated 10 per cent of their budget for the NER.",""],[1,"192","6","NLCPR Fund Availability Acknowledgement","The Ministry of Finance should formally acknowledge the availability of funds under the NLCPR.","The Ministry of Finance"],[1,"192","7","State Development Blueprint Preparation","Each state within the NER may be encouraged to draw up their development blueprint in consultation with the NITI Aayog and the North-East Council (NEC).",""],[1,"192","8","North-Eastern Region Best Practices Documentation and Dissemination","The Ministry of Development of North-Eastern Region (MDoNER) should document such best practices and disseminate its findings within the region so that the learning can be implemented suitably in other states.","Ministry of Development of North-Eastern Region (MDoNER)"],[1,"192","12","Regional Multi-Modal Transit Agreement for the NER","India could consider initiating a regional multi-modal transit agreement between the NER and the four neighbouring countries.",""],[1,"192","14","Agartala-Akhaura Rail Project","One of the projects that will boost connectivity within India and significantly benefit the NER is the Agartala-Akhaura rail project.","Ministry of Railways"],[1,"192","15","UDAN III Launch","UDAN III may be launched.",""],[1,"193","1","UDAN III Viability Gap Funding Support","The viability gap funding (VGF) required for UDAN III could come from the Government of Assam or could be met from the NLCPR.",""],[1,"193","2","North-East Industrial Development Scheme","On March 21, 2018, the Union Cabinet approved the North-East Industrial Development Scheme (NEIDS) with a project outlay of INR 3,000 crore up to March 2020, to incentivize new industrial units in manufacturing and services sector in the region.",""],[1,"193","4","Industrial Estates and Parks Development","Set up industrial estates/parks in the region.",""],[1,"193","7","Regional Skill Development Acceleration","Accelerate skill development as suitable for the region.",""],[1,"193","8","Attractive Rehabilitation and Resettlement Packages for Hydropower Projects","Attractive R&R packages should be devised for hydropower projects in the region.",""],[1,"193","9","Eco-Tourism and Adventure Tourism Promotion","Tourism, particularly eco-tourism and adventure tourism, should be promoted by identifying suitable sites and creating supporting infrastructure at these sites through the PPP mode.",""],[1,"193","10","Accelerated Completion of Ongoing Irrigation Projects","Early completion of ongoing irrigation projects, particularly Borolia, Dhansiri and Champavati in Assam, and Thoubal and Dolaithabi Barrage in Manipur under the Accelerated Irrigation Benefits Programme, should be accorded high priority.",""],[1,"193","10","North East Water Management Authority","It is expected that the establishment of the North East Water Management Authority will help address the issue.",""]],"49":[[1,"19","6","Government Data Systems and Real-Time Analytics Reform","The government will revamp its data systems and analysis so that all policy interventions and decision-making are based on evidence and real-time data.",""],[1,"28","3","Quarterly Public Data Dissemination System","Disseminate publicly available data, collected through rigorous household and enterprise surveys and innovative use of administrative data on a quarterly basis by 2022-23.",""],[1,"29","6","Employment Data Improvement and Regular Release Initiative","With MOSPI collecting employment data through its enterprises and household surveys - particularly the Periodic Labour Force Survey - and the focus on improving payroll data, the effort is to vastly improve availability of reliable employment data and release it on a regular basis.",""],[1,"30","15","Employment Data Collection Improvement","Improve data collection on employment",""],[1,"30","16","Periodic Labour Force Survey Completion and Data Dissemination","Ensure that data collection for the Periodic Labour Force Survey (PFLS) of households initiated in April 2017 is completed as per schedule and data disseminated by 2019.",""],[1,"30","17","Annual Enterprise Survey Using GSTN Sample Frame","Conduct an annual enterprise survey using the goods and service tax network (GSTN) as the sample frame.",""],[1,"30","18","Administrative Employment Data Tracking System","Increase the use of administrative data viz. EPFO, ESIC and the NPS to track regularly the state of employment while adjusting for the formalization of the workforce.",""],[1,"38","2","Project Monitoring Portal","Set up a portal to monitor projects beyond a given threshold so that any roadblocks are identified and addressed on a real time basis.",""],[1,"38","2","Inter-Ministerial Project Coordination Body","An inter-ministerial body with representatives of state governments and project promoters (as special invitees) may be constituted.",""],[1,"211","1","Evidence-Based Policy Making Integration","Evidence based policy making should be made integral to the overall governance structure in New India, 2022-23.",""],[1,"211","1","Timely Data Generation and Dissemination System","timely generation and dissemination of robust data at all levels of governance would be a pre-requisite.",""],[1,"211","2","Data Collection Using Latest Technologies","Collecting data for new measurable parameters using latest technologies.",""],[1,"211","3","Government Data Collection Efficiency Improvement","Improving efficiencies in processes related to existing data collection by government departments and agencies.",""],[1,"211","4","Data Warehousing Expansion","Expanding warehousing facilities for storing and integrating data from different sources.",""],[1,"211","5","Open Data Access for Industry and Research Stakeholders","Making data available for industry practitioners, academicians, researchers, etc., wherever feasible.",""],[1,"211","6","Integration of Data Analysis and Interactive Data Visualization in Policy Formulation","Integrating data analysis and interactive data visualization into all policy formulation.",""],[1,"212","5","Streamlined Data Collection and Reporting Mechanism","It will be a huge challenge to get all these stakeholders on board for a streamlined data collection and reporting mechanism as envisaged for 2022-23.",""],[1,"212","9","Grassroots Technology Adoption and Local Functionary Skills Development","Enabling adoption of the latest technology at the grassroots level would involve substantial investment along with skill development of local functionaries.",""],[1,"212","10","Technology Integration for Ground-Level Data Aggregation","planning will be required to integrate different technologies so that ground level data can be aggregated.",""],[1,"213","6","Sector-Specific Data-Led Governance Platform","Data Led Governance Platform (Sector Specific) State specific customized platform in local language Captures sector specific variations in the state of interest",""],[1,"213","8","Real-Time Digital Data Collection Across Sectors","Both administrative and survey data need to be collected in digital formats across various sectors in real time to move from paper based to digitally driven operations.",""],[1,"213","8","Adoption of Digital Survey Technologies","This would require the adoption of latest technologies that require recording in digital format, geo-tagging etc.",""],[1,"213","9","National Data Analytics Portal","NITI Aayog is already engaged in developing a National Data Analytics Portal, which is envisioned as a central repository for real-time data across different sectors for all states/UTs.","NITI Aayog"],[1,"213","10","Real-Time Data Sharing Through APIs","Enable data sharing in real time through Application Programming Interfaces (API)",""],[1,"213","14","Statistics System Reform","Necessary reform of our statistics and",""],[1,"214","2","Technology-Enabled Evidence-Based Policymaking Measures","Measures to leverage technology for informed policymaking will be implemented in a time bound manner and closely monitored for desired results.",""],[1,"214","5","Government Data Science Capacity Strengthening Roadmap","A roadmap for strengthening various government agencies including MoS&PI needs to be formulated and implemented in a time bound manner.","MoS&PI"],[1,"214","5","Government-Wide Re-skilling Programme","Re-skilling needs to be promoted across government agencies, both at the state level and at the centre.",""]],"50":[[1,"28","1","Codification of Central Labour Laws into Four Codes","Complete codification of central labour laws into four codes by 2019.",""],[1,"28","4","Labour Market Formalization and Labour Law Reform","Encourage increased formalization of the labour force by reforming labour laws, easing of industrial relations and ensuring of fair wages, working conditions and social security through significant productivity improvements in the economy.",""],[1,"28","10","Labour Compliance Simplification and Rationalization","the central government has recently introduced policies to make compliance easier and more effective.",""],[1,"28","10","Labour Law Simplification and Rationalization","They are also simplifying and rationalizing the large and often overlapping",""],[1,"29","3","Labour Law Rationalization and Online Compliance Reform","These measures include moving licensing and compliance processes online, simplifying procedures and permitting self-certification in larger number of areas.",""],[1,"30","8","Labour Law Codification Reform","Complete the codification of labour laws at the earliest.",""],[1,"30","9","Formal Sector Labour Law Simplification and Reform","Simplify and modify labour laws applicable to the formal sector to introduce an optimum combination of flexibility and security.",""],[1,"31","1","Industrial Relations Formalization Reform","Ease industrial relations to encourage formalization",""]],"52":[[1,"41","7","Pradhan Mantri Krishi Sinchai Yojana","Pradhan Mantri Krishi Sinchai Yojana (PMKSY) aims to expand irrigation coverage whilst promoting water use efficiency.",""],[1,"42","10","Micro-Irrigation Expansion for Irrigation Coverage","The focus should be on increasing coverage through micro- irrigation.",""],[1,"43","7","Micro-Irrigation Investment Subsidy Scheme","Investment subsidies for micro-irrigation: Rather than power and water subsidies, investment subsidies for micro-irrigation can be provided through the DBT mode.",""],[1,"44","2","Efficient Agricultural Water Use Programme","Therefore, more efficient irrigation technologies, water harvesting and better crop selection must be encouraged.",""],[1,"50","1","Precision Agriculture Technology Support","Focus on precision agriculture: Support research on energy friendly irrigation pumps, micro irrigation, climate smart technologies, internet of things (IoT), and use of technology in animal husbandry to monitor animal behaviour, health and production to prepare for future challenges.",""],[1,"116","3","Universal Farm Irrigation and Water-Use Efficiency Programme","Provide irrigation to all farms (Har Khet Ko Pani) with improved on-farm water-use efficiency (more crop per drop).",""],[1,"117","3","Pradhan Mantri Krishi Sinchayee Yojana Irrigation Project Completion","The scheme, Pradhan Mantri Krishi Sinchayee Yojana (PMKSY), which is an umbrella scheme for irrigation has prioritized 99 major and medium irrigation projects for completion by December 2019.",""],[1,"118","1","PMKSY Field-Level Coordination Mechanism","A coordination mechanism at the field level may be set up for PMKSY to find the reasons for delays in the completion of projects and corrective measures undertaken project wise to ensure speedy implementation.",""],[1,"118","2","Command Area Development Works Completion Action Plan","The Ministry of Water Resources (MoWR) may draw up an action plan to complete CAD works in 317 identified projects to reduce the gap between the irrigation potential created and utilized.","Ministry of Water Resources (MoWR)"],[1,"118","16","PMKSY - Har Khet Ko Pani Irrigation Expansion","PMKSY - Har Khet Ko Pani - envisaging enhancement of food production more than two-fold in 96 prioritized most 'deprived irrigation districts' in 12 states by creating",""],[1,"119","1","Expansion of Irrigation Facilities in Tribal and Backward Areas","irrigation facilities through tube wells, dug wells, bore wells and dug-cum-bore wells, should be expedited.",""],[1,"119","4","Watershed Development and Micro-Irrigation Expansion","The MoWR may develop specific strategies to tap water through watershed development (check dams) in rain-fed areas, expand micro irrigation coverage to 80 lakh ha, and link ground water development to aquifer mapping.","MoWR"],[1,"119","6","Public-Private Partnerships for Micro-Irrigation CAD Works","Introduce public-private partnerships in the water sector, initially to develop micro- irrigation-based CAD works based on a hybrid annuity model.",""]],"53":[[1,"129","13","Teacher Regulation Enforcement Mechanism","State governments should develop and formulate robust mechanisms to enforce regulations on teacher qualifications, teacher absenteeism and learning outcomes.",""],[1,"137","2","Teacher Eligibility Testing and Induction Standards","Enforcing minimum teacher standards through rigorous teacher eligibility tests and criteria for the induction of teachers.",""],[1,"137","3","In-Service Teacher Training System Improvement","Improving in-service teacher training system.",""],[1,"137","4","Teacher Accountability for Learning Outcomes","Increasing teacher accountability for learning outcomes of students.",""],[1,"138","11","Institution Recognition Criteria Development Committee","A committee should be set up to develop transparent/objective and rigorous criteria to recognize institutions.",""],[1,"138","12","Teacher Education Institution Accreditation and Closure Reform","the accreditation system developed should ensure the closure of fraudulent or dysfunctional teacher education institutions.",""],[1,"138","13","Teacher Training Institutions of Eminence","Five to six teacher training institutions of eminence with an annual intake of 2000 students each need to be established.",""],[1,"138","14","In-Service Teacher Professional Development Reform","In-service teacher professional development programmes should be redesigned with continuous progressive development through different modes such as early tenure coaching, peer-learning, resource centres, demonstration classes, sabbaticals for research/advanced studies, seminars and visits to other institutions.",""],[1,"138","15","Pt. Madan Mohan Malviya National Mission for Teachers and Teaching","The Pt. Madan Mohan Malviya National Mission for Teachers & Teaching, which seeks to \"build a strong professional cadre of teachers by setting performance standards and creating top",""],[1,"139","1","Teacher Professional Development Mission","class institutional facilities for the professional development of teachers\"6, should be taken up in mission mode.",""],[1,"139","2","National Electronic Teacher Registry","A national electronic teacher registry should be set up as part of the National Education Registry that has been proposed in the section on school education.",""],[1,"139","3","Teacher Performance Monitoring and Salary Incentive Reform","Universal monitoring of teachers' competencies should be done using PINDICS or any such state developed tool on an annual basis and uploaded on the National Electronic Teacher Registry.",""],[1,"139","4","Tri-Annual Teacher Competency Testing","States should test teachers tri-annually on the same test designed for the children they are teaching.",""],[1,"139","5","Teacher Eligibility Test Strengthening and Standardization","The Teacher Eligibility Test (TET) accross states should be strenthened as per central TET: standardization of results, quality benchmarking of testing-items and extending the TET for teachers at pre-school and classes 9-12 levels.",""],[1,"139","7","Teacher Demand Forecasting and Training Capacity Planning","Each state must develop a teacher-demand forecast model for all levels, starting from elementary to higher education.",""]],"54":[[1,"19","7","Implementation of Second Administrative Reforms Commission Recommendations","Implementing the recommendations of the Second Administrative Reforms Commission as a prelude to appointing a successor for designing reforms in the changing context of emerging technologies and growing complexity of the economy.",""],[1,"19","8","Arbitration Council of India","A new autonomous body, viz., the Arbitration Council of India, may be set up to grade arbitral institutions and accredit arbitrators to make the arbitration process cost effective and speedy, and to pre- empt the need for court intervention.",""],[1,"194","2","Legal and Judicial Reform","Legal and judicial reforms are urgently needed to address the massive pendency and capacity issues in Indian courts, which impede access to justice.",""],[1,"194","2","Police and Legal-Judicial Reform Linkage","A part of police reform is intrinsically linked to legal/judicial reform, which would result in efficient criminal justice dispensation.",""],[1,"194","7","Repository of Central and State Laws, Rules and Regulations","Create a repository of all existing central and state laws, rules and regulations",""],[1,"194","8","Legal and Regulatory Repository Development","The centre and state(s) need to create repositories of laws, rules, regulations and government orders.",""],[1,"195","1","Legal Deregulation Initiative","Repeal redundant laws and introduce a new initiative to remove restrictive clauses in existing laws",""],[1,"195","3","Regulatory Simplification Programme","A new programme to repeal unnecessarily restrictive clauses and procedures in existing laws should be started.",""],[1,"195","5","Procedural Law Reform for Commercial Disputes","Introduce changes to procedural laws in line with the principles and thinking behind the Commercial Division Bill.",""],[1,"195","6","Review of the Code of Civil Procedure","To begin with, a review of the Code of Civil Procedure (CPC), 1908, may be considered.",""],[1,"195","7","Pre-Institution Mediation and Settlement Amendment","The Commercial Court, Commercial Division and Commercial Appellate Division of High Courts Act, 2015, needs to be amended to provide for pre- institution mediation and settlement by using the services of agencies created under the Legal Services Authorities Act.",""],[1,"195","8","Decriminalization of Minor Offences and Compounding Reform","Reduce the criminalization of violations, and move towards compounding of minor offences:",""],[1,"195","9","Reduction of Under-Trial Waiting Time","The under-trial waiting time needs to be drastically reduced.",""],[1,"195","9","Expansion of Community Service and Non-Imprisonment Punishments","It is also necessary to move towards community service and other non-imprisonment based punishments.",""],[1,"195","10","Criminal Procedure Reform for Time-Bound Case Resolution","It is necessary to re-examine the procedure for initiating criminal proceedings, arrest and bail.",""],[1,"195","11","Forensics and Ballistics Testing Outsourcing Reform","Reform forensics and ballistics testing by outsourcing to accredited laboratories.",""],[1,"195","13","School-Level Rule of Law Education Programmes","The process should start at the school level and can be effected by mandatorily introducing innovative programmes with well thought out content and activities.",""],[1,"195","14","Incentive and Sanction-Based Legal Compliance Model","Introduce incentive and sanction-based models of motivation to ensure that citizens abide by the law.",""],[1,"195","15","Prohibitive Penalties for Civic and Traffic Violations","Prohibitive penalties should be imposed to check traffic violations, civic violations including littering in public, first time petty offenders, etc.",""],[1,"196","2","Legislative Amendment Timeframe and Sunset Clause Reform","A time line for implementation of necessary amendments should be stipulated.",""],[1,"196","3","Mandatory Continuing Legal Education","Continuing legal education in selected areas should be made mandatory for lawyers and judges",""],[1,"196","3","Professional Conduct and Ethics Rules for Legal Professionals","rules of professional conduct and ethics need to be drawn up and implemented",""],[1,"196","4","Government Official Sensitization Programme","This will require an attitudinal reorientation among government officials through sensitization programmes.",""],[1,"196","5","Plain-Language Drafting of New Laws","New laws should be drafted in simple, plain language.",""],[1,"196","7","Commercial Courts Workload Diversion","Shift certain sections of the workload out of the regular court system to commercial courts,",""],[1,"196","8","Specialized Court Divisions for Case Decongestion","the commercial division and the commercial appellate division of High Courts for commercial disputes and the Criminal Judicial Magistrate for criminal cases at least in metropolitan areas to decongest courts.",""],[1,"196","10","Arbitration and Conciliation Act Amendment","The Arbitration and Conciliation Act, 1996, should be amended to make India a robust centre for institutional arbitration, both domestic and international.",""],[1,"196","10","Arbitration Council of India Establishment","A new autonomous body, viz., the Arbitration Council of India, should be set up to grade arbitral institutions and accredit arbitrators to make the arbitration process cost effective and speedy, and to pre-empt the need for court intervention.",""],[1,"196","11","Tribunal Rationalization and Appointment Streamlining Reform","Merge and rationalize tribunals to enhance efficiency.","Department of Personnel and Training (DoPT)"],[1,"197","2","Continuing Training for Skills and Ethics Development","Continuing training may be introduced to ensure development of skills, ethics, knowledge and awareness of international best practices.",""],[1,"197","4","E-Platform Live-Streamed Training Modules","Training modules should be live streamed on an e-platform to make information easily accessible, and widely disseminated.",""],[1,"197","5","Judicial Performance Index and State Justice Access Index","Consider a performance index for judges and a separate state wise index for ease of getting justice.",""],[1,"197","6","Administrative Cadre in the Judicial System","Introduce an administrative cadre in the judicial system to streamline processes.",""],[1,"197","7","Court Process Automation and Electronic Case Management","Prioritize court process automation and ICT enablement for electronic court and case management, including electronic management of court schedules and migration of all courts to the unified national court application software.",""],[1,"197","8","Video Conferencing Facilities for Access to Justice","Facilitate the availability and usage of video- conferencing facilities to assist in speedy access to justice and to minimize logistical issues.",""]],"55":[[1,"199","1","Civil Service Recruitment, Training, and Performance Evaluation Reform","To put in place a reformed system of recruitment, training and performance evaluation of the civil service to ensure more effective and efficient delivery of public services to achieve the development goals envisaged in New India 2022.",""],[1,"199","2","Institutional Mechanism to Monitor Accepted ARC Recommendations","Decisions on the accepted recommendations have been sent to the relevant central ministries and state/union territories, with a request to set up an institutional mechanism to monitor their implementation.",""],[1,"199","3","Civil Service Reform and Modernization Measures","These include, the introduction of a multi-stakeholder feedback (MSF) performance evaluation, dispensing with interviews for lower level positions, introduction of online mechanisms for appraisals and filing of various returns by employees, implementation of e-office, and strengthening training and merit-based postings.",""],[1,"199","9","Implementation of Accepted Second ARC Recommendations","The strategy for 2022-23 should be centred on the implementation of the Second ARC recommendations that have been accepted by",""],[1,"200","2","Officer-Oriented Culture and Cadre Expansion","Improve the teeth to tail ratio: Promote an officer-oriented culture and focus on expanding the numbers of officers.",""],[1,"200","3","Objective Recruitment and Placement Reform","Objectivity in the recruitment and placement process: Widely disseminate job descriptions and selection criterion and eliminate elements of arbitrariness.",""],[1,"200","4","Civil Services Rationalization and Central Talent Pool","The existing 60 plus separate civil services at the central and state level needs to be reduced through rationalization and harmonization of services.",""],[1,"200","5","Lateral Entry of Specialists into Government","Encourage lateral entry: Inducting specialists at higher levels of government will provide much needed expertise.",""],[1,"200","6","Civil Service Specialization and Mobility Reform","The key to reform in the civil services is encouraging officers to cultivate specializations based on their education and skills early on in their careers.",""],[1,"200","7","Officer Mentorship and Soft-Skills Support Programme","Upon induction, young officers should be assigned mentors, preferably with an officer having a similar functional specialization or with high-quality NGOs for values and soft- skill mentorship.",""],[1,"200","8","Information Technology Upscaling for Planning and Staffing Forecasting","Use of IT needs to be significantly upscaled for planning, forecasting staffing requirements and recruitments.",""],[1,"200","9","Civil Service Hiring Policy Reform","The upper age limit for the civil services should be brought down to 27 years for the general category in a phased manner by 2022-23.",""],[1,"200","9","Autonomous Body Employment Conditions Harmonization","Service conditions for employees of autonomous bodies need to be regulated and harmonized.",""],[1,"200","12","Training System Reorientation for Job Outcomes and Urban Management","Alter the current system of training to meet job-outcome oriented goals.",""],[1,"200","13","Mid-Career Training Modules for All Services","Introduce mid-career training modules for all services.",""],[1,"201","1","Online Training Platform Expansion","Strengthen and leverage online avenues for training",""],[1,"201","2","Pre- and Post-Training Skills Matching for Postings","Introduce pre and post-training matching of skills to determine postings.",""],[1,"201","4","Competency Matrix for Skills Monitoring and Matching","Develop a competency matrix to monitor ongoing skill acquisition and help match requirements with resources in real time.",""],[1,"201","5","E-Learning Training Platform","Institute an e-learning platform to conduct training modules.",""],[1,"201","6","Mid-Career Examination and Skill Assessment for Future Postings","Mid-career exams/skill assessment might be undertaken to evaluate and decide on future postings.",""],[1,"201","7","Skill Orientation Handbook Preparation","Prepare handbooks for skill orientation to improve competency.",""],[1,"201","8","Living University Concept","Introduce the 'living university' concept of value creation based on outcomes and good ideals.",""],[1,"201","9","District-Based Training and Immersion Modules","Develop ongoing training and immersion modules on a district-by-district basis.",""],[1,"201","10","Multi-Stakeholder Feedback System for Performance Appraisal","Consider replacing annual confidential reports (ACRs) with multi stake holder feedback (MSF): ACRs could be replaced with MSF.",""],[1,"201","11","Smart Performance Appraisal Reporting System Rollout","Institute the online Smart Performance Appraisal Report Recording Online Window (SPARROW) template in all central and state cadres.",""],[1,"201","12","Performance Incentive Scheme Review and Expansion","Incentivization: Review existing schemes and introduce new schemes of incentives for extraordinary performance.",""],[1,"201","13","Compulsory Retirement for Underperforming Officers","Develop benchmarks to assess the performance of officers and compulsorily retire those deemed unable to meet the benchmarks.",""],[1,"201","17","Civil Servant Protection and Due Process Safeguards","Protection of civil servants: Introduce an appropriate system of checks and balances, including for the process of suspension, to ensure that officers are given their due process and are not vulnerable to vested interests and political pressures.",""],[1,"202","3","Recruitment, Placement and Training Transparency Initiative","Improving transparency in placement through initiatives in recruitment, placement and training.",""]],"56":[[1,"201","3","Digitization of Human Resource Records Across States","Digitize human resource records across states.",""],[1,"201","14","Citizen-Centric Policy Framework Development","An inclusive policy framework with citizens at the centre needs to be developed.",""],[1,"201","14","ICT and RTI-Based Public Information Access Expansion","Apart from improving public access to information through the use of Information and Communication Technology (ICT) and the Right to Information Act (RTI), the RTI's management information system portal needs to be expanded to cover more public authorities, especially subordinate offices of ministries and public sector units.",""],[1,"201","15","Monitoring System for Suo Moto Disclosures","Institutionalize system for effective monitoring of suo moto disclosures",""],[1,"201","16","Capacity Building for Public Information Authorities","Enhance capability of public authorities: The capabilities and knowledge base of central public information officers (CPIOs), appellate authorities (AAs) and information commissions need to be upgraded on a continuous basis to enable them to perform their assigned roles without external influence.",""],[1,"201","18","Review of Allocation and Transaction of Business Rules","Every ministry/department should review their AoBR/ ToBR keeping in view present day requirements.",""],[1,"202","1","Anti-Corruption Institutional Strengthening","Ensure probity in governance: Strengthen institutional mechanisms for prevention and detection of corruption:",""],[1,"202","2","Vigilance Manual and Instructions Review","Reviewing existing vigilance operating manuals and instructions to ensure probity.",""],[1,"202","5","Centralized Public Grievance Redressal and Monitoring System Reform Framework","Strengthen implementation of a Centralized Public Grievance Redressal and Monitoring System (CPGRAMs): Develop a reform framework for the top twenty departments for periodic monitoring of grievance receipts.",""],[1,"202","5","Updated CPGRAMS Grievance Transfer and Bulk Disposal Upgrade","An updated version that enables transfer of grievances between ministries/departments, bulk disposal of",""],[1,"202","7","CPGRAMS Grievance Redressal Mechanism Expansion","These initiatives need to be continued with greater vigour and over time; CPGRAMs should emerge as a strong mechanism for efficient redressal of public grievances with similar mechanisms across all states/UTs.",""],[1,"202","8","e-Office Implementation Expansion","Implementation of e-Office may be expedited in all ministries/ departments; all states/UTs may also be encouraged to adopt it.",""],[1,"202","9","Administrative Process Simplification and Single-Window Clearance Expansion","Every department should seek to simplify their processes to cut administrative delays and ensure participatory feedback mechanisms for efficient service delivery.",""],[1,"202","9","Participatory Feedback Mechanisms for Service Delivery","Every department should seek to simplify their processes to cut administrative delays and ensure participatory feedback mechanisms for efficient service delivery.",""],[1,"202","9","IT-Enabled Single-Window Clearance and Policy Consultation System","IT tools need to be expanded for single window clearances and stakeholder consultations in policy.",""],[1,"202","10","e-Office Mission Mode Project","e-Office is a mission mode project under the National e-Governance Project of the government.",""]],"58":[[1,"27","2","North-East Cross-Border Trade Facilitation Infrastructure","Building the physical infrastructure and putting in place measures to facilitate seamless cross-border movement of goods in the North-East region would help accelerate integration and promote exports.",""]],"59":[[1,"5","2","Innovation- and Technology-Driven Policy Formulation and Implementation","The 'Strategy for New India @ 75' put together by NITI Aayog is an attempt to bring innovation, technology, enterprise and efficient management together, at the core of policy formulation and implementation.","NITI Aayog"],[1,"5","2","Public Consultation and Feedback Mechanism for Policy Refinement","It will encourage discussion and debate, and invite feedback for further refining our policy approach.",""],[1,"5","2","Public Participation for Economic Transformation","We believe that economic transformation cannot happen without public participation.",""],[1,"8","2","Flagship Scheme Implementation and New Initiative Design","'Strategy for New India @ 75' has identified 41 different areas that require either a sharper focus on implementing the flagship schemes already in place or a new design and initiative to achieve India's true potential.",""],[1,"8","2","Constraint-Addressing Policy Measures","It then identifies the binding constraints and proposes measures to address these constraints.",""],[1,"8","2","Readily Implementable Measures Inventory","It is our hope that this new approach will provide an inventory of readily implementable measures for the government departments and agencies both in the central and state governments.",""]],"60":[[1,"7","3","Regional Mainstreaming and Balanced Development Initiative","We will have to focus on the necessary modernization of our agriculture and mainstreaming of regions such as the North East, hilly states and the 115 Aspirational Districts.",""],[1,"19","5","Regional Equity Strategy for the North-East and Aspirational Districts Programme","Implementing strategies to achieve regional equity by focusing on the North-East region and successfully rolling out the Aspirational Districts Programme.",""]],"61":[[1,"18","4","Zero Budget Natural Farming Promotion","A strong push would be given to 'Zero Budget Natural Farming' (ZBNF) techniques that reduce costs, improve land quality and increase farmers' incomes.",""],[1,"41","7","Second Cycle of the Soil Health Card Scheme","The second cycle of the Soil Health Card (SHC) scheme is underway, which will focus on job creation and entrepreneurship development through local entrepreneurship models.",""],[1,"43","2","Strengthen Soil Health Card Scheme","Strengthen the SHC scheme and include not merely nine but all sixteen parameters in the tests.",""],[1,"43","2","Ground-Level Soil Health Card Fertilizer Distribution","This will ensure SHC based fertilizer distribution at the ground level.",""],[1,"43","2","Integrate Soil Health Cards with Fertilizer Management System","Seed SHCs with the integrated fertilizer management system.",""],[1,"43","2","Link Soil Health Cards with Kisan Credit Cards","Link SHCs with Kisan credit cards and make SHCs mandatory for subsidies.",""],[1,"43","2","Ensure Proper Functioning of Soil Health Card Laboratories","Ensure proper functioning of the SHC labs.",""],[1,"43","3","Fertilizer Subsidy Reform to Include Secondary and Micronutrients","Reorient fertilizer subsidy policy: The current lopsided fertilizer subsidy policy needs to bring secondary and micronutrients on the same nutrient- based subsidy (NBS) platform as phosphorus (P) and potash (K).",""],[1,"43","6","Targeted Liquid Fertilizer Subsidy for Fertigation","Targeted subsidy should be provided on liquid fertilizers to encourage fertigation with micro-irrigation.",""],[1,"50","8","Nationwide Deployment of Patented Herbal Soil Inputs","these herbal inputs, for which actual performance data is now available for a few thousand farmers, need to be applied across the country.",""]],"62":[[1,"19","3","Atal Tinkering Labs Expansion","including the creation of a new innovation ecosystem at the ground level by establishing at least 10,000 Atal Tinkering Labs by 2020.",""],[1,"33","6","Atal Innovation Mission","The government has set up the Atal Innovation Mission (AIM) to transform radically the innovation, entrepreneurship and start-up ecosystem of the country.",""],[1,"35","5","District Innovation Fund","a non-lapsable \"District Innovation Fund\" with a corpus of about INR 2 crore in each district may be created and used to promote grass root innovations.",""],[1,"35","6","Atal New India Challenges","AIM has already launched Atal New India Challenges in partnership with five ministries to create products from technologies and prototypes in areas of national importance such as solid waste management, water and wastewater management as well as road and",""],[1,"35","8","Atal Tinkering Labs Expansion","AIM has set up over 1000 Atal Tinkering Labs (ATLs) around the country covering over 625 districts.",""],[1,"35","9","Atal Incubation Centre Support for Entrepreneurship and Startups","To promote entrepreneurship and startups, AIM is supporting AICs across the country including at Tier II/III locations.",""],[1,"35","11","Higher Education Innovation and Entrepreneurship Credit Scheme","The Higher Education Commission once set up may consider giving credits for innovation and start-ups and also setting up online entrepreneurial development courses in colleges and universities.",""],[1,"36","4","Start-up India Initiative","the Start-up India initiative to promote entrepreneurship and nurture innovation",""]],"63":[[1,"23","1","Accelerate GDP Growth to About 8 Percent","Steadily accelerate the gross domestic product (GDP) growth rate to achieve a target of about 8 per cent during 2018-23",""],[1,"24","8","Physical Infrastructure Investment","Investment in physical infrastructure will address long-standing deficiencies faced by the economy.",""]],"64":[[1,"24","4","Tax-GDP Ratio Increase and Tax Reform Measures","To enhance public investment, India should aim to increase its tax-GDP ratio to at least 22 per cent of GDP by 2022- 23.",""],[1,"24","4","Direct Tax Rationalization","In addition, efforts need to be made to rationalize direct taxes for both corporate tax and personal income tax.",""],[1,"24","4","Digital Tax Compliance Simplification","Simultaneously, there is a need to ease the tax compliance burden and eliminate direct interface between taxpayers and tax officials using technology.",""],[1,"24","7","State Own-Source Revenue Mobilization and GST Administration Improvement","States could also undertake greater mobilization of own taxes such as property tax, and taking specific steps to improve administration of GST to increase tax collections.",""]],"65":[[1,"25","2","Exit from Non-Strategic Central Public Sector Enterprises","The government should continue to exit central public sector enterprises (CPSEs) that are not strategic in nature.",""],[1,"25","2","Public Stake Dilution in Large CPSEs","For larger CPSEs, the goal should be to create widely held companies by offloading stake to the public to create entities where no single promoter has control.",""],[1,"26","2","Public Sector Bank Governance Reform","Governance reforms in public sector banks require, apart from the establishment of independent and commercially driven bank boards, performance assessment of executives and increased flexibility in human resources policy.",""],[1,"36","4","Public Sector Bank Recapitalisation","it has undertaken massive recapitalisation of public sector banks to ease availability of credit to micro, small and medium enterprises (MSMEs)",""]],"66":[[1,"25","8","Flexible Fiscal Target-Setting under FRBM","the government should be flexible in its approach towards setting annual targets based on prevailing economic conditions.",""],[1,"25","9","Effective Revenue Deficit Reduction and Capital Expenditure Reclassification","The effective revenue deficit should be brought down as rapidly as possible.",""],[1,"25","11","Nominal Exchange Rate Volatility Reduction Policy","Policy should be directed to minimize volatility in the nominal exchange rate.",""]],"67":[[1,"26","8","Power Tariff Rationalization for Industrial Competitiveness","Power tariff structures may be rationalized to ensure global competitiveness of Indian industries.",""],[1,"26","9","Import Tariff and Productivity Support Measures","Import tariffs that seek to promote indigenous industry should come with measures to raise productivity which will provide the ability to compete globally.",""],[1,"26","10","Acceleration of Announced Infrastructure Projects","Improve connectivity by accelerating the completion of announced infrastructure projects.",""],[1,"26","11","Labour and Land Regulatory Easing","Work with states to ease labour and land regulations.",""],[1,"26","11","Fixed-Term Employment Expansion","All state governments should speedily implement fixed term employment (FTE) that has now been extended to cover all sectors.",""],[1,"50","11","Accelerated Growth in Manufacturing, Services, and Exports","India will also have to accelerate growth in the manufacturing, services and exports sectors to wean labour away from agriculture.",""]],"68":[[1,"26","13","Performance-Based Evaluation and Restructuring of Export Promotion Councils","Strengthen the governance and technical capabilities of Export Promotion Councils (EPCs) by subjecting them to a well-defined, performance-based evaluation.",""],[1,"26","14","Regional Economic Integration Initiative","Explore closer economic integration within South Asia and the emerging economies of South East Asia particularly Cambodia, Laos, Myanmar and Vietnam, using the existing Bangladesh, Bhutan, India, Nepal (BBIN) and",""]],"69":[[1,"30","11","National Policy for Domestic Workers","The National Policy for Domestic Workers needs to be brought in at the earliest to recognize their rights and promote better working conditions.",""],[1,"30","12","Enhance Female Labour Force Participation","3. Enhance female labour force participation",""],[1,"30","13","Implementation and Enforcement of Workplace Gender Protection Laws","Ensure the implementation of and employers' adherence to the recently passed Maternity Benefit (Amendment) Act, 2017, and the Sexual Harassment of Women at Work Place (Prevention, Prohibition and Redressal) Act.",""],[1,"30","13","Extension of Workplace Gender Protection Laws to the Informal Sector","It is also important to ensure implementation of these legislations in the informal sector.",""]],"70":[[1,"30","10","Workplace Conditions Compliance Reform","Make the compliance of working conditions regulations more effective and transparent.",""],[1,"31","3","Labour Dispute Resolution System Overhaul","Overhaul the labour dispute resolution system to resolve disputes quickly, efficiently, fairly and at low cost.",""],[1,"31","4","Labour Court and Tribunal Strengthening for Timely Dispute Resolution","Strengthen labour courts/tribunals for timely dispute resolution and set a time frame for different disputes.",""],[1,"31","11","Compulsory Establishment Registration for Workplace Monitoring","Ensure compulsory registration of all establishments to ensure better monitoring of occupational safety as well as recreation and sanitation facilities.",""],[1,"31","12","Online Labour Complaint and Standardized Inspection Mechanism","Enhance transparency in the labour inspection system by allowing online complaints and putting in place a standardized and clear mechanism.",""]],"71":[[1,"31","2","Severance Pay Enhancement","Increase severance pay, in line with global best practices.",""],[1,"31","5","Mandatory National Floor-Level Minimum Wage Compliance","Make compliance with the national floor level minimum wage mandatory.",""],[1,"31","6","Minimum Wages Act Coverage Expansion","Expand the Minimum Wages Act, 1948, to cover all jobs.",""],[1,"31","7","Wage Payment Enforcement Through Digital and Cheque Transfers","Enforce the payment of wages through cheque or Aadhaar-enabled payments for all.",""],[1,"31","9","Comprehensive Occupational Health and Safety Legislation","Enact a comprehensive occupational health and safety legislation based on risk assessment, employer-worker co-operation, and effective educational, remedial and sanctioning.",""],[1,"31","9","On-site Workers Housing Initiative","Workers housing on site will help to improve global competitiveness of Indian industry, along with enhancing workers' welfare.",""],[1,"31","10","Informal Sector Occupational Safety and Health Programme","Enhance occupational safety and health (OSH) in the informal sector through capacity building and targeted programmes.",""]],"72":[[1,"35","1","Domestic Preference in Government Procurement","In all government procurements, international competitive bidding for both products and services should be resorted to only when Indian manufacturers are unable to supply products/services of comparable international quality.",""],[1,"35","2","Quarterly Public Procurement Awareness Workshops","Quarterly workshops may be organised for creating awareness among procurement managers of various ministries/ departments/state governments/CPSUs, about the DIPP's Public Procurement Order 2017",""],[1,"35","3","Expert Inclusion in Government Procurement Committees","To adopt innovative technologies, experts/scientific practitioners should be mandatorily included on board/committees related to government procurement.",""],[1,"35","4","Startup Procurement Preference in Technical Evaluation","In order to promote procurement of goods/ services developed by Indian start-ups, preference in the technical evaluation could be provided to them.",""]],"73":[[1,"38","7","Digitized Electronic Approval Process Reform","Streamline discretionary powers vested at different levels of governance by adopting digitized processes and making all approvals electronic in a transparent, time bound manner.",""],[1,"40","3","Single Window Investor Clearance System","Introduce a \"single window\" system in all states that provides a single point of contact between investor and government and facilitates all required licences and approvals.",""],[1,"40","4","Accountability System for Approval and Inspection Bodies","For efficient approval/inspection process, develop a system of accountability for major stakeholders like inspection bodies, testing labs, etc.",""],[1,"40","5","GIS-Based Pre-Approved Land Bank System for Manufacturing","For geographical planning and ease of environmental clearances, adopt the system of using Geographic Information System (GIS) based maps at all levels to create pre-approved land banks for manufacturing facilities.",""],[1,"40","7","Third-Party Certification Accreditation Agency Development","To strengthen third party certification systems, develop suitable accreditation agencies.",""],[1,"40","8","Integration of Shram Suvidha and State Agency Portals","Ensure the seamless integration of the Shram Suvidha portal and state agencies' portals.",""]],"74":[[1,"38","8","Government-Industry-Academia Coordination for Workforce Skills Alignment","A greater connect between government-industry-academia is required to identify the changing requirements in manufacturing and prepare an employable workforce.",""],[1,"38","8","Review of Engineering Education Standards and Industry Linkages","there is a need for thorough review of standards of engineering education and its linkages with industry.",""]],"75":[[1,"38","10","Harmonization of Indian Quality Standards with Global Standards","Harmonize Indian quality standards with global standards in many sectors.",""],[1,"39","2","Standards and Productivity Assessment for Global Benchmarking","Task the Bureau of Indian Standards and Quality Council of India with assessing the improvements in standards and productivity required to achieve global standards.",""],[1,"55","12","Expansion and Accreditation of Testing Laboratories","Increase the number of testing laboratories: There exists a shortage of testing laboratories, essential for health certificates for exports.",""]],"76":[[1,"42","11","Hybrid and Improved Seed Adoption Initiative","Increase adoption of hybrid and improved seeds: States should take the lead through the following measures:",""],[1,"42","12","Dynamic Seed Development Planning","Dynamic seed development plans are required.",""],[1,"42","14","Variety Replacement and Climate-Resilient Seed Development","Increase Variety Replacement Ratio (VRR): Phase out old varieties of seeds and replace them with hybrid and improved seeds to enhance productivity.",""],[1,"42","15","Seed Testing Facility Upgradation and Performance Monitoring","Strengthen seed testing facilities: Seed testing facilities need upgradation in terms of both personnel and technical expertise.",""],[1,"43","1","Uniform National Seed Licensing Procedure","Uniform national procedure for seed licensing: To tackle the problem of heterogeneity in seed licensing procedures across states, the central government should develop model guidelines for seed licensing and support states in implementing these.",""],[1,"44","5","Vegetable Hybrid Variety Adoption","Shift to using hybrid varieties for vegetables.",""],[1,"44","6","Rootstock Standardization and Promotion for Fruit Production","Measures should be taken to standardize and promote usage of rootstocks to produce fruits.",""]],"77":[[1,"43","4","Farmer Extension Services for Best Practices","Strengthen extension activities to ensure that best practices reach the average farmer.",""],[1,"43","8","ATMA Programme Reorientation for Bottom-Up Planning","The ATMA programme needs to be reoriented to include bottom up planning at the district and block levels to develop Strategic Research Extension Plans (SREP).",""],[1,"43","8","Decentralization and Autonomy for Agricultural Extension","Further decentralization and autonomy are essential to the success of this programme.",""],[1,"43","8","KVK Research Alignment with Block Action Plans","Subject matter specialists at KVKs should orient their research to the block action plans developed by ATMA.",""],[1,"43","9","Public-Private Partnership in Agricultural Extension Delivery","The guiding principles of ATMA provide for the promotion of PPP in extension delivery.",""],[1,"43","10","Market-Led Agricultural Extension Services","Give priority to extension services that disseminate information to farmers regarding (i) crop selection (ii) demand for and supply of crop produce, (iii) expected price of commodity and (iv) availability of infrastructure facilities for storage, transport and marketing of produce.",""],[1,"43","11","Value-Added Agricultural Extension Services","Prioritise value added extension services to enable a reduction in post- harvest losses by converting raw agricultural produce to processed products.",""],[1,"43","12","District-Level Agricultural Skill Mapping and Training Coordination","ICAR and SAUs should map the demand for and supply of skills in agriculture at the district level and coordinate with skill development missions to impart the required skills to farmers and agricultural labour.",""],[1,"43","13","Dealer Training Programme Replication in State Agricultural Universities","Replicate dealer training programme in state agricultural universities:",""],[1,"44","1","Replication of Dealer Training Programme in SAUS","Agricultural Extension Management's (MANAGE) dealer training programme should be replicated in SAUS, with diploma holders granted licences to conduct extension activities.",""],[1,"48","10","Agriculture Advisory Service","An effective and technology driven Agriculture Advisory Service may be considered on the lines of those of the United States Department of Agriculture (USDA) and the European Union (EU).",""],[1,"50","3","Agricultural Knowledge Hub for Best Practice Dissemination","Create a knowledge hub to disseminate best practices:",""],[1,"50","4","Integrated Farming Model Development","Develop models of integrated farming:",""]],"78":[[1,"44","3","High-Value Crop Diversification Incentive Mechanism","Design an incentive mechanism to wean farmers away from cereal crops to HVCs.",""],[1,"44","4","Regional Horticulture Production Belt Development","regional production belts for HVCs need to be identified and supported through the Mission on Integrated Development of Horticulture (MIDH).",""]],"79":[[1,"44","8","Organic Niche Products Market Development","Strengthen market for organic products: Targeted efforts to create a market for niche products is recommended.",""],[1,"44","8","State Spice Branding Initiative","Spices unique to a state can be branded by the Spice Board to encourage the production of organic spices.",""]],"80":[[1,"44","9","Agricultural Waste Recycling and Utilization Initiative","Recycling and utilizing agricultural waste would give a further filip to farmers' income.",""]],"81":[[1,"44","10","Crossbreeding of Indigenous and Exotic Cattle","Breeding of indigenous cattle with exotic breeds needs to be encouraged to arrest the issue of inbreeding.",""],[1,"44","11","Bull Mother Farm Development Programme","Promote and develop bull mother farms: Employing multiple ovulation and embryo transfer technologies, these farms can significantly enhance milk productivity through the supply of cattle with enhanced milk potential to farmers.",""],[1,"44","12","Village-Level Dairy Procurement and Value Chain Support","Installing of bulk milk chillers and facilities for high value conversion of milk are needed to promote dairy in states.",""],[1,"44","12","Private Sector Incentives for Dairy Value Chains","The private sector should be incentivized to create a value chain for HVCs and dairy products at the village level.",""]],"82":[[1,"45","1","Fisheries Scheme Convergence and Aquaculture Cluster Development","Integrate the Blue Revolution scheme with MGNREGA.",""],[1,"45","2","Fish Breeder and Farmer Capacity Building Programme","Capacity building for fish breeders and farmers: Establish fish co-operative organisations and run village level schemes in coordination with panchayats to disseminate best practices and research.",""]],"83":[[1,"48","3","Agricultural Export Policy Framework","the Government of India should come up with a coherent and stable agricultural export policy, ideally with a five to ten-year time horizon and a built-in provision for a mid-term review.",""],[1,"55","4","Railway Freight Operations Strengthening","Railway freight operations should be strengthened through temperature-controlled containers and loading and unloading facilities to reduce post-harvest losses and connect land-locked states to export markets.",""],[1,"56","1","Green Channel Clearance for Perishable Produce","Efforts must be made to setup a green channel for perishable produce at identified airports handling cargo.",""],[1,"56","2","Regulatory Framework for Marine Produce Export Compliance","Regulatory frameworks regarding use of pesticides, growth hormones, and antibiotics for marine produce need to be developed",""],[1,"56","4","Farmer Producer Organization, Export Cluster, and Contract Farming Promotion","Promotion of farmer producer organizations (FPOs), export-based clusters and contract farming will go a long way towards ensuring traceability of farm produce, a key export requirement.",""]],"84":[[1,"48","4","Agricultural Tribunal Replacement Proposal","The government should consider replacing the Commission on Agricultural Costs & Prices (CACP) by an agriculture tribunal in line with the provisions of Article 323 B of the Constitution.",""],[1,"48","4","NITI Aayog Review Group on Agricultural Reform","NITI Aayog should set up a group to examine the following:","NITI Aayog"]],"85":[[1,"48","12","Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana Modification","Crop insurance: PMFBY needs to be modified to -",""],[1,"48","13","Weather-Based Insurance Promotion","Promote weather-based insurance.",""],[1,"48","14","Non-Loanee Farmers' Insurance Coverage Expansion","Increase non-loanee farmers' insurance coverage.",""],[1,"48","15","Mixed Cropping and Crop Notification Expansion","Allow for mixed cropping and increase the number of crops notified.",""]],"86":[[1,"49","6","Promotion of Farmer Producer Organizations","Promote farmer producer organizations (FPOs):",""]],"87":[[1,"53","4","Rural Road Connectivity under PMGSY","connecting habitations through the Pradhan Mantri Gram Sadak Yojana (PMGSY).",""],[1,"53","4","Household Electrification under SAUBHAGYA","household electrification has been given a significant push under the SAUBHAGYA scheme.",""],[1,"53","4","Agriculture Infrastructure Upgradation","Agriculture infrastructure, such as rural markets, warehouses, cold chain, farm machinery hubs and public irrigation need upgradation.",""],[1,"55","8","Revision of Rural Habitat Identification Criteria for Road Connectivity","To ensure better inclusion, the criteria for identification of habitats for rural roads connectivity in hill and left-wing extremism (LWE) affected districts must be revisited.",""],[1,"55","9","Rural Feeder Separation Incentive Scheme","All distribution companies (DISCOMs) need to be incentivized for rural feeder separation.",""],[1,"55","10","Private Farm Implement Mechanization Hubs","Private entrepreneurs should be incentivized to establish small farm implement mechanization hubs for every 1000 ha and big machinery hubs for every 5000 ha of cultivated area.",""]],"88":[[1,"59","5","Comprehensive Financial Literacy Scheme","Launching a new scheme for comprehensive financial literacy",""],[1,"59","6","Arthik Shiksha Abhiyan Financial Literacy Programme","An Arthik Shiksha Abhiyan will help improve financial literacy and may be integrated in the regular school curriculum.",""],[1,"59","6","Financial Literacy Mass Media Campaigns","Besides, efforts to improve financial literacy should be complemented by mass media campaigns to provide information on financial products and their use.",""],[1,"59","7","Banking Correspondent Performance Assessment and Incentive Reform","Assess the performance of banking correspondents and give better incentives",""],[1,"59","8","Bank Correspondent Certification and Training Framework","The issue of inadequate training is being addressed by the RBI which has developed a framework for certification for both basic and advanced levels.",""],[1,"59","8","Improved Monetary Incentives for Banking Correspondents","There is also a need to create better monetary incentives for banking correspondents as well as to provide them better training.",""]],"89":[[1,"59","10","Paperless Banking Reform","Paperless banking will reduce friction, documentation proof requirements and the cost of banking services.",""],[1,"59","11","E-KYC Transaction Limit Relaxation for Deposit and Loan Accounts","Ease transaction limits for e-KYC based deposit and loan accounts.",""],[1,"59","12","Digital Signature and Paperless Loan Account Initiative","Push digital signature for loan accounts by asking public sector banks to carry out at least 25% of their transactions through paperless accounts by 2022-23.",""],[1,"59","13","DigiLocker Service Expansion","Expand digilocker services by including more issuers of documents.",""],[1,"59","14","Technology-Enabled Creditworthiness Assessment","Using technology to improve the assessment of credit-worthiness for households and informal businesses",""],[1,"59","16","Data-Sharing Framework for Credit Access","Create a new data-sharing framework that builds on the success of Jan Dhan and Aadhaar platforms to enable easier access to credit, with adequate safeguards for maintaining data privacy.",""]],"90":[[1,"57","5","Household Asset Diversification through Capital Market Participation","Asset diversification: Allowing diversification of asset portfolio of households through increased participation in capital markets.",""],[1,"60","1","National Cyber Security Framework","A common cyber security framework across different stakeholders should be created.",""],[1,"60","4","Flexible Regulatory Framework for Payment Banks","A flexible and proactive approach towards regulations on payment banks, such as regulations on minimum capital requirements, transaction amounts, and restriction on investments, should be adopted to ensure that the payment bank model becomes commercially viable and scalable.",""],[1,"60","7","Formal Financial Products Regulatory Overhaul","Overhaul the regulatory framework governing formal financial products to attract households",""],[1,"60","8","Simplification of Financial Product Regulations","Household acceptance of formal financial products, such as insurance, equity, etc., can be increased if regulations governing these are simplified and made more consumer-friendly.",""],[1,"60","9","Financial Product Mis-Selling Regulatory Overhaul","Instances of mis-selling of financial products to households needs to be tackled by overhauling the regulatory framework.",""],[1,"60","9","Insurance and Pension Disclosure Strengthening","Disclosure requirements for insurance and pension products need to be strengthened to make it easier for consumers to understand them.",""],[1,"60","10","Insurance Sector Regulatory Simplification","Simplification and relaxation of insurance sector regulations - Substantial simplification of broker regulations can be made.",""],[1,"60","11","Capital Markets KYC Easing and Integration Reform","KYC restrictions in the capital markets can be eased and linked to other KYC information to enable ease of doing business and increase the participation of retail investors.",""],[1,"60","12","Gold Bond Lock-in Period Reduction","The lock-in period for gold bonds should be reduced to make them more attractive.",""]],"91":[[1,"66","9","Global E-Visa Awareness Campaign","Increase e-visa awareness globally by launching an information campaign through our consulates abroad.",""],[1,"66","9","E-Visa Regime for MICE Market Attraction","It is also necessary to launch an e-visa regime to attract clientele from the meetings, incentives, conferences and exhibitions (MICE) market.",""],[1,"66","9","Extended E-Visa Validity for Repeat Visitors","To attract repeat visitors, the validity period of e-visas may be increased to 10 years.",""],[1,"66","10","Expansion of E-Medical Visa Visit Allowances","Enhance the number of annual visits allowed under an e-medical visa.",""],[1,"66","11","Online Foreigner Registration Simplification","Simplify the process of registering online with the Foreigner Regional Registration",""],[1,"67","1","FRRO Help-Desks at Major Airports and Hospitals","Establishing FRRO help- desks at major Indian airports and hospi- tals will provide visitors with the informa- tion to complete the process online.",""],[1,"67","2","Expansion of E-Medical Visa Accompanying Persons","Increase the number of accompanying persons with e-medical visa holders from two to up to four under the same visa, as has been done in countries like Malaysia.",""]],"92":[[1,"67","6","Regional Connectivity Scheme for Aviation","Improve flight connectivity to tourist destina- tions through the timely implementation of the Ministry of Civil Aviation's Regional Connectivity Scheme - UDAN (RCS-UDAN).","Ministry of Civil Aviation"],[1,"67","6","Transit Hub Upgrading for Major Cities","Larger cities like Delhi, Mumbai, Kolkata and Chennai should be converted into efficient and seamless transit hubs.",""],[1,"67","9","River Cruise Tourism and Waterway Navigation Development","Promote river cruise tourism by making the entire stretch of National Waterway No. 1, the River Ganga, from Allahabad to the Farakkah Barrage, fully navigable.",""],[1,"69","3","Common Passes for Multiple Heritage Sites","Create common passes to visit multiple heritage sites.",""],[1,"69","5","Tourist Information Centre Operations","Tourist information centres should be operated by trained personnel and must have resources like maps, travel guides, etc.",""]],"93":[[1,"67","8","National Boating Guidelines for Marine Leisure Industry Regulation","Develop the marine leisure industry by issuing national boating guidelines to regulate the industry in terms of safety, security, marina development, nautical infrastructure for safe access to water, cruising and charters, crewing (skill training), rescue and rationalization of import duties and local taxes to encourage the growth of local boat building.",""],[1,"67","10","Deep-Water Marina Development and Enabling Coastal Activity Policies","Build deep-water marinas in the coastal areas of India including in the Andaman and Nicobar Islands and in Mumbai.",""],[1,"67","10","Enabling Policy Framework for Scuba Diving and Boat-Based Activities","Create enabling policies that permit scuba diving or other activities requiring boat travel.",""]],"94":[[1,"68","3","Community-Based Tourism Enterprise Support","Connect local communities to tourism by encouraging them to set up small enterprises to supply the tourism industry (accommodation, food and material).",""],[1,"68","3","Local Hiring Incentives for Organized Tourism Sector","Employment opportunities can be expanded by ensuring that investors and operators in the organized sector are encouraged to hire staff locally.",""],[1,"68","4","Heritage Conservation and Restoration Employment Initiative","Local craftspersons, masons, carpenters and labourers should be engaged for heritage conservation and restoration activities to create jobs.",""],[1,"68","5","Artisan Database Development","Create a database of artisans based on the different craft forms they are associated with and the areas where they live.",""],[1,"68","6","Tourism Worker Skills Upgrading Programme","Upgrade the skills of existing workers such as taxi drivers, boat operators, guides, and restau- rant and dhaba workers through state tourism departments in association with local tourism and hospitality institutes and industry.",""],[1,"68","7","Heritage Hotel Skill Development Programme","Expertise available with heritage hotels may also be used for skill development in the sector.",""],[1,"68","8","Tour Guide Language Competency Bridge Course","Language competencies of tour guides should be improved through a bridge course conducted by the sector council all across the country.",""],[1,"68","9","Private Sector Tourism Training Support","Support private sector institutes in tourism regulated by government to create the required talent pool.",""],[1,"68","11","Tourism Sector Centres of Excellence","Create Centres of Excellence for leadership in the tourism sector as a fulcrum of professional education, research and advocacy to create managers and entrepreneurs in tourism.",""],[1,"68","11","Tourism Management and Leadership Course Integration","Additionally, ensure that tourism management and leadership is included as a distinct course in top management institutes in India.",""]],"95":[[1,"68","12","Market Linkage Support for Traditional Handicrafts Producers","Enable access to markets for traditional handicrafts producers by linking them with global markets.",""],[1,"68","12","Tribal Handicrafts Export Promotion","The government should also encourage the export of tribal handicrafts.",""],[1,"68","14","Targeted Tourism Promotion Campaigns in Asian Markets","Launch targeted promotional campaigns in Asian countries such as China, Thailand, Malaysia, Singapore and South Korea, using digital media including TV advertisements.",""],[1,"68","15","Data-Driven Consumer Targeting Policy","Design policies using data on consumer usage to target marketing efforts and segments of the population.",""],[1,"68","16","Differential Pricing Review for Heritage Sites","Reconsider differential pricing for heritage sites as the higher ticket price for non-Indians leads to losing out on a large segment of youth travellers.",""],[1,"68","17","International Cultural Centres Expansion","Consider establishing cultural centres in additional countries to spread Indian culture worldwide.",""],[1,"69","4","Foreign Exchange Counters at Tourist Sites","Provide foreign exchange counters at each tourist site.",""]],"96":[[1,"68","1","Museum Gift Acceptance Simplification Reform","Further, ease the process of accepting gifts by museums in India.",""],[1,"68","18","Online Heritage Sites Portal","Create an online portal of all heritage sites to increase awareness regarding these.",""],[1,"68","19","Monument and Museum Ticketing and Access Improvement","Ticketing and access to monuments and museums.",""],[1,"69","1","Online Ticket Distribution System for Heritage and Wildlife Sites","An online ticket distribution system for heritage sites and wild life areas should be developed with time slots to visit.",""],[1,"69","2","Reception Centre Ticketing Streamlining","Buying tickets at reception centres should be streamlined to avoid long queues.",""]],"97":[[1,"71","7","Explore in India Mission","To facilitate participation by private sector players in exploration, launch a mission \"Explore in India\", by revamping the minerals exploration and licensing policy",""],[1,"71","9","Mineral Exploration Area Reservation and Auction Allocation","the provision of \"reservation\" of areas for exploration by state agencies should be utilised and such areas should be allocated through the auction route after the development of reserves.",""],[1,"71","11","Private Sector Rare Earth Mineral Exploration Rules","An exclusive subset of rules to facilitate the exploration of rare earth minerals through private sector participation should be framed.",""],[1,"71","12","Co-mining Permission for Mineral Extraction","Mining companies should be allowed the freedom to co-mine other minerals found in the same mining area.",""],[1,"72","1","Tax Structure Rationalization and Investment Facilitation","To promote this sector we need to rationalize tax structures and facilitate investment including FDI.",""],[1,"72","3","PARIVESH Single-Window Clearance Hub","While PARIVESH has been launched on August 10, 2018 as a single window hub for environment, forest, wildlife and CRZ clearances, the Ministry of Environment and Forest (MoEF) should declare upfront inviolate forest areas.","Ministry of Environment and Forest (MoEF)"],[1,"72","4","Statutory Approval Time-Bound Mineral Exploration and Mining Clearance Reform","All statutory approvals should mandatorily be granted within 180 days of application for exploration and mining of minerals.",""],[1,"72","5","Delegation of Forest Clearance Permission for Exploration","Local forest officers may be empowered to grant permission under the FC Act, 1980 for exploration in forest areas.",""],[1,"72","7","Relaxed Minor Minerals Licensing Regime","Boosting minor minerals through a relaxed licensing regime",""],[1,"72","8","Minor Mineral Mining Rights for Landowners and Farmers","Landowners/farmers/tribals need to be given mining rights for minor minerals on their land, to enable them to mine either on their own or by outsourcing it, without auction or payment of an additional 30 per cent of the royalty to the DMF.",""],[1,"72","10","Mining Lease Auction Allocation","mining leases can be allocated through the auction route.",""],[1,"72","12","National Mineral Regulatory Authority","A National Mineral Regulatory Authority, with subordinate state authorities, may be created to regulate the minerals sector to operate transparently with internationally recognized technical standards.",""],[1,"72","13","National Data Repository for Mineral Resources","A National Data Repository (NDR) of Mineral Resources should be created and uploaded online.",""],[1,"72","14","Public Reporting Mechanism for Exploration Firms","Introduce a robust and transparent public reporting mechanism for exploration firms, which is compliant with the Joint Ore Resources Committee (JORC) code or an equivalent code in the statute.",""],[1,"72","15","De-reservation and Reallocation of Unused Mineral Bearing Areas","The huge mineral bearing areas reserved for state agencies that have not been utilized for more than 2 years should be de-reserved and allocated to the end user industry/ auctioned.",""],[1,"72","16","Self-Certification and GIS-Based Monitoring for MMDR Act Enforcement","Instead of field inspections, a system of self- approval/self-certification with GIS based monitoring should be adopted for enforcing the provisions of the MMDR Act.",""],[1,"72","18","Mining Taxation and Royalty Rationalization","Rationalize taxation/royalty and other levies on mining, capping it at a maximum of 40 per cent of the sale value, as per global practice, to make mining competitive globally.",""],[1,"73","1","Mining Engineering Colleges as Mineral Exploration Centers","Mining engineering colleges should be developed as centres for mineral exploration.",""],[1,"73","2","Technology Upgradation Import Duty Reduction","Encourage technological upgradation by reducing import duty, initially for a period of five to ten years, on equipment/cutting edge technology to boost safety, limit environmental damage, improve productivity and increase growth.",""],[1,"73","3","Strategic Overseas Mine Acquisition Organization","India should create an organization for strategic acquisitions of mines in other countries and to sign diplomatic and trade agreements.",""],[1,"73","4","Zero Waste Mining Incentive Scheme","Promote zero waste mining by incentivizing leaseholders to utilize and sell sub-grade minerals/rejects.",""],[1,"73","5","Advance Bidding Process for Expiring Non-Captive Mines","To ensure smooth transition in 2020 and to avoid disruption in mineral supplies and job losses, the Ministry of Mines should complete the process of bidding for these mines one year before the date of expiry.","Ministry of Mines"],[1,"80","24","Exploration-Cum-Mining Lease Exploration Programme","Expeditiously complete detailed exploration through exploration-cum-mining leases based on production/revenue sharing model.",""],[1,"80","25","State Land Availability for Mining Facilitation","Put the onus on concerned state governments to make the land required for mining available.",""],[1,"81","1","Commercial Coal Mining Operationalization","Expeditiously operationalize commercial coal mining.",""]],"98":[[1,"72","6","Compensatory Afforestation on Degraded Government Forestland","State PSUs and the private sector should also be allowed to undertake compensatory afforestation on degraded government forestland like central PSUs.",""]],"99":[[1,"79","3","Extend GST to Energy Commodities","Oil, natural gas, electricity and coal may be brought under GST to enable input tax credit.",""],[1,"79","4","Uniform GST Rate for Energy Forms","Have the same GST rate for all forms of energy to enable a level playing field.",""],[1,"79","5","Functional Energy Subsidy Reform","All form of subsidies should be provided as functional subsidies to end-consumers to empower them to choose the energy form most suitable and economical to them.",""],[1,"79","7","Competitive Bidding for Power Purchase Agreements","All PPAs including those with state generation companies (GENCOs) should be based on competitive bidding.",""],[1,"79","8","Capacity Market for Flexible Power Supply","Introduce a capacity market to encourage flexible capacity for peak demand and intermittency.",""],[1,"80","4","Direct Benefit Transfer Agricultural Input Subsidy","For agriculture, an upfront subsidy per acre of land through Direct Benefit Transfer (DBT) may be considered instead of providing separate subsidies for fertilizers, electricity, crop insurance etc.",""],[1,"80","9","Time-of-Day Tariff for Renewable Energy Use","Introduce time-of-day tariff to promote the use of renewable energy.",""]],"100":[[1,"80","12","Common Carrier and Open Access Gas Pipeline Policy","Provide for a common carrier and open access to gas pipelines.",""],[1,"80","13","Separation of PNGRB Developmental and Regulatory Functions","Separate the developmental and regulatory functions of the PNGRB.",""],[1,"80","14","National Gas Grid Establishment","Expedite establishing the National Gas Grid.",""],[1,"80","15","City Gas Distribution Expansion","Promote city gas distribution to provide piped natural gas (PNG).",""],[1,"80","22","R-LNG Transportation Fuel and Rural PNG Promotion","Declare regasified liquefied natural gas (R-LNG) as transportation fuel and promote PNG in rural areas.",""]],"101":[[1,"80","16","Flexibility in Contract Terms for Stranded Oil and Gas Assets","Review and provide the required flexibility in contract terms to make stranded oil and gas assets functional.",""],[1,"80","17","Production Enhancement Contracts for Existing Oil and Gas Fields","Enhance production from the existing fields of ONGC and OIL using cutting-edge technology through a framework of production enhancement contracts.",""],[1,"80","18","Market Pricing for Non-Viable Gas Blocks","Consider market pricing for blocks that are not viable because of low gas pricing.",""],[1,"80","19","Shared Oil and Gas Evacuation Infrastructure","Provide for shared infrastructure for evacuation of oil and gas from small and scattered on- shore and offshore fields.",""],[1,"80","23","Strategic Reserve Creation Policy","Create strategic reserves through various policy options.",""]],"102":[[1,"80","20","Priority Sector Support for 2G Bio-Ethanol Projects","Provide \"priority sector\" status for 2G bio- ethanol projects.",""],[1,"80","20","Biofuel Solar Park Model and Government Land Leasing for Energy Crops","The concept of 'solar parks' can be applied to bio-fuels; land can be leased by the government to oil marketing companies (OMCs) for energy crops.",""],[1,"80","21","Viability Gap Funding for 2G Ethanol Projects","The government should provide viability gap funding/financial assistance for 2G ethanol project developers/technology partners.",""],[1,"81","7","Commercial Biogas Subsidy Support","Commercial biogas needs to be promoted by providing subsidy to consumers.",""]],"103":[[1,"84","4","National Highway Maintenance Management System","Maintain NH assets by adopting a maintenance management system (MMS).",""],[1,"84","5","Contractor Penalties for Poor O&M Quality","Build in heavy penalties on contractors for poor quality of operations and maintenance (O&M) into contracts across all contract modes.",""],[1,"84","8","Land Acquisition Streamlining Reform","Streamline land acquisition",""],[1,"84","9","Bhoomi Rashi Web Portal Operationalization","Ensure that MORTH's Bhoomi Rashi web portal, which is integrated with the Ministry of Finance's Public Financial Management System (PFMS), is fully functional by March 2019.","MORTH | Ministry of Finance"],[1,"84","10","Stakeholder Sensitization for Land Acquisition Reform","Sensitize stakeholders to iron out details of land acquisitions like determining market",""],[1,"85","5","Electronic Toll Collection System Expansion","Expand the reach of the electronic toll collection (ETC) system",""],[1,"85","6","FASTag Electronic Toll Collection Rollout","Complete the setup of 'FASTag', which employs radio-frequency identification, for ETC in all lanes for the 418 toll plazas with the National Highway Authority of India (NHAI) by March 31, 2019.",""],[1,"85","7","FASTag Charging System Streamlining","Streamline the 'FASTag' charging system.",""],[1,"85","8","Electronic Toll Collection Infrastructure Upgrade at Toll Plazas","Engage with stakeholders and concessionaires (for PPP toll plazas) to ensure that all toll plazas have the requisite infrastructure for ETC.",""]],"104":[[1,"84","6","Black Spot Elimination through Road Safety Infrastructure","Eliminate 789 black spots identified by the Ministry of Road Transport and Highways (MORTH) by March 2020 by constructing permanent structures such as flyovers/vehicular underpasses (VUPs) and pedestrian underpasses (PUPs).","Ministry of Road Transport and Highways (MORTH)"],[1,"84","7","Motor Vehicles Amendment Bill Passage","The Motor Vehicles (Amendment) Bill, 2016, pending before the Rajya Sabha, must be passed without delay.",""],[1,"84","7","National Road Safety Board","Constitute a National Safety Board to enforce road safety rules.",""],[1,"84","13","Driving Training Centres for Commercial Vehicle Drivers","Collaborate with original equipment manufacturers and other stakeholders to set up driving training centres (DTCs) to train commercial vehicle drivers.",""],[1,"84","14","Automated Driving Testing System","Ensure stringent testing of driving skills before granting driving licences by adopting technologically advanced methods such as the automated driving testing system.",""]],"105":[[1,"83","14","PWD Institutional Strengthening and Training","Improve the implementation capacity of states'/ UTs' public work departments (PWDs) through institutional strengthening and training.",""],[1,"84","12","Vocational Training Courses on Road Construction","Introduce vocational training courses on road construction in Industrial Training Institutes (ITIs).",""],[1,"84","15","Worker Training Programme for Project Employees","MORTH has targeted training more than one lakh workers employed in various projects by June 2018 and a further 2.5 lakh workers by 2019 under its programme.","MORTH"],[1,"84","17","Road Transport Research and Development Budget Earmark","Earmark 0.1 per cent of MORTH's annual budget for R&D.",""],[1,"84","18","National Transport Data Centre for Road Research","Establish a transport data centre at the national level for applied research on roads.",""],[1,"84","19","IT-Enabled Traffic Management R&D Enhancement","Enhance R&D on IT-enabled traffic management systems.",""],[1,"84","20","Construction Materials and Techniques Development","Develop new materials/techniques for construction.",""],[1,"84","21","Periodic Revision of Highway Technology Codes and Guidelines","Periodically revise codes/standards/guidelines related to technology use in line with the latest technological developments in the highways sector and disseminate codal provisions.",""]],"106":[[1,"86","6","Railway Safety Improvement Programme","Improve the safety of the railways, achieving zero fatalities from the 2016-17 level of 238 fatalities and reducing the number of accidents from the 73 recorded in 2017-18.",""],[1,"88","16","Train Safety Enhancement and Station Modernization","4. Enhance safety of trains to reduce accidents and modernize stations:",""],[1,"89","1","Railway Level Crossing Elimination and Track Fencing","Eliminate level crossings and cattle crossings and fence railway tracks in areas with high levels of activity to prevent accidents.",""],[1,"89","2","Rail Safety Technology Upgradation","Increase the use of proven, advanced technologies such as automatic train protection, fog safety devices, end of train telemetry devices and on-board/online condition monitoring systems.",""],[1,"89","3","Implementation of High-Level Safety Review Committee Recommendations","Implement the 22 recommendations of the High-Level Safety Review Committee chaired by Dr. Kakodkar.",""],[1,"89","4","By-pass Crossing and Grade Separation Upgrade Programme","Upgrade and ensure the smooth functioning of by-pass crossings and grade separations.",""],[1,"89","5","Railway Station Redevelopment Programme","Redevelop 100 out of 400 identified railway stations by 2022.",""],[1,"89","6","Station Cleaning Contracting and Bio-Toilet Expansion","Award station-cleaning contracts to private vendors and sharply increase the number of bio-toilets by 2019.",""]],"107":[[1,"89","19","Technology Absorption and Human Resource Development Measures","Put in place measures to absorb new technologies and develop human resources.",""]],"108":[[1,"91","7","Airport Charges and Tariff Transparency Reform","Ensure that airport tariffs, taxes on fuel, landing charges, passenger services, cargo and other charges are determined in an efficient, fair and transparent manner.",""],[1,"93","6","Airport Tariff Structure Reform","The Ministry of Civil Aviation has mandated that all airports move from a single to a hybrid till structure.","Ministry of Civil Aviation"],[1,"93","14","Domestic Hub Development Provisions in Traffic Rights Auctions","Include provisions for domestic hub development while auctioning traffic rights.",""],[1,"93","15","Sector Investment Support","Increase investment in the sector through financial and infrastructure support",""],[1,"94","18","Airport Regulatory Environment Reform","Ease the regulatory environment for airports",""],[1,"94","19","Aviation Market Deregulation and Liberalization","Deregulate further and open up the aviation market to help increase passenger and freight traffic in India.",""],[1,"94","20","Consistent Tariff Determination Model","Adopt a consistent model for tariff determination so that it reduces passenger cost.",""],[1,"94","21","Aviation Turbine Fuel GST Alignment Reform","Align taxation and pricing structure to global benchmarks by considering bringing aviation turbine fuel (ATF) under the rubric of GST.",""],[1,"94","22","Airport Land Commercial Use Liberalisation","Amend the AAI Act to allow commercial usage of land with airports by liberalising end-use restrictions for existing and future airports.",""],[1,"94","23","PPP Regulatory Capacity Strengthening and Judicial Review Streamlining","Strengthen regulatory capacity with respect to public private partnerships and streamline the judicial review process to ensure timely implementation of DGCA's decisions.",""],[1,"94","24","DGCA Regulatory Independence Reform","Ensure that the DGCA acts as a truly independent regulator, with the Ministry of Civil Aviation focusing on policies.","Ministry of Civil Aviation"],[1,"94","25","ICAO Compliance and Personnel Skilling","Meet the regulatory and security requirements prescribed by the International Civil Aviation Organization (ICAO) at all times.",""],[1,"95","5","DGCA Autonomy for Aviation Safety Oversight","DGCA should be given autonomy for an effective aviation safety oversight system.",""],[1,"95","8","Single-Window Aviation Services System","DGCA should create a single-window system for all aviation related transactions, queries and complaints.",""]],"109":[[1,"91","3","MRO Industry Expansion","Expand the maintenance, repair and overhaul (MRO) industry from USD 1.8 billion in 2017 to USD 2.3 billion.",""],[1,"93","16","MRO Tax Reduction and Infrastructure Status Reform","Reduce taxes on MRO services and consider granting infrastructure status for MRO.",""],[1,"94","3","Airport Real Estate Monetization Initiative","Monetize vacant real estate near AAI airports in all major centres of traffic to increase non- aeronautical revenues.",""],[1,"94","9","GST Rate Reduction for Avgas","A further reduction in GST rates on Avgas will allow flying training organizations to make training more affordable.",""],[1,"94","10","Air Cargo Growth Promotion","4. Promote air cargo growth",""],[1,"94","11","Transhipment Hub Development Initiative","Promote \"Fly-from-India\" through the creation of transhipment hubs.",""],[1,"94","12","Integrated Digital Supply Chain and E-Cargo Gateway","Develop an integrated digital supply chain or e-cargo gateway based on the National Air Cargo Community System (NACCS) platform.",""],[1,"94","14","E-Contracting and Cargo Booking Platform","e-contracting/booking of cargo - with access to financial payment gateways.",""],[1,"94","16","E-Compliances Online Clearance System","e-compliances (initially online clearances by six participating governmental agencies; rest to follow).",""],[1,"94","17","Cargo Sewa Grievance Redressal Module","Cargo Sewa - a grievance redressal module linked to Air Sewa.",""]],"110":[[1,"94","5","Aviation Industry Collaboration and Training Initiative","Promote collaboration between original equipment manufacturers (OEMs), industry and educational institutes to teach the latest concepts in the aviation industry including management principles, IT in aviation, etc.",""],[1,"94","6","Long-Term Aviation Technology Research Plan","Formulate long-term plans for advanced research in aviation technologies to create a manufacturing ecosystem in the country.",""],[1,"94","7","National Aviation University Course Commencement","Expedite commencement of courses by the National Aviation University after due consultation with stakeholders.",""],[1,"94","8","Private Sector Participation in Aviation, Training, and R&D Sponsorship","Facilitate greater involvement of the private sector in sponsoring aviation institutions, industrial training and R&D projects.",""]],"111":[[1,"99","12","Merchant Shipping Bill Reform","The new Merchant Shipping Bill to replace the Merchant Shipping Act, 1958, needs to be enacted at the earliest to promote the ease of doing business, transparency and effective delivery of services.",""],[1,"100","7","Shipbuilding Finance Scheme Revival","Revive the shipbuilding finance scheme in line with the subsidy scheme that was in force during 2002-2007, which led to high growth rates in the shipping sector and full order books for Indian shipyards.",""]],"112":[[1,"97","9","Fishing Harbour and Fish Processing Centre Development","Devlopment of fishing harbours, fish processing centres",""]],"113":[[1,"107","4","Standardized Procurement of Citizen Service Digital Platforms","Procurement of such digital platforms could be standardized by the central government based on an analysis of successful case studies in India.",""],[1,"107","5","Comprehensive Cyber Security Framework","MeitY will need to evolve a comprehensive cyber security framework for data security, safe digital transactions and complaint redressal.","MeitY"],[1,"107","5","Periodic Compliance Audit of State E-Services","The National e-governance Division of MeitY should periodically audit compliance of e-services offered by state governments.","MeitY | National e-governance Division of MeitY"],[1,"107","5","E-Services Performance Reporting System","It should bring out a performance report of e-services with a view to improve service delivery.","National e-governance Division of MeitY"]],"114":[[1,"109","4","Integrated Mobility Planning and Coordination Architecture","An integrated institutional architecture for planning and coordinating the regulation of mobility such as a Unified Metropolitan Transport Authority is needed.",""],[1,"109","4","Integrated Land-Use and Transport Planning","Spatial plans should provide for integrating land-use and transport planning to support more mixed-use development for enhancing economic activity, reducing commuting time and improving environmental quality.",""],[1,"109","4","Public Transport and Intermediate Transit Support","There is a need for focused attention to public transport, including existing intermediate and para-transit services, especially in smaller cities.",""],[1,"109","4","Pooled Green Transport Fund","A pooled green transport fund to support such investments is recommended.",""],[1,"109","4","Inter-Ministerial Electric Vehicle Mission","A high-level inter-ministerial electric vehicle (EV) mission is necessary for proper coordination on the EV agenda.",""]],"115":[[1,"110","1","Urban Capital Investment Output and Outcome Measurement Framework","There is a need for a framework that mandates measurable outputs and outcomes for all capital investments in infrastructure and services in cities.",""],[1,"110","3","Urban Digital Transformation Roadmap","cities need to put in place a digital transformation roadmap across both hard infrastructure and software applications.",""],[1,"110","5","Urban Digital Transformation Roadmap","Additionally, the digital transformation roadmap would also build on the considerable work done in cities on geographic information systems (GIS) and apply these for geo-locating, mapping and publishing public assets in the city such as parks, playgrounds, public toilets, bus stops, streetlights, manholes, water and sewerage lines, storm water drains, power lines, etc., and linking these to grievance redressal, participatory budgeting, transparent works management, and contractor payments.",""],[1,"111","2","Data Observatories in Partnership with Civil Society","Data observatories in partnership with civil society.",""],[1,"111","2","Smart Command and Control Centres","More than 20 smart command and control centres are under implementation and an equal number are under tendering.",""],[1,"111","3","Open-Source Urban Data Observatory Guidelines","The MoHUA guidelines should institutionalize the need for regulation around data observatories and make them open source in nature (by limiting private ownership of such data), while at the same time protecting the privacy of citizens.","MoHUA"],[1,"111","3","Inter-Agency Coordination through Urban Information Systems","Institutionally, there is need to leverage information to achieve better inter- agency coordination within ULBs and with SPVs.",""]],"116":[[1,"108","11","Urban Poor Voice Enhancement Mechanisms","Smart mechanisms to enhance the voices of the urban poor, slum dwellers, migrants and other underprivileged citizens.",""],[1,"110","6","Urban Poor Service Access Single-Window Facility","Cities should dedicate a single-window facility for the urban poor to access basic services such as water supply, drainage and sewerage, and affordable housing in the form of dormitory and rental housing.",""],[1,"110","6","Urban Poor Financial Inclusion Through Jan Dhan Yojana","Cities must ensure that the urban poor and slum dwellers including recent migrants can avail of city services and subsidies and are financially included through the Jan Dhan Yojana.",""],[1,"110","6","Area-Based and Pan-City Urban Inclusion Mapping","Urban poor communities and slums, benefitted by area-based development (ABD) or pan city proposal (PCP) solutions, should be mapped in conjunction with improvements in parameters such as access to public assets and reducing service deficit including in the areas of education and health.",""]],"117":[[1,"112","2","Open Defecation Free India Initiative","Making India Open Defecation Free (ODF) by October 2, 2019.",""],[1,"114","1","Rural Household Toilet Construction in Lagging States","0.90 crore are to be constructed in two states, namely Uttar Pradesh and Bihar.",""],[1,"114","4","Community Toilet Construction and Community Maintenance","Where space is a constraint, construct community toilets with participation and ownership of stakeholders.",""],[1,"114","5","Promotion of Steep-Slope Rural Toilets","To ensure continued usage of toilets and limit water used for flushing, rural toilets with steep slope should be widely promoted in rural areas.",""],[1,"114","10","Highway Community Toilet Expansion","Increase the number of community toilets along the highways.",""],[1,"114","17","Accelerated Household Toilet Construction Strategy","A special strategy should be adopted to expedite the construction of household toilets in the states of Uttar Pradesh and Bihar.",""],[1,"115","1","Twin-Pit Toilet Adoption","Adopt the wider use of twin-pit toilets.",""]],"118":[[1,"112","3","Sanitation Information, Education and Communication and Behaviour Change Campaigns","Carrying out extensive information, education and communication (IEC) and behaviour change campaigns to change the attitude of people regarding healthy sanitation practices.",""],[1,"114","2","Swachh Bharat Mission Expansion and Reform Package","The strategies to tackle the challenges faced by SBM have been categorized under four broad heads - expanding the scope of SBM, inducing behavioural change, expediting construction and leveraging technology, and changing governance and practices.",""],[1,"114","3","Swachhata Integration in Public Institutions","The concept of Swachhata needs to be integrated into hospitals, government offices and other public establishments.",""],[1,"114","11","Behaviour Change Communication and Inter-Personal Communication Campaigns","Plan intensive behaviour change communication (BCC) and inter-personal communication (IPC) campaigns beyond the SBM target year of 2019.",""],[1,"114","12","Behaviour Change Communication Campaign for ODF Progress","Draw up a clear and concerted behaviour change communication campaign specifically aimed at panchayats and cities that have shown slow progress towards ODF status.",""],[1,"114","13","School and Campus Waste Management Awareness Programme","Children should be made aware of sustainable waste management practices through suitable changes in the school syllabus; engage college campuses and teachers to spread awareness of these practices.",""],[1,"114","14","Waste Segregation Behavior Change Communication","BCC should lay greater emphasis on encouraging people to segregate waste into wet, dry and hazardous waste right at the point of waste generation.",""]],"119":[[1,"113","13","Decentralized Waste Treatment Practice","The continuing practice of decentralized treatment of waste.",""],[1,"114","6","On-site Waste Treatment by Bulk Generators","Bulk generators of waste should ensure on-site treatment of waste.",""],[1,"114","7","Sewage Treatment Coverage for Drains and Tributaries","All drains/tributaries flowing to rivers should be covered with sewage treatment plants by 2022- 23.",""],[1,"114","8","Monetary Compensation and Social Security for Waste Segregators","Give higher monetary compensation and social security to rag pickers and small sanitation workers for segregating waste.",""],[1,"114","9","Expansion of Swachh Bharat Mission to Landfills and Plastic Waste Initiatives","The scope of SBM may be expanded to cover initiatives for landfills and plastic waste.",""],[1,"114","15","Decentralized Local Waste Disposal System","Promote disposal of kitchen and home waste at the local level through resident welfare associations.",""],[1,"114","16","Promotion of Bio-digester Technology for Sewage Infrastructure","To reduce the cost and time incurred on laying sewage pipelines and constructing sewage treatment plants, SBM should encourage the use of bio-digester technology.",""],[1,"115","2","Household Modular Wet Waste Disposal Devices","Promote the use of modular wet waste disposal machines or other such devices for the disposal of bio-waste at the household level itself.",""],[1,"115","3","Recycled Construction and Demolition Waste Use Promotion","The cement and construction sectors should be encouraged to consume material made of recycled construction and demolition (C&D) waste.",""],[1,"115","3","Organic Waste Compost Procurement by Fertilizer Sector","Similarly, the fertilizer sector should procure compost produced out of organic waste.",""],[1,"115","4","Public Dustbin Provision in Urban and Peri-Urban Areas","Ensure the availability of adequate numbers of dustbins in public spaces in urban and peri- urban areas.",""],[1,"115","5","GST Concession for Bio-toilets and Bio-digesters","Expenditure on bio-toilets/bio-digesters may be considered for concession from the goods and services tax (GST) to encourage large-scale adoption.",""],[1,"115","6","Ward-Level SBM and Faecal Sludge Management Integration Action Plan","Draft and implement a 5-year action plan to integrate SBM and faecal sludge management (FSM) at the ward level in cities.",""],[1,"115","7","Waste-to-Energy Plant Tripartite Agreement Framework","Companies that want to establish waste-to-energy plants should have tripartite agreements in which one party is the producer of energy from waste; the other two should be the concerned municipal body and electricity distributing company.",""]],"120":[[1,"115","8","Urban Local Body User Charge Reform for Waste and Toilet Services","ULBs should be nudged to charge adequate user charges for collection and disposal of waste and maintenance of toilets.",""],[1,"115","9","Priority Sector Lending for Solid and Liquid Waste Management Projects","Solid and liquid waste management projects should be covered under priority sector lending.",""],[1,"115","10","ODF Status Monitoring and Corrective Action","the government should continue to monitor and undertake corrective measures for areas that might be slipping back from ODF status.",""]],"121":[[1,"116","5","River Cleanliness and Continuous Flow Initiative","Ensure Aviral and Nirmal Dhara in the Ganga and other rivers along with their tributaries.",""],[1,"117","3","Namami Gange River Cleaning and Rejuvenation Scheme","The government also launched the \"Namami Gange\" scheme in 2014-15 to clean and rejuvenate the River Ganga to maintain \"Aviral\" and \"Nirmal Dhara\" and ensure its ecological and geological integrity.",""],[1,"118","3","River Linking and Feeder Canal Completion Programme","Other notable programmes that need to be completed include the Ken-Betwa River linking project, the Pancheshwar project, the Rajasthan feeder and Sirhind feeders (Punjab &Rajasthan) and the Siang project in North-East India.",""],[1,"118","4","National Mission for Clean Ganga Coordination for Waste Management","The National Mission for Clean Ganga needs to coordinate with the Ministry of Drinking Water, Supply and Sanitation for solid and liquid waste management in 1600 gram panchayats (covering 4464 villages situated on the banks of the Ganga in five states).","Ministry of Drinking Water, Supply and Sanitation"],[1,"118","4","Acceleration of Clean Ganga Project Completion","Corrective measures need to be taken to expedite the completion of the projects.",""],[1,"119","9","Integrated River Basin Management and River Basin Organisations","To mitigate conflicts and achieve equitable distribution of water, an integrated river basin management approach needs to be adopted.",""],[1,"119","10","River Revitalization Pilot and Scale-Up","NITI Aayog has developed a concept note on Revitalization of Rivers, which may be implemented on a pilot basis before being expanded across major states.",""],[1,"119","11","Integrated Ganga River Management","To ensure Aviral and Nirmal Dhara in the Ganga, the river should be managed as a single system.",""],[1,"119","12","Medium-Term Flood Management Scheme","There is need for a scheme on medium term measures for flood management.",""],[1,"119","12","Long-Term Flood Protection Measures","Besides, long term measures for Bihar, UP and NE states should be explored to achieve permanent protection from floods.",""],[1,"119","12","North East Water Management Authority","The formation of North East Water Management Authority (NEWMA) in North- East states will comprehensively address the flood issue in the region.",""],[1,"120","8","River Cleanliness and Continuous Flow Initiative","Ensuring Aviral and Nirmal Dhara in the Ganga, Yamuna, and other rivers.",""],[1,"120","12","National Mission for Clean Ganga","the government is aware of this challenge and has launched National Mission for Clean Ganga to address this concern",""]],"122":[[1,"120","5","Universal Household LPG Coverage for Cooking","Ensuring the coverage of all households with LPG for cooking.",""],[1,"122","19","Pradhan Mantri Ujjwala Yojana Continuation","The air pollution issue will require continued efforts on the Pradhan Mantri Ujjwala Yojana.",""]],"123":[[1,"120","4","Crop Residue Burning Elimination Initiative","Eliminating crop residue burning.",""],[1,"121","6","Farm Mechanization Scheme Modifications for Crop Residue Management","the Ministry of Agriculture, Cooperation and Farmers' Welfare should introduce suitable modifications in their guidelines of schemes for farm mechanization to provide support to farmers to purchase equipment to collect, transport and sell biomass to processing sites for economic benefits.","Ministry of Agriculture, Cooperation and Farmers' Welfare"],[1,"121","7","Biomass Management Action Plan Implementation","The Task Force on Biomass Management, constituted by NITI Aayog under the 'Cleaner Air, Better Life' initiative, has made the following key recommendations in its report titled \"Action Plan for Biomass Management\" that need to be implemented by the central and state governments expeditiously:","NITI Aayog | central and state governments"],[1,"121","8","Financial Support for In-Situ Crop Residue Management","Extend financial support to farmers in the short- term for in-situ treatment of paddy-straw/non- burning of crop residue.",""],[1,"121","9","Clean Air Impact Fund","Create a \"Clean Air Impact Fund\" to provide viability gap funding (VGF) for projects with long gestation periods and low returns on investment such as bio-power or bio-ethanol projects.",""],[1,"122","1","Crop Harvesting Technology Upgradation and Farm Residue Utilization","Upscale technologies for crop harvesting and utilization of farm residue",""],[1,"122","2","Support Service-Based Shared Infrastructure","Support service-based shared infrastructure.",""],[1,"122","3","Process-Based Incentives for Entrepreneurs","Provide process-based incentives for entrepreneurs.",""],[1,"122","4","Accelerated Depreciation for Farm Implements","Allow accelerated depreciation for farm implements.",""],[1,"122","6","Village Panchayat Zero Burning Reward Scheme","Institute a reward scheme for village panchayats with zero burning.",""],[1,"122","7","Farm Fire Monitoring Mechanism","Put in place a mechanism to monitor farm fires.",""],[1,"122","8","Regulatory Support for Crop Residue Utilization Business Models","Provide regulatory support for business models for crop residue utilization",""],[1,"122","9","Fuel Quality Criteria Review for Crop-Residue Briquettes and Pellets","o Re-assess the fuel quality criteria for briquettes/pellets made out of crop residue.",""],[1,"122","10","Paddy-Straw Briquette and Pellet Procurement Directive","Issue directives to power plants to procure paddy-straw briquette/pellet.",""],[1,"122","11","Removal of Size Limit for Bio-power Captive Generation","Remove the size limitation for bio-power captive generation.",""],[1,"122","12","Farmer Soil Management Awareness Campaign","Create awareness amongst farmers for better soil management practices",""],[1,"122","13","Farmer Awareness Campaigns","Plan awareness campaigns for farmers.",""],[1,"122","14","Recognition Incentives for Non-Burning Farmers","Recognize farmers following non-burning practices.",""],[1,"122","15","Information Tools for In-Situ Mulching and On-Farm Management","Design information tools for in-situ mulching and on-farm management.",""]],"124":[[1,"120","13","National Forest Policy Reform","The new National Forest Policy seeks to increase the sustainability of forest management in India.",""],[1,"123","9","National Forest Policy Implementation","The new National Forest Policy, after incorporating the comments of states, concerned central ministries/departments and other stakeholders, should be expeditiously implemented.",""],[1,"123","13","Low-Cost Climate Finance Access Promotion","Access to low cost finance especially through the Green Climate Fund should be encouraged.",""],[1,"123","14","Review of National Climate Change Missions","Review all eight national missions under the National Action Plan on Climate Change in the light of new scientific information and technological advances.",""],[1,"123","15","Waste-to-Energy Mission","New national missions on wind energy, waste-to-energy and coastal areas should be developed.",""],[1,"123","15","Coastal Areas Mission","New national missions on wind energy, waste-to-energy and coastal areas should be developed.",""],[1,"124","2","Implementation of State Action Plan Climate Change Projects","Projects under state action plans on climate change that have been endorsed by the National Steering Committee on Climate Change need to be implemented.",""],[1,"124","3","Climate Resilience Strengthening through Adaptation Financing","Use the National Adaptation Fund for Climate Change and other global funds for strengthening resilience against climate change in sectors like agriculture, forestry, infrastructure and others.",""],[1,"124","4","Climate Change Assessment Capacity Strengthening","Scientific and analytical capacity for climate change related assessments should be strengthened.",""]],"125":[[1,"127","5","Student Tracking and Learning Outcomes Monitoring Framework","Creating a robust framework for tracking individual students across their schooling years that incorporates data on their learning outcomes.",""],[1,"129","2","National Achievement Survey","Recent changes by the government include the introduction of a new and comprehensive National Achievement Survey.",""],[1,"129","2","Competency-Based School Grading Framework","The Ministry of Human Resource Development has also spelt out the competencies and learning levels at different grades on which school grading will be based.","Ministry of Human Resource Development"],[1,"129","13","Independent Learning Outcomes Assessment System","Learning outcomes should be regularly assessed by bodies independent of the line ministries.",""],[1,"130","7","Learning Outcomes Codification and Continuous Evaluation Reform","states should codify the expected learning outcomes for each class and put greater emphasis on continuous and comprehensive evaluation (CCE) to achieve the defined learning outcomes.",""],[1,"130","8","Annual National Achievements Survey Institutionalization","The comprehensive national achievements survey initiated in 2017 needs to be institutionalised on an annual basis.",""],[1,"130","9","Remedial Education Integrated with Regular Schooling","The remediation process should be made part of the education system and should be run concurrently with regular classes so that no child gets left behind.",""],[1,"130","10","High-School Readiness and Bridge Programmes","high-school readiness programmes/ tutorials, including bridge programmes, should be incorporated just after class VIII or in the early months of class IX especially for remediation.",""],[1,"130","11","Compartmental Examination and Remediation Assessment Reform","The CCE should also encompass compartmental exams to check the quality and outcomes of remediation.",""],[1,"130","12","Electronic National Educational Registry","An electronic national educational registry may be conceptualised for tracking each child's learning outcomes based on CCE and final exams through a unique ID.",""],[1,"130","13","Credit-Based Student Progression System","Develop a system of awarding credits for every subject and grade passed, specifying the minimum credits required to appear in the final exam for any grade.",""]],"126":[[1,"127","6","Vocational Education Pathway Expansion","Providing a real and viable alternative path for vocational education starting at higher levels to improve employability.",""],[1,"130","14","Secondary School Vocational Course Pathways","Give children the option, under the guidance of the school and parents, of branching into vocational courses from secondary school level",""],[1,"131","2","Separate Academic Tracks in General Education","Develop separate track even within the general education stream, as has been done in certain advanced countries.",""],[1,"131","3","State-Level Vocational Education Implementation Guidelines","Design guidelines for states to implement vocational education at the school level, which may cover aspects such as selection of schools/ trades, tendering process for labs, database of industry contacts for field visits/guest lectures, timings, workshops, permitting informal apprenticeships or assistantship in the formal system, etc.",""],[1,"131","4","Vocational Education Innovation Pilot Programme","Pilot different innovation models in vocational education and provide adequate funding for successful innovative programmes.",""],[1,"131","5","Competency-Based Pre-Primary and Primary Curriculum Reform","Pre-primary and primary syllabus should be designed on a skill/competency-based continuum.",""],[1,"131","7","NSQF-Aligned Vocational Education Syllabus Reform","The vocational education syllabus should be NSQF-aligned and ensure smooth transition from school education to vocational education.",""],[1,"131","8","Curriculum Enrichment with Summer Activities and Study Trips","The curriculum should include summer activities and monthly study trips, including visits to practitioners for practical learning.",""],[1,"131","12","Life Skills Curriculum Integration","Life skills, including coping with failure/crises and stress management, should be included as part of the school curriculum.",""],[1,"140","8","Secondary School Skill Development Integration","Skill development should be made an integral part of the secondary school curriculum.",""],[1,"142","10","Vocational Education from Class VIII","vocational education may be initiated from class VIII.",""]],"127":[[1,"128","1","School-Based Child Mental Health Support","Strengthening support for children as part of the school curriculum to improve child mental health.",""],[1,"131","13","School-Based Mental Health Counselling Access","Easy and safe access to mental health support should be strengthened.",""],[1,"131","14","School Counselling and Support Services for Girl Children","Easy and safe access to counselling and support must be provided for girl children in schools, especially focused on victims of abuse, violence and other gender-related social evils.",""]],"128":[[1,"129","12","Increase Public Education Spending","Government spending on education as a whole (not just school education) should be increased to at least 6 per cent of GDP by 2022.",""],[1,"132","2","Inclusive Higher Education for Vulnerable Groups","Make higher education more inclusive for the most vulnerable groups.",""],[1,"132","11","Continuation of Rashtriya Uchchatar Shiksha Abhiyan","Implementation and continuation of the centrally sponsored scheme, Rashtriya Uchchatar Shiksha Abhiyan (RUSA):",""],[1,"133","4","RUSA Phase II Quality Enhancement and Equity Support","The second phase of RUSA puts a premium on quality enhancement and addresses concerns of access and equity in the aspirational districts identified by the NITI Aayog.",""],[1,"136","1","Continuation of RUSA","RUSA may be continued beyond March 2020, subject to a credible third-party evaluation.",""]],"129":[[1,"132","3","Mandatory Accreditation Quality Assurance Framework","Adopt accreditation as a mandatory quality assurance framework and have multiple highly reputed accreditation agencies for facilitating the process.",""],[1,"133","5","National Assessment and Accreditation Reform","While making accreditation of higher education institutions mandatory, the reforms move away from an intrusive system to a more enabling, mixed method of assessment and accreditation.",""],[1,"135","8","Mandatory Regular Accreditation of Higher Education Institutions","All higher education institutions must be compulsorily and regularly accredited.",""],[1,"135","9","Transparent Accreditation Agency Empanelment and Disclosure Reform","One way to bridge this gap by 2022-23 is to allow credible accreditation agencies, empanelled through a transparent, high quality process, to provide accreditation.",""]],"130":[[1,"132","4","Research and Innovation Enabling Ecosystem","Create an enabling ecosystem to enhance the spirit of research and innovation.",""],[1,"134","3","Research Parks, Incubation Centres, and University-Society Linkage Centres","Open research parks, incubation centres, university society linkage centre",""],[1,"135","10","Institutions of Eminence University Excellence Initiative","Twenty universities - 10 each from the public and private sector - are being selected as 'Institutions of Eminence' and are helping to attain world-class standards of teaching and research.",""],[1,"135","11","Central University Evaluation and Strategic Planning Initiative","An evaluation may be undertaken to understand the challenges faced by these central universities, and they should be asked to develop strategic plans for getting into the top 500 of global universities rankings in the next 10 years.",""]],"131":[[1,"132","5","Higher Education Employability Improvement Initiative","Improve employability of students completing their higher education.",""],[1,"134","2","Establish Constituent Units and Off-Campus Centres","Open constituent units/off-campus centres within its geographical jurisdiction",""],[1,"134","5","Exemption from Off-Campus Centre Inspection and Monitoring","Exemption from section 12B inspections & annual monitoring of off-campus centres/study centres of private universities",""],[1,"134","6","Establish New Courses, Departments, Schools, and Centres","Start a new course/dept/school/centre",""],[1,"134","7","NSQF-Aligned Skill Courses","Start NSQF-aligned skill courses",""],[1,"134","8","Merit-Based Faculty Incentive Scheme","Merit-based incentives for faculty to attract talent",""],[1,"134","9","Foreign Student Admission and Fee Flexibility Policy","Admit upto 20% of foreign students on merit with freedom to fix fees",""],[1,"134","10","Open and Distance Learning Courses","Offer courses in open & distance learning mode",""],[1,"134","11","Establish New Courses, Programmes, Departments, Schools, and Centres","Start a new course/programme/department/school/centre",""],[1,"134","12","NSQF-Aligned Skill Courses","Start NSQF-aligned skill courses",""],[1,"134","13","Merit-Based Faculty Incentive Scheme","Merit-based incentives to faculty to attract talent",""],[1,"134","14","Foreign Student Admission and Fee Autonomy Policy","Admit upto 20% of foreign students on merit, with freedom to fix fees",""],[1,"134","15","Open and Distance Learning Courses","Offer courses in open and distance learning mode",""],[1,"135","2","Foreign University Collaboration Framework","Create a framework to allow foreign universities of global repute to operate in India, in collaboration with Indian institutions to offer joint degree programmes.",""],[1,"135","5","Higher Education Curriculum Standardization and Continuous Update","Domain experts in each educational field should be asked to develop a basic minimum standard in curriculum that will serve as a benchmark for institutions at the undergraduate and post-graduate levels.",""],[1,"135","6","Integrated Post-Secondary Skills and Vocational Training","Diverse post-secondary career options should be provided through skills/vocational training that should be integrated seamlessly with higher education and the skilling mission.",""],[1,"135","7","Undergraduate Internship Promotion and Mandate Policy","Internships by students in undergraduate courses should be encouraged and potentially mandated in all professional and technical courses.",""],[1,"136","10","Expansion of MOOCs and Open and Distance Learning","There is a need to broaden the scope of Massive Open Online Course (MOOCs) and Open and Distance Learning (ODL) and tap their potential to provide access to quality education beyond geographical boundaries.",""],[1,"136","10","Online Education Programme Authorization for High-Accreditation Universities","Universities with high accreditation scores may be permitted to offer online education programmes.",""],[1,"136","10","Technology-Enabled Teaching to Address Faculty Shortages","In regular courses, technology could be leveraged to overcome faculty shortages.",""]],"132":[[1,"133","6","Graded Autonomy Regulations for Universities and Colleges","Regulations for graded autonomy to universities and autonomous colleges: A three- tiered graded autonomy regulatory system has been initiated, with the categorization of institutions as per their accreditation score by the National Assessment and Accreditation Council (NAAC) or other empanelled accreditation agencies, or by their presence in reputed world rankings.","University Grants Commission (UGC)"],[1,"134","25","Higher Education Regulatory Coordination and Rationalisation","Ensure effective coordination of roles of different higher education regulators, such as the UGC, All India Council for Technical Education (AICTE) and National Council for Teacher Education (NCTE), and restructure or merge these where needed.",""],[1,"135","1","UGC Act Amendment for Tiered Regulatory Structure","Amend the UGC Act to provide legislative backing to the tiered regulatory structure.",""],[1,"135","3","Transparent and Objective Vice-Chancellor Selection Process","Ensure that the selection process of Vice- Chancellors of universities is transparent and objective.",""],[1,"135","4","Performance-Linked Grant Allocation","Link at least a proportion of the grants to performance and quality.",""],[1,"135","12","Performance-Linked Higher Education Funding","Going forward, funding to these institutions should be linked to performance and outcomes through the Ministry of Human Resource Development and the newly constituted Higher Education Funding Agency.","Ministry of Human Resource Development"]],"133":[[1,"136","2","Faculty Recruitment Standards Reform","Develop stringent norms for faculty recruitment in universities and colleges.",""],[1,"136","3","Scheme to Attract Teachers of Indian Origin","A central scheme may be launched to attract teachers of Indian origin.",""],[1,"136","4","Recruit Experienced Industry Practitioners as Faculty","Enable and encourage the recruitment of practitioners with distinguished experience from professional bodies/industry as faculty.",""],[1,"136","5","Alternative Faculty Recruitment Track","This can be achieved through the creation of a separate parallel track, on which the mandatory Ph.D qualification for faculty may be relaxed.",""],[1,"136","5","Adjunct Faculty Recruitment from Industry","These industry practitioners may also be encouraged to join as adjunct faculty in the higher education institutions.",""],[1,"136","6","Pre-Service and Continuous Faculty Training Programme","Introduce pre-service faculty training (3-6 months), including faculty exposure to the latest tools/techniques of quality teaching and research.",""],[1,"136","7","Outcome-Based Faculty Evaluation System","Develop a system of outcome-based faculty evaluation in higher education, which is flexible across different categories of institutions.",""],[1,"136","8","Regular Journal Quality Review Mechanism","Conduct regular quality checks of journals, espe- cially those that are used for evaluating faculty on academic performance indicators (APIs).",""],[1,"139","6","Continuation of NET/SLET Eligibility Requirement for Assistant Professor Recruitment","The UGC-recognised NET/SLET should be continued as a minimum eligibility criterion for recruitment to Assistant Professor positions.",""]],"134":[[1,"140","1","Skilling, Reskilling, and Upskilling Capacity and Infrastructure Development","India needs to build the capacity and infrastructure for skilling/reskilling/up-skilling existing and new entrants to the labour force.",""],[1,"140","5","Development of National Occupation Standards and Qualification Packs","Developing internationally compliant National Occupation Standards (NOS) and the Qualification Packs (QP) that define a job role.",""],[1,"140","6","NSQF Compliance for Training Programmes","Making all training compliant with the National Skills Qualification Framework (NSQF).",""],[1,"140","7","Future Skills Anticipation for Skill Development Courses","Anticipating future skill needs to adapt skill development courses.",""],[1,"140","12","Curriculum Upgradation and Skills Certification Reform","To improve the relevance and quality of courses offered by industrial training institutes (ITIs), polytechnics and private training providers, sector skill councils (SSCs) have been involved in curriculum up-gradation/preparation, and in the assessment and certification process.",""],[1,"140","12","National Skills Qualifications Framework Alignment","Courses are being aligned to the National Skills Qualifications Framework (NSQF).",""],[1,"141","12","Assessment and Certification System","Putting in place an effective, internationally recognized assessment and certification system.",""],[1,"142","2","Industry Skill Requirements Data Reporting Incentive Mechanism","Industry stakeholders must be incentivized to provide data on their skill requirements on an ongoing basis, which could be used as input for the skill requirement assessment made at different levels.",""],[1,"142","3","Regular Labour Market Studies and Curriculum Update Mechanism","Regular labour market studies should be conducted and published by the MSDE in collaboration with the SSCs.","MSDE"],[1,"142","4","Vocational Training Innovation Centres","Create vocational training innovation centres for systematic research and conducting longitudinal studies on improving vocational education.",""],[1,"142","6","National Skilling Regulatory Body","A single regulatory body with branches in all states should be set up to lay down minimum standards for all players in the skilling system like training providers, assessors, etc., and to issue NSQF aligned certificates.",""],[1,"142","8","Transferable Skills Identification Initiative","In addition to scaling RPL, there should be a focus on the identification of transferable skills.",""],[1,"142","9","Skills and Trade Matrix Development","This can be done by developing a skills/trade matrix; and highlighting the overlap of skills across different trades, such as information and communication technology (ICT), knowledge of languages, etc.",""],[1,"142","9","Basic Skill Development Curriculum Reform","The most common transferable skills across the board should be made part of the basic skill development curriculum.",""],[1,"143","7","Sector Skill Council Clustering and Convergence Reform","SSCs should be clustered and based on occupations/functions with respect to job standards/QPs across domains.",""],[1,"143","9","State-Level Skilling Programme Monitoring Indicators","Hence, it is necessary to develop state level indicators, such as placement rates, which help monitoring whether demand requirements are being addressed, and the impact of various government schemes.",""]],"135":[[1,"140","12","Recognition of Prior Learning and Bridge Training","Recognition of prior learning (RPL) has been introduced to ensure certification of and bridge training for the existing work force.",""],[1,"141","10","Apprenticeship Programme Expansion","Involving industry for improved quality and relevance - scaling up the apprenticeship programme.",""],[1,"142","5","Teacher Training Institute Capacity Upgrading","Capacities of teacher training institutes need to be upgraded to ensure the availability of qualified trainers.",""],[1,"142","5","Industry-Institute Linkage for Teacher Cross-Learning","It is also important to provide for cross learning by teachers and industry experts through industry-institute linkages.",""],[1,"142","7","Recognition of Prior Learning Scale-Up under PMKVY","To address the requirement of skilled workers in the unorganized sector, scaling up RPL is required under the PMKVY, using bridge training, apprenticeship, dual training, work- based learning and advanced courses.",""],[1,"142","11","Private School Training Facility Expansion Incentive","Participation by private schools should be incentivized with lower interest rates on loans to expand training facilities.",""],[1,"142","12","Apprenticeship Act and NAPS Awareness Advocacy","Active advocacy is needed to create awareness about recent amendments in the Apprenticeship Act, 1961, and about the National Apprenticeship Promotion Scheme (NAPS) among different stakeholders.",""],[1,"142","13","NAPS Stipend Reimbursement Claim Streamlining","The claim process for reimbursement, through which companies get appropriate refund for funds spent on stipends under the NAPS, needs to be streamlined.",""],[1,"143","1","Apprenticeship System Linked to MUDRA Scheme","apprenticeship system by linking it to MUDRA scheme.",""],[1,"143","2","Academic Equivalence System for ITI Qualifications","Mainstreaming skill development with education through a system for academic equivalence to ITI's qualifications.",""],[1,"143","4","Role Model Promotion for Vocational Training Beneficiaries","Publicize role models/micro entrepreneurs who have benefitted from vocational training courses.",""],[1,"143","6","Expansion of the Skill Programme through MGNREGA","Employment Guarantee Act (MGNREGA), etc., should be tapped to expand the skill programme and contribute to national skill development fund.",""],[1,"143","10","Partnerships with Private Job Counseling Agencies","NSDC may get into partnerships with private jobs counseling agencies for helping newly skilled persons with soft skills and adapting to local conditions.",""]],"136":[[1,"142","14","MSME Sector Integration into Global Value Chains","Facilitate the integration of the micro, small & medium enterprises (MSME) sector into the",""],[1,"143","3","Overseas Employment Promotion Agency","An Overseas Employment Promotion Agency should be set up at the national level under the Ministry of External Affairs.","Ministry of External Affairs | MSDE"]],"137":[[1,"145","1","Public and Preventive Health System Revamp","To revamp radically the public and preventive health system in the nation through the following strategic interventions:",""],[1,"145","2","Integrated Public Health Action and Wellness Movement","Mobilize public health action through an integrated, inter-sectoral and pan-stakeholder approach, targeted at communities and individuals as well as grassroots organizations, aimed at creating an unprecedented people-led movement for health and wellness.",""],[1,"146","3","Lifestyle and Community-Level NCD Prevention Interventions","The large burden of NCDs requires lifestyle and community-level interventions.",""],[1,"147","4","Multi-level Public Health Action Mobilization","Mobilize public health action at multiple levels",""],[1,"147","5","Increase Public Health Funding","Public funding on health should be increased to at least 2.5 per cent of GDP as envisaged in the National Health Policy, 2017.",""],[1,"147","6","Healthy Choices and Behaviours Promotion Policy Measures","Create an environment, through appropriate policy measures, that encourages healthy choices and behaviours:",""],[1,"147","7","School Yoga Programme","Make the practice of yoga a regular activity in all schools through certified instructors.",""],[1,"147","8","Health Tax Increase on Tobacco, Alcohol, and Unhealthy Foods","Increase taxes on tobacco, alcohol and unhealthy foods such as soda and sugar sweetened beverages.",""],[1,"147","10","Village Health Sanitation and Nutrition Day Platform Expansion","Strengthen the Village Health Sanitation and Nutrition Day platform to cover a broader set of health issues across various population groups instead of only focusing on child health.",""],[1,"147","11","Preventive Health Behaviour Change Communication Campaign","Activate multiple channels (schools, colleges, women's groups, traditional events like fairs, social media platforms, National Cadet Corps etc.) and prepare communication materials for catalysing behavioural change towards greater recognition of preventive health care.",""],[1,"148","11","Comprehensive NCD Management Information System","Develop a comprehensive MIS including baseline data for NCDs.",""],[1,"149","3","Local Preventive and Health Promotion Services","Deliver preventive and promotion services, and action on the ground to tackle determinants of ill health locally.",""],[1,"149","4","Healthy India Mass Movement","Create a mass movement for Healthy India (Swasth Bharat Jan Andolan).",""],[1,"152","8","Coordinated Disease Prevention and Public Health Promotion Action","Coordinate action for disease prevention and public health promotion and to address social determinants of health",""],[1,"152","9","Preventive Health Services for Healthy Behaviors and Family Health","Provide preventive services to improve healthy behaviours for family health and control",""]],"138":[[1,"146","2","Mission Indradhanush","During the last four years, the government has taken several steps to strengthen public health in the country including the launch of Mission Indradhanush and Intensified Mission Indradhanush as well as the National AYUSH Mission.",""],[1,"146","2","Intensified Mission Indradhanush","During the last four years, the government has taken several steps to strengthen public health in the country including the launch of Mission Indradhanush and Intensified Mission Indradhanush as well as the National AYUSH Mission.",""],[1,"146","2","National AYUSH Mission","During the last four years, the government has taken several steps to strengthen public health in the country including the launch of Mission Indradhanush and Intensified Mission Indradhanush as well as the National AYUSH Mission.",""],[1,"146","2","Neglected Tropical Diseases Elimination Effort","Efforts have also been intensified for eliminating Neglected Tropical Diseases like Kala Azar and Lymphatic Filariasis.",""],[1,"146","2","National Tuberculosis Strategic Plan","the war against Tuberculosis has been escalated through the launch of the National Strategic Plan in 2017.",""]],"139":[[1,"145","3","Public Health Cadre and Agency Operationalization","Operationalize vital enablers - a) public health and management cadre, b) public health agency with capacitated supporting institutions (c) municipalities and panchayati raj institutions.",""],[1,"147","13","State Public Health and Management Cadre","2. Institute a public health and management cadre in states",""],[1,"147","14","Dedicated Public Health Cadre Creation Incentives","Incentivize state governments to invest in creating a dedicated cadre for public health at the state, district and block levels:",""],[1,"147","16","Public Health Officials Training Programme","Train officials in public health related disciplines including epidemiology, biostatistics, demography and social and behavioural sciences.",""],[1,"147","17","Hospital Management Training Programme","Provide training in hospital management to suitably equip personnel responsible for managing large facilities.",""],[1,"147","18","Public Health Career Pathway in State Health Departments","Create a career pathway up to the highest levels within the state health departments for those trained in public health, as well as for those with clinical specialties.",""],[1,"148","1","Public Health Cadre Career Progression Reform","healthcare to rise to higher-level positions within the cadre.",""],[1,"148","1","Inclusion of Block and District Public Health Functionaries in Cadre","Similarly, allow public health functionaries at the block and district levels to enter the cadre.",""],[1,"148","2","Leadership Qualification Requirement for Officials","Mandate a master's level qualification, in addition to specified training, for officials taking on leadership positions.",""],[1,"148","4","Model Public Health and Management Cadre Development","Develop a model public health and management cadre by drawing upon best practices and engage with states to adapt, refine and institutionalize the model.",""],[1,"148","5","Cadre Creation Guidelines for Existing Functionaries","Formulate guidelines to create the cadre, primarily by re-aligning the requisite skill sets of existing functionaries with service conditions.",""],[1,"148","8","State Public Health Agency Establishment","Create a counterpart Public Health Agency in each state, where they do not already exist.",""],[1,"148","10","Reform of the Technical Directorate and Creation of a Public Health Directorate","Redefine the role of the technical directorate (Directorate General of Health Services) and create a Directorate of Public Health.",""]],"140":[[1,"148","6","Designated Autonomous Disease Surveillance Focal Agency","Create a designated and autonomous focal agency with the required capacities and linkages to perform the functions of disease surveillance, information gathering on the health impact of",""],[1,"148","7","National Centre for Disease Control Empowerment and Capacity Building","An appropriately empowered and capacitated National Centre for Disease Control may be considered to play this role with support from relevant organizations.",""],[1,"148","9","Public Health Act","Explore the need for a Public Health Act to legislatively empower and, if necessary, institutionalise the Public Health Agency discussed above.",""]],"141":[[1,"158","9","PM-JAY Universal Health Coverage Scheme","The decision to launch PM-JAY under Ayushman Bharat is a path breaking step towards Universal Health Coverage.",""],[1,"160","3","Ayushman Bharat-National Health Agency Establishment","Establish the Ayushman Bharat-National Health Agency at the central level and counterpart institutions at the state and district levels for management of the PM-JAY.",""],[1,"160","4","Digital Health IT Platform Development","Develop a robust, modular, scalable and interoperable IT platform as per standards formulated by the National Digital Health Authority to enable paperless and cashless transactions under the scheme.",""],[1,"160","5","Fraud Prevention and Grievance Redressal Mechanisms","Put in place mechanisms for fraud prevention, detection and control as well as for grievance redressal.",""],[1,"160","6","Media and Outreach Strategy for Scheme Awareness","Design a comprehensive media and outreach strategy to increase awareness of the scheme among intended beneficiaries and other stakeholders.",""],[1,"160","7","Health Technology Assessment Institutionalization","Institutionalise health technology assessment at the central and state levels to determine the service packages to be covered under PM-JAY in the future.",""],[1,"160","8","Procedure Costing Framework Development","Develop costing frameworks for determining accurate package rates for procedures.",""],[1,"160","9","Standard Treatment Guidelines for Priority Conditions","Develop standard treatment guidelines for priority conditions.",""],[1,"160","11","Health Services Data Analytics for Strategic Purchasing","Put in place data analytics systems to guide strategic purchasing2 of health services, forecasting and generating policy inputs.",""],[1,"160","12","Independent Scheme Audit Mechanism","Institutionalize a mechanism for undertaking independent audits of the scheme.",""],[1,"160","14","Public and Private Health Facility Mobilization","Galvanize health facilities in the public sector and engage the private sector",""],[1,"160","15","Public Hospital Autonomy and Claims Fund Utilization","Provide greater autonomy to public hospitals to use claims money generated under PM-JAY to improve facilities, purchase the necessary drugs/tests and provide performance-based incentives to staff.",""],[1,"160","16","District Hospital Upgrading to Indian Public Health Standards","Strengthen district hospitals to conform to the Indian Public Health Standards.",""],[1,"160","17","District Hospital Performance Ranking System","Institutionalize ranking of district hospitals based on their performance on health indicators to foster competition and nudge them towards quality improvement.",""],[1,"160","18","Gate-Keeping Mechanisms for Health and Wellness Centre Adoption","Introduce appropriate gate-keeping mechanisms for adoption by the proposed health and wellness centres.",""],[1,"160","19","Public Sector Health Worker Compensation Reform","Reform the compensation system for professionals in public sector health facilities by shifting to a blended capitation mode of payment (part salary and part incentive based on achieving pre-agreed outcomes).",""],[1,"160","20","Incentives for Hospital Empanelment in Rural and Supply-Deficit Areas","Trigger private investments in rural/supply deficit areas by providing appropriate incentives for empanelling hospitals.",""]],"142":[[1,"159","2","Medicine Price Capping and Access Expansion","the government has taken significant steps to enhance access to medicines especially for the poor and middle classes",""],[1,"159","2","Pradhan Mantri Bhartiya Janaushadhi Pariyojana Expansion","The Pradhan Mantri Bhartiya Janaushadhi Pariyojana has been expanded from 99 functional stores in May, 2014 to 4,024 functional stores in September, 2018.",""],[1,"161","1","Affordable Drugs and Medical Devices Access Initiative","Ensure access to affordable drugs and medical devices",""],[1,"161","2","Drug Price Control Order Reform","Institute a new Drug Price Control Order (DPCO), which ensures rational drug prices by reducing trade margins.",""],[1,"161","3","Expand Drug Price Control Order Coverage to Consumables","Include consumables, in addition to drugs, in the DPCO to control undue profiteering.",""],[1,"161","6","Jan Aushadhi Store Business Model Reform and Scale-Up","Review and iron out the challenges with the business model of Jan Aushadhi stores to ensure that they can function as self-sustaining entities and scale up rapidly across the country.",""],[1,"161","7","Scale Up Bulk Drug Procurement","Find the best pathways for scaling up and adapting the process of bulk procurement of drugs adopted in states like Tamil Nadu and Rajasthan.",""]],"143":[[1,"159","9","Medical Devices Regulatory Framework","a clearly defined and comprehensive regulatory framework is required.",""],[1,"161","4","National Pharmaceutical Policy Finalization","Finalize the national pharmaceutical policy to enable access to affordable medicines, promote the use of generic drugs, clamp down on unfair marketing practices and give a boost to local manufacturing to reduce dependence on imports.",""],[1,"161","5","E-Pharmacy Policy","Formulate and implement the e-pharmacy policy to facilitate online access to quality medicines in a cost-effective and timely manner.",""],[1,"161","8","API Intermediate Cluster Development","Boost domestic production of APIs by setting up six large API intermediate clusters as per the recommendations of the Katoch Committee.",""],[1,"161","9","Single-Window Clearance Mechanism for Manufacturers","Streamline regulatory processes including providing a single window clearance mechanism to manufacturers.",""],[1,"161","10","Medical Devices Act","Introduce a separate Act for medical devices as per global best practises,",""],[1,"161","12","Medical Device Pricing Policy","Formulate an appropriate pricing policy for medical devices and re-examine it periodically to ensure access to affordable devices for the population while also ensuring a sufficient return on investment.",""]],"144":[[1,"161","13","National List of Essential Medical Devices","Develop the National List of Essential Medical Devices along the lines of the National List of Essential Medicines",""],[1,"161","14","Health Research Capacity Strengthening","4. Strengthen health research capacity",""],[1,"161","15","Research Consortia for Priority Diseases","Set up research consortia for diseases of high priority including neglected tropical diseases and emerging infections along the lines of the India TB Research and Development Corporation.",""],[1,"161","16","Regional Medical Training Hub Network","Identify at least 20 academic or research institutions at the regional level to act as hubs capable of training a minimum of 500 doctors every year.",""],[1,"161","17","Model Rural Health Research Unit Expansion","Ensure the presence of at least one model rural health research unit in every state.",""],[1,"161","18","National Viral Research and Diagnostic Laboratory Network","Cover the entire country with a network of viral research and diagnostic laboratories with a testing capacity of more than 15 lakh samples per year.",""]],"145":[[1,"161","19","Collaborative Traditional and Modern Medicine Research Initiative","Identify key research areas in traditional medicine and facilitate collaborative research with modern systems of medicine.",""]],"146":[[1,"163","14","Implementation of the National Nutrition Strategy","NITI Aayog has already detailed a possible action agenda in its National Nutrition Strategy,2 which needs to be urgently implemented.",""],[1,"164","2","POSHAN Abhiyaan State Flexibility and Innovation Support","Provide greater flexibility to states under the POSHAN Abhiyaan to adapt programmes for context-specific implementation and to experiment with innovative approaches to attain high coverage, quality, equity and better outcomes.",""],[1,"164","5","Annual Integrated Health, Nutrition and Swachh Bharat Mission District Action Plans","Develop and implement Annual Integrated Health, Nutrition and Swachh Bharat Mission (SBM) action plans for all districts under the POSHAN Abhiyaan.",""],[1,"164","7","Institutional Engagement for Action Plan Delivery","Actively engage panchayati raj institutions, the public distribution system (PDS) and public health engineering departments for delivery of the action plans.",""],[1,"164","8","Village-Level Health, Sanitation and Nutrition Service Integration","Integrate health, SBM and nutrition services at the village level through the Village Health, Sanitation and Nutrition Committees and by ensuring regular observance of Village Health Sanitation and Nutrition Days (VHSNDs).",""],[1,"164","9","Integrated Nutrition Action Implementation Guide","Develop an implementation guide for integrated action for nutrition ('a cook book') for district administrators.",""],[1,"164","10","State-Level Nutrition Convergence Mechanism","Establish a state-level convergence mechanism for nutrition under the chief secretary/ equivalent officer and corresponding structures at the district and block levels.",""],[1,"164","11","Mission Mode Malnutrition Reduction in High-Burden Districts","Implement mission mode action in districts with a high burden of malnutrition under POSHAN Abhiyaan",""],[1,"164","14","Additional Home-Based Contacts Strategy under Home-Based Young Child Care","As envisaged under the POSHAN Abhiyaan, devise a strategy for additional home-based contacts under the home-based young child care initiative with:",""],[1,"164","18","Maternal and Child Nutrition and Health Intervention Package","Replace the food-centric approach with more broad-based action that includes healthcare measures (special care of low birth weight in- fants and immunization), birth spacing, delaying age of marriage, exclusive breastfeeding for 6 months, and timely and adequate access to complementary food interventions.",""],[1,"164","19","Targeted Immunization Expansion in High-Focus Districts","Focus on immunization including Rota Virus and Pneumococcal Vaccines; target the vaccines preferentially to high focus districts.",""],[1,"165","15","POSHAN Abhiyaan Jan Andolan","Make 'POSHAN Abhiyaan' a Jan Andolan",""],[1,"165","16","POSHAN Abhiyaan Community-Led Movement","Make POSHAN Abhiyaan a community-led movement with adequate political backing.",""],[1,"165","17","Behavior Change Communication Modules for Frontline Workers","Develop behavioural change communication modules and ensure its use by all frontline workers, especially during VHSNDs; emphasise individual as well as group counselling.",""]],"147":[[1,"164","3","Independent Annual Programme Audit Mechanism","Establish an institutional mechanism, outside the government, to conduct independent annual audits of the programme to achieve implementation improvements.",""],[1,"164","6","Local Administration Accountability Measures","Ensure accountability of the local administration.",""],[1,"164","12","Multi-level Convergence and Monitoring Mechanism","Set up convergence mechanisms at the state, district and block levels; develop action plans specifying timelines; ensure sufficient budgetary allocation; strengthen monitoring systems; galvanize coordination; demonstrate change guided by annual surveys and intensively monitor implementation by NITI Aayog.",""],[1,"165","4","National Nutrition Surveillance System","Create a national nutrition surveillance system to track food quality and consumption patterns and nutritional deficiency profiles for all age groups in different regions.",""],[1,"165","5","Programme Implementation Research Studies","Conduct implementation research studies to inform improvements in the programme.",""],[1,"165","11","Nutrition MIS Scale-Up and Monitoring Strengthening","Scale-up nutrition MIS and strengthen monitoring mechanisms",""],[1,"165","12","IT-Based Real-Time Monitoring Mechanism","Establish an IT-based real time monitoring mechanism by rolling out the Common Application Software (CAS) developed by the Ministry of Women and Child Development on a countrywide basis.","Ministry of Women and Child Development"],[1,"165","13","Joint Health and Nutrition Review Mechanism","Undertake joint health and nutrition reviews in the field as a standard practice.",""],[1,"165","14","Accountability Framework with Defined Responsibilities","Establish accountability with defined responsibilities at all levels - state, district and field.",""]],"148":[[1,"165","1","Mandatory Staple Food Fortification Policy","Consider mandatory fortification of staples produced in the organized sector and provide incentives to the industry to do so.",""],[1,"165","2","Fortified Food Integration in Government Nutrition Programmes","Incorporate fortified food grains and double fortified salt within government programmes such as ICDS, mid-day meal scheme, and PDS.",""],[1,"165","3","Bio-fortification of Grains Initiative","Explore approaches to bio-fortification of grains for micronutrient deficiencies.",""],[1,"165","7","ICDS Programme Reform Review","Evaluate ICDS programme in depth and suggest reforms for greater effectiveness.",""],[1,"165","9","Adolescent Girls Nutrition Programme Redesign","Review and redesign nutrition programmes targeted at adolescent girls; link these with pre- pregnancy interventions.",""],[1,"165","10","Population-Level Obesity Prevention Pilot Approaches","Test approaches to prevent childhood and adult obesity at the population level.",""],[1,"165","18","National Anaemia Control Programme","Galvanize the National Anaemia Control Programme",""],[1,"165","19","Revised Anaemia Control Programme Strategy","Implement the revised strategy for the anaemia control programme based on evidence; incorporate home, community, school and facility level action; embed the strategy in the activities of the emerging health and wellness centres.",""],[1,"165","20","Screen-and-Treat Anaemia Control Package","Consider 'screen and treat' as a part of the anaemia control intervention package.",""]],"149":[[1,"167","9","Gender-Sensitive Legislation and Policy Mainstreaming","Ensure gender-sensitive thinking for legislation and policies keeping in view the challenges faced by women including",""],[1,"168","1","Legal Framework Reform to Eliminate Discrimination Against Women","Strengthen legal frameworks to eliminate discrimination against women and promote gender equity",""],[1,"168","2","Gender-Sensitive Labor Legislation for Women in the Unorganized Sector","Craft legislations for women engaged in the unorganized sector to ensure at least a minimum set of gender-sensitive provisions such as access to privacy, minimum wages, maternity benefits, leave and grievance redressal.",""],[1,"168","3","Implementation Mechanisms for Mandatory Labour Protection Laws","Ensure mechanisms for implementation of mandatory laws like the Maternity Benefit Act and The Sexual Harassment of Women at Work Place (Prevention, Prohibition and Redressal) Act, including for workers in the informal sector.",""],[1,"168","4","Women’s Workforce Re-entry Legal and Guideline Reform","Create liberal laws/guidelines that encourage women to re-enter the workforce after a break.",""],[1,"168","5","Equal Opportunity Policy Development and Implementation","Develop and implement Equal Opportunity Policies:",""],[1,"168","6","Workplace Gender Equality and Flexible Work Norms","Establish a set of norms (for job advertisements and selection guidelines, availability of crèche at workplace, grievance redressal, flexi hours, part-time work, maternity benefits etc.) for both the government and private sectors.",""],[1,"168","7","Voluntary Equal Opportunity Job Advertisement Initiative","Persuade the private sector, autonomous organizations and others to voluntarily inscribe a statement in job advertisements to the effect: 'We are an equal opportunity organization and are fully committed to women's inclusion in our workforce', pending a formal policy.",""],[1,"168","8","Equal Child Sex Ratio IEC Campaigns","Reward villages/districts with an equal child sex ratio through information, education, and communication (IEC) campaigns.",""],[1,"168","9","Gender-Disaggregated Data and State Ranking System","Generate gender-disaggregated data and rank states on key indicators",""],[1,"168","10","Dedicated Unit within the Ministry of Women and Child Development","Establish a dedicated unit within the Ministry of Women and Child Development.","Ministry of Women and Child Development"],[1,"168","11","Gender Target Monitoring and Budgeting Mechanism","The unit should focus on data gathering, conducting regular reviews with other ministries on explicitly defined gender targets ... ensuring optimum budgetary resources for women's welfare and evaluating the effectiveness of gender-based budgeting.",""],[1,"168","12","State-Level Gender Equality Monitoring Units","State government should establish similar units at the state level.",""],[1,"168","13","Gender-Disaggregated Data Systems Improvement","Improve data systems to generate gender- disaggregated data through the use of technology, geo locating information and generating maps in real time.",""]],"150":[[1,"168","15","Women's Participation in Industry and Enterprise Promotion","Encourage women's participation in industry and enterprise",""],[1,"168","16","Sector-Specific Women's Employment Target Development and Firm Incentives","Develop sector/industry specific targets for women's employment and incentivize their implementation by firms.",""],[1,"168","17","Women Entrepreneurs Credit Access Policy and Guidelines","Create policies and guidelines, on priority, to enhance access to credit by women entrepreneurs; provide facilitated credit access",""],[1,"169","11","Tax Incentives for Women-Employing Firms","Consider incentivizing sectors/companies that have over 30 per cent women workers by providing tax benefits.",""],[1,"169","13","Priority Land and Water Leasing Support for Women Farmers","Prioritize groups of women farmers seeking to lease land, water bodies, etc., at the village panchayat level.",""],[1,"169","14","Women’s Land Registration Incentive Campaign","Encourage joint registration with spouses/ sole registration of land in the name of the woman through registration fee and stamp duty concessions through special drives/awareness campaigns.",""],[1,"169","15","Women's Rights over Common Property Resources","Recognize and secure women's rights over common property resources like irrigation systems, fishing grounds, forests and water.",""],[1,"169","16","Enabling Conditions for Women in Agriculture","Create enabling conditions for women engaged in agriculture",""],[1,"169","17","Women Farmers Membership in Farmer Producer Organizations","Ensure 50 per cent membership of women farmers in Farmer Producer Organizations (FPOs).",""],[1,"169","18","Budget Support for Women FPO Registration Fees","Consider creating a separate budget to bear the registration/processing fee for the registration of women FPOs.",""],[1,"169","19","Women’s Skill Development for Rural Livelihood Activities","Specially focus on skill development among women, particularly for activities such as soil conservation, social forestry, dairy development, horticulture, organic farming, and livestock rearing (including animal husbandry, poultry, fisheries).",""],[1,"169","20","Inclusive Agricultural Extension Services for Women Farmers","Target agricultural extension services to women farmers as well, not just males.",""],[1,"169","24","Women’s Non-Traditional Skills Development Programme","Promote skill development among women in non-traditional work such as electronic technicians, electricians, plumbers, taxi drivers etc.",""],[1,"170","1","Women Professional Groups and Guilds Formation","Organize women into professional groups/ guilds to improve their bargaining power.",""],[1,"170","2","Digital Platform Support for Guild Apps and Market Linkages","Use platforms like Digital India (i) to create apps for the guilds (ii) for marketing and branding purposes and (iii) to establish linkages with corporates, markets and consumers.",""]],"151":[[1,"169","22","Expansion of the Post Graduate Indira Gandhi Scholarship for Single Girl Child","Consider extending the Post Graduate Indira Gandhi Scholarship for Single Girl Child scheme to families with two girl children.",""],[1,"169","23","Financial Incentives for Girls' Education","Provide relatively higher financial incentives for girls' education until Class XII to curb the higher dropout rate among girls and raise the average age at marriage by keeping girls in schools.",""],[1,"170","4","Affordable Housing and Gender-Friendly Urban Facilities","Provide affordable housing, residential hostels and gender friendly facilities in upcoming towns and big cities.",""],[1,"170","5","Rural Connectivity and Public Transport Improvement","Improve rural connectivity and public transport systems.",""]],"152":[[1,"170","6","Gender-Sensitive Time-Bound Trials for Violence Against Women Cases","Ensure gender-sensitive, rights-based and time-bound trials as well as disposal of cases pertaining to violence against women.",""],[1,"170","7","Standard Operating Protocols for Crimes Against Women","Strengthen the standard operating protocols for tackling crimes against women, including new forms of violence such as cybercrimes.",""],[1,"170","8","Training on Women-Specific Issues and Laws","Introduce training (including refresher training) on women-specific issues and laws for all ranks and categories of police personnel, health practitioners, protection officers, legal service authorities, judicial authorities as well as other stakeholders who interact with survivors of violence, especially in remote areas.",""]],"153":[[1,"171","8","Revision of the National Policy for Older Persons","Given the changing demographics and socio- economic needs, revise the National Policy for Older Persons.",""],[1,"171","9","Integrated Implementation and Monitoring Plan for Senior Citizens Schemes","An integrated implementation and monitoring plan should be developed in consultation with stakeholders",""],[1,"172","2","Amendment of the Maintenance and Welfare of Parents and Older Persons Act","Bring the necessary amendments to the Maintenance and Welfare of Parents and Older Persons Act, 2007, currently under consideration by the Ministry of Social Justice and Empowerment (MoSJE).","Ministry of Social Justice and Empowerment (MoSJE)"],[1,"172","3","District Old Age Home Establishment Initiative","Consider establishing an old age home in every district by 2020 and ensure adherence to minimum quality standards.",""],[1,"172","4","Expansion of the National Programme for Health Care of the Elderly","Expand the National Programme for Health Care of the Elderly to all districts following a comprehensive evaluation of the scheme.",""],[1,"172","5","Assistive Devices Supply for Poor Senior Citizens","Prioritize supply of aids and assistive devices for senior citizens below the poverty line.",""],[1,"172","6","Barrier-Free Public Infrastructure for the Elderly","Ensure a barrier-free environment in all public buildings, parks, etc., for the elderly.",""],[1,"172","7","Strengthening of Social Defence Training Institutions","Strengthen the National Institute of Social Defence and Regional Resource Training Centres to meet the rising demand for quality caregivers.",""]],"154":[[1,"174","7","Strengthening National Disability Institutions and Monitoring","The National Institutes (NIs), Composite Regional Centres (CRCs), District Disability Rehabilitation Centres (DDRCs) and the Rehabilitation Council of India (RCI) need special attention to ensure adequacy of resources and infrastructure as well as effective monitoring of schemes.",""],[1,"174","8","Disaggregated Data Collection for Informed Policymaking","Disaggregate data by sex, age and socio- economic status in order to identify reliable and regular trends for informed policymaking.",""],[1,"174","9","National Electronic Database for Persons with Disabilities","Feed data collected into an electronic database for PwDs at the national level and link with the Unique Disability Identity Card.",""],[1,"174","11","DEPWD Strategic Reorientation for Data and Evaluation","Reorient the DEPWD to focus on data collection, identifying gaps and evaluating the impact of various schemes, instead of focusing on the implementation of a large number of schemes with small budget allocations.",""],[1,"174","12","Mainstream Disability-Focused Programmes into Line Ministries","Bring programmes focused on improving specific issues related to PwDs under the purview of the relevant line ministries.",""],[1,"174","13","Budget Earmark for Schemes for Persons with Disabilities","Earmark at least 5 per cent of the total budget of social sector ministries for schemes for PwDs.",""],[1,"174","14","Disability Etiquette and Inclusion Curriculum Integration","Include courses in disability etiquette and success stories on PwDs in the mainstream curriculum to change attitudes towards PwDs.",""],[1,"174","15","Special Education Training in Teacher Training Courses","Provide special education training in teacher training courses.",""],[1,"174","16","Scholarships and Fellowships for Students with Disabilities","Enhance scholarships/fellowships to students with disabilities.",""],[1,"174","17","Inclusive School Access and Curriculum Reform","Make schools more inclusive by addressing the barriers related to the physical environment (e.g. accessible toilets), admission procedures as well as curriculum design.",""],[1,"174","18","Universal Design Compliance in Schools","Ensure that schools have at least one section of every class accessible under the Universal Design Guidelines.",""],[1,"174","19","Partnerships for Inclusive and Special School Synergies","Foster partnerships between the Ministry of Human Resource Development and MoSJE to promote synergies among inclusive and special schools in the government and private sectors.","Ministry of Human Resource Development | MoSJE"],[1,"174","20","School Inclusivity Rating Indicators","Develop indicators for rating schools on inclusivity.",""],[1,"175","1","Disabled-Friendly School and College Programmes","Include disabled friendly sports, cultural and technical programmes in schools and colleges.",""],[1,"175","3","Cochlear Implant and Corrective Surgery Programme for Children","Conduct cochlear implant and corrective surgeries for 5000 children annually.",""],[1,"175","4","State Spinal Injury Centres Establishment","Establish 20 state spinal injury centres.",""],[1,"175","5","District Early Diagnostic and Intervention Centres","Set up early diagnostic and intervention centres at the district level to screen children and identify special needs or requirements for assistive devices at an early age.",""],[1,"175","6","Integrated Skill Development for Intellectually Disabled Persons","Integrate the skill development scheme with schemes of the National Trust (e.g., Disha), to address the needs of the intellectually disabled.",""],[1,"175","7","Dedicated Training Centres for Persons with Disabilities","Establish dedicated training centres for PwDs to meet the requirements of the private sector.",""],[1,"175","8","Integrated Skill Training, Soft Loan, and Entrepreneurship Support for Persons with Disabilities","Integrate initiatives of various ministries to provide skill training, soft loans and entrepreneurship opportunities to PwDs.",""],[1,"175","10","Upgrade National Institutes into Centres of Excellence","Upgrade NIs into centres of excellence.",""],[1,"175","11","Establishment of Child Resource Centres","Establish 50 CRCs in states having a population of more than 6 crore.",""],[1,"175","12","Comprehensive Rehabilitation Services for Persons with Disabilities","Provide comprehensive rehabilitation services to 50 lakh PwDs through the NIs and CRCs.",""],[1,"175","13","Rehabilitation Personnel Long-Term Training Programme","Enrol 17,000 rehabilitation personnel in various long-term courses offered by NIs and CRCs every year.",""],[1,"175","15","Accessible India Campaign Mass Mobilization","Make the Accessible India Campaign a mass movement with the involvement of citizens and civil society.",""],[1,"175","16","Disability Awareness Programmes","Conduct awareness programmes in collab- orations with DDRCs, CRCs and Vocational Rehabilitation Centres (VRCs).",""],[1,"175","17","Universal Design and Accessibility Standards Integration in Higher Education Curricula","Incorporate universal design and accessibility standards in engineering, architecture and computer science studies.",""],[1,"175","18","Accessibility Certificate Requirement for Commercial Enterprises","Introduce the requirement of an accessibility certificate for all future commercial enterprises above a specified size in order to be awarded a completion certificate.",""],[1,"175","19","Expansion of DDRC Schemes to All Districts","Extend the DDRC schemes to all districts.",""],[1,"175","20","Residential Homes for Disabled Adults","Construct residential homes for disabled adults whose parents are no longer alive.",""],[1,"175","21","Community-Based Rehabilitation Mission Mode Programme","Adopt a life-cycle approach for community- based rehabilitation in mission mode.",""]],"155":[[1,"176","4","Transgender Housing and Community Services Provision","Mandate the provision of housing and community services to accommodate at least 50 per cent of transgender persons.",""],[1,"176","6","District Residential Schools Scheme","Formulate and implement a scheme for establishing residential schools in all districts",""],[1,"176","7","Transgender Identification in Official Records","Provide for identification of transgender persons in all government and non-government records by introducing a separate column to include the",""],[1,"176","8","Transgender Skills and Employability Training Scheme","Design a scheme for providing skill and employability training to transgender persons to integrate them with mainstream society.",""],[1,"176","9","Centrally Sponsored Scheme for New India","Launch a centrally sponsored scheme to provide",""],[1,"176","13","Aadhaar and Direct Benefit Transfer Implementation and Monitoring for Social Security Programmes","Ensure Aadhaar and Direct Benefit Transfer based implementation and monitoring of social security programmes.",""],[1,"176","14","Transgender Participation Forum in Governance","Create a forum for the active participation of transgender persons at all levels of governance.",""],[1,"176","15","Institutional Mechanisms for Transgender Programmes","Put in place institutional mechanisms to effectively implement programmes for transgender persons.",""],[1,"176","16","National Fund for State Social Inclusion Support","Consider creating a fund at the national level for supporting states that have mapped out the needs of and designed the necessary policy interventions for various vulnerable sections of society including persons with disabilities, senior citizens and transgender persons in line with the relevant legislations.",""]],"156":[[1,"177","2","Focused Affirmative Action for Socially Excluded Groups","To accelerate the socio-economic development of SCs, STs, OBCs, safai karamcharis as well as DNTs, NTs and SNTs through focused affirmative action so as to bring them on par with the rest of the population as far as key human development indicators are concerned.",""],[1,"178","7","Baseline Survey for Remote and Tribal Habitations","Undertake a baseline survey and target remote and tribal habitations for implementation of various development programmes.",""],[1,"178","8","Tailored Community-Specific Schemes","Design schemes that are tailored to and narrowly focus on the challenges and needs of specific communities.",""],[1,"178","10","National Institute for Tribal Research","Establish the National Institute for Tribal Research.",""],[1,"178","11","Earmarked Funding for DNTs, SNTs, and NTs","Earmark funds under all developmental programmes for DNTs, SNTs and NTs.",""],[1,"178","12","Legislation Implementation Monitoring Mechanism","Put in place mechanisms to regularly monitor the implementation of legislations like the Panchayat (Extension to Scheduled Areas) Act and Forest Rights Act (FRA), 2006.",""],[1,"178","13","Permanent Commission for NTs, DNTs and SNTs","Set up a permanent commission for NTs, DNTs and SNTs along the lines of the National Commission for SCs and STs.",""],[1,"178","14","Residential Schools with Vocational Training","Establish residential schools in uncovered blocks/districts with facilities for vocational training.",""],[1,"178","15","Residential School Quality Standards","Define and ensure adherence to quality parameters for existing and new residential schools.",""],[1,"178","16","Scholarship Expansion for Pre-Matric and Post-Matric Students","Increase the number of scholarships provided under the pre-matric, post-matric,",""],[1,"179","1","National Fellowship and National Overseas Scholarship Schemes for SCs, STs and OBCs","National Fellowship and National Overseas Scholarship schemes for SCs, STs and OBCs.",""],[1,"179","2","Stand-Up India Scheme Expansion","Expand the Stand-Up India scheme to include uncovered social groups like OBCs, DNTs, NTs and SNTs.",""],[1,"179","3","Venture Capital and Credit Guarantee Support for Marginalized Groups","Extend venture capital funds and credit guarantee schemes for covering STs, OBCs, DNTs, NTs and SNTs.",""],[1,"179","5","Concessional Loans for OBC Entrepreneurship","Provide concessional loans for promoting entrepreneurship among OBCs by doubling the number of beneficiaries covered under the National Backward Classes Finance & Development Corporation by 2022-23.",""],[1,"179","6","Promotion of Indigenous Tribal Medicine","Encourage indigenous tribal medicine alongside other systems to create additional livelihood opportunities.",""],[1,"179","7","Youth Employer Linkage and Pre-Job Training","Establish contact points with potential employers along with pre-job training sessions for youth.",""],[1,"179","8","Universal Coverage for DNT, SNT and NT Identity and Poverty Cards","Ensure universal coverage of DNT, SNT and NT populations for BPL and Aadhaar cards.",""],[1,"179","9","Vulnerability Index and Vulnerability Intervention Index for PVTGs","Prepare a Vulnerability Index and Vulnerability Intervention Index for PVTGs based on the methodology suggested by the National Institute of Rural Development and Panchayati Raj, Hyderabad.",""],[1,"179","10","Extension of Habitat Rights to PVTGs","Extend habitat rights to PVTGs within the FRA framework, as has been done for the Baiga Tribe of Dindori District, Madhya Pradesh.",""],[1,"179","11","Project-Based Funding under Special Central Assistance","Provide project-based funding under special central assistance (SCA) to SCSP and to TSP, especially in gram panchayats/blocks where the population of SCs/STs is more than 25 per cent.",""],[1,"179","12","Targeted Nutrition Support for Vulnerable Tribal Children","Prioritize vulnerable groups like tribal children under the National Nutrition Mission through tag-tracking and additional home visits for underweight children conducted by frontline workers.",""],[1,"179","13","Community-Owned Radio Station Promotion","Empower marginalized communities by promoting community-owned radio stations.",""],[1,"179","14","Inclusive Mixed-Community Habitation Promotion","Promote habitations along the lines of Samasthapuram in Tamil Nadu where people belonging to all communities live together.",""],[1,"179","15","Affirmative Action for Minority Inclusion","To bridge the gap between minority communities and the rest of the population with respect to various socio-economic and human development indicators through affirmative action.",""]],"157":[[1,"182","2","MoMA Data Collection, Monitoring, and Scheme Outreach Enhancement","Increase the emphasis of the MoMA on data collection and analysis, identifying gap areas, online monitoring of the PM's 15-Point Programme, evaluating the impact of various schemes and popularizing schemes in local languages using social media.","MoMA"],[1,"182","3","Scholarship Expansion for Minority and Merit-Based Students","Enhance pre-matric scholarships, post-matric scholarships, merit-cum-means scholarships, Maulana Azad National Fellowships and National Overseas Scholarships with a 15 per cent increase annually from 2019-20.",""],[1,"182","4","Scholarship Expansion for Girls from Minority Communities","Increase the number of scholarships for girls from minority communities by 10 per cent every year.",""],[1,"182","5","Post-Class 8 Education Continuation Support for KGBV Girls","Ensure that girls who pass out from Kasturba Gandhi Balika Vidyalayas can continue their education after completing Class 8.",""],[1,"182","6","Girls' Transport Access Support","Provide access to public transport in the form of buses and cycles or vouchers for meeting private transport costs to raise enrolment rates among girls from vulnerable communities.",""],[1,"182","7","Nai Roshni Minority Women Training Scheme","Train at least 100,000 minority women under the Nai Roshni scheme every year.",""],[1,"182","8","Targeted Identification of Poor Minority Households","Identify the poorest among the minority communities through the Socio-Economic Caste Census data for proper targeting of various schemes.",""],[1,"182","9","Nai Manzil Integrated Education and Livelihood Programme","By 2022-23, provide integrated education and livelihood programmes to 100,000 beneficiaries under the Nai Manzil programme.",""],[1,"182","10","Seekho Aur Kamao Beneficiary Training Programme","Train at least 350,000 beneficiaries during the 5-year period under Seekho Aur Kamao.",""],[1,"182","11","Expanded Lending to Vulnerable Sections through Alternative Channels","Achieve a 15 per cent increase per annum in loans to vulnerable sections through the use of alternative channels like regional rural banks.",""],[1,"182","12","Localized Job Advertisement Dissemination","Put out job advertisements in Urdu and local language newspapers as well as through other locally appropriate channels.",""]],"158":[[1,"185","1","Balanced District Development Programme","Achieve balanced development in India by uplifting 115 districts, currently below the national average in the areas of health and nutrition, education, agriculture and water resources, financial inclusion and skill development, and basic infrastructure.",""],[1,"186","7","District Vision and Planning Framework","The ADP aims to address governance issues by using a combination of approaches: lifting levels of aspirations through a vision and district plan, adequate institutional arrangements, convergence in all stakeholders' efforts and above all, ranking- based public competition among the districts by setting up a real-time monitoring mechanism.",""],[1,"186","7","Stakeholder Convergence and Institutional Arrangements","The ADP aims to address governance issues by using a combination of approaches: lifting levels of aspirations through a vision and district plan, adequate institutional arrangements, convergence in all stakeholders' efforts and above all, ranking- based public competition among the districts by setting up a real-time monitoring mechanism.",""],[1,"186","7","Real-Time District Monitoring and Competition Mechanism","The ADP aims to address governance issues by using a combination of approaches: lifting levels of aspirations through a vision and district plan, adequate institutional arrangements, convergence in all stakeholders' efforts and above all, ranking- based public competition among the districts by setting up a real-time monitoring mechanism.",""],[1,"186","10","District Vision and Action Plan Preparation","district officials will draw up a vision and action plan for their districts spanning the period 2018-19 to 2022-23.",""],[1,"186","11","Aspirational Districts Mass Movement Initiative","The scheme's design encourages states and district administrations to give a lead role to such champions of change to turn this initiative into a mass movement.",""],[1,"187","4","District Performance Rankings and Open Data Publication","Making these rankings and the underlying data available in the public domain will help boost competition between districts.",""],[1,"187","5","Government Scheme Convergence Initiative","The ADP aims to ensure convergence between different government schemes while also",""],[1,"187","6","District Action Plans for Aspirational Districts","the action plan prepared by the district collectors of aspirational districts will identify the thrust activity, map existing schemes and their respective implementation agencies and set targets for rapid improvement.",""],[1,"188","1","ADP Coordination of Stunting Prevention Schemes","The ADP will bring together these efforts.",""],[1,"188","2","Federalism and Intergovernmental Coordination Mechanisms","Promote federalism and put in place institutional mechanisms to ensure teamwork between the central, state and district administration",""],[1,"188","3","District Team Formation and Guardian Officer Coordination Mechanism","a major innovation here is the emphasis on team formation.",""],[1,"188","4","Empowered Committees of Secretaries for Social Sector Scheme Oversight","Set up Empowered Committees of Secretaries of Government of India to supervise and troubleshoot.",""],[1,"188","5","Public-Private Partnership Technical Expertise Mobilization for ADP","another core component is bringing in technical expertise through public private partnerships.",""]],"159":[[1,"194","2","Modernisation of Police Forces Scheme","The recently announced umbrella scheme on \"Modernisation of Police Forces\" to strengthen law and order and modernize the police is a welcome stimulus.",""],[1,"195","16","Advanced Technology for Anti-Corruption Enforcement","Use of advanced technology is an essential pre-requisite to check these violations of the law; person-to-person direct interface should be minimized to eliminate corruption.",""],[1,"197","10","Model Police Act Legislative Reform","The Model Police Act of 2015 can serve as the basis for legislative reform as it modernizes the mandate of the police, puts in place a governance mechanism that insulates the police from political interference and provides for the measurement and tracking of police performance.",""],[1,"197","11","Task Force for Outsourcing Non-Core Functions","A task force may be created under the Ministry of Home Affairs (MHA) to skill personnel and identify non-core functions that can be outsourced to save on staff.","Ministry of Home Affairs (MHA)"],[1,"197","12","Women’s Recruitment Policy for the Police Force","The MHA should come up with a policy to encourage greater participation of women to achieve a target share of 30 per cent women among new recruits.","MHA"],[1,"197","13","Nationwide Emergency Contact Number","Launch a common nation-wide emergency contact number to attend to emergency security needs of citizens.",""],[1,"197","14","Integration of Anti-Corruption Laws into Police Reforms","Integrate the Lokpal and Prevention of Corruption Acts into police reforms to enhance accountability.",""],[1,"197","15","Transparent Police Transfers and Postings Reform","Transfers/postings of police personnel should be made more transparent",""],[1,"197","15","Review of Police Role in Prosecution","the involvement of police in prosecution needs to be looked at more closely",""],[1,"197","16","Police Training Modernization and Certification System","It is important to consider introduction of remodelled training modules, refresher courses and continuing education for police personnel including live-streaming of training modules on e-platforms.",""],[1,"197","16","Security Personnel Certification and Career Linkage Scheme","A concept of certification of security personnel with identified skill sets may be considered with linkage to promotion and deployment.",""],[1,"197","17","First Information Report Lodging Reform","Introduce reform of the First Information Report (FIR) lodging mechanism, including introducing filing e-FIRs for minor offences.",""],[1,"198","1","Police Station Online Records Portal","challans, investigation reports, etc., should be made available through the online portal of each police station.",""],[1,"198","3","Expert Panel on Psychology, Negotiation, Language Proficiency and Training","A panel of experts in psychology, negotiation, language proficiency and training may be put together.",""],[1,"198","4","Police Technology Benchmarking Centre","A technology centre may be considered for benchmarking and identifying suitable technologies for the police under BPR&D",""]],"160":[[1,"198","2","Cyber Crime Cadre Development","A separate cadre for exclusively looking into cyber-crimes, cyber threats and fraud needs to be developed.",""],[1,"198","5","National Cyber Security Division","A separate National Cyber Security Division may be considered to support and coordinate initiatives of state governments in handling cyber-crimes.",""],[1,"198","5","Citizen Cybercrime Reporting and Redressal Dashboard","A separate dashboard for interface with citizens for reporting and redressal of cyber crimes may be considered.",""],[1,"198","5","Crime and Criminal Tracking Network and Systems Project Phase 2","The Crime and Criminal Tracking Network and Systems project may be completed along with the launch of Phase 2 for linking of crime, prosecution, court and prison databases.",""]],"161":[[1,"207","5","Forest Land Management Efficiency Improvement","Increase efficiency in the management of forest land.",""],[1,"208","1","Forest Community Rights Strengthening","Strengthen property rights, especially community rights over forest land.",""],[1,"209","5","Forest Land Management Efficiency Improvement","2. Increase efficiency around the management of forest land",""],[1,"209","6","Forest Rights Act Implementation","Implement effectively the Forest Rights Act (FRA) in all states to strengthen the property rights of forest dwellers, tribal populations and local communities.",""],[1,"209","7","Priority Land Zoning for Forest and Revenue Demarcation","Zone land on a priority basis to clearly demarcate forest and revenue lands.",""],[1,"210","6","Recognition of Customary Land Tenure in Tribal Areas","Recognize the customary land tenure system including community ownership in tribal areas.",""],[1,"210","9","Revenue and Forest Land Demarcation","Define and demarcate revenue and forestland, including land used for shifting cultivation.",""]],"162":[[1,"209","8","Agroforestry Expansion on Wasteland and Fallow Land","Bring more area under agro forestry using wasteland, non-cultivable fallow lands, etc.",""],[1,"209","9","Tree-Felling Policy Review and Farm Tree Promotion","Revisit the policy on tree-felling.",""],[1,"209","10","Relaxation of Restrictions on Tree Species and Wood Movement","easing restriction on certain species of trees.",""],[1,"210","10","Urban Master Planning and Vertical Growth Strategy","Plan urbanization as per master plans with greater emphasis on vertical growth.",""],[1,"210","11","Land Degradation and Soil Erosion Prevention Policy","Prevent land degradation and soil erosion through policies that promote fertilization and organic farming.",""]]}});